=E2=80=9D</a></u>  An =E2=80=9Cunknown known=E2=80=9D is a criterion so obv=
ious to you that you would never think to write it down, though you would r=
ecognize it when you saw it. An =E2=80=9Cunknown unknown=E2=80=9D is a ques=
tion you have not considered at all=E2=80=94which the model may encounter i=
n the course of its work without a map to guide it.</p>
<p>Every=E2=80=99s experience with Fable illustrates both kinds. Head of te=
ch consulting <strong><u><a href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fev=
ery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebe=
fcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiVXNlIEZhYmxlIEJlZm9yZSBZb3UgS25vdyBXaGF0I=
