ARTICULATE YOUR BETS

Your strategy is already making bets about these axes. The question is =
whether you=E2=80=99ve written them down and made them explicit.

Having explicit bets creates internal alignment. Your team knows what =
you=E2=80=99re building toward and what would cause a pivot. They can make =
local decisions that stay consistent with the overall direction because =
they understand the assumptions underneath. When the plan changes, they =
still know where it=E2=80=99s headed.

Explicit bets enable faster =
adaptation. When signals shift, you recognize it sooner because you know =
what you were watching for. You=E2=80=99ve already thought through the =
implications. You=E2=80=99re not starting from scratch.

So, take an hour. Write down your implicit bet on each axis and what it =
means for your business. Then write down the signals that would tell you =
you=E2=80=99re wrong.

This is harder than it sounds. Most teams discover =
their bets aren=E2=80=99t as crisp as they thought, or that they=E2=80=99ve=
 been making incompatible ones in parallel. If you can=E2=80=99t articulate=
 them, your strategy is less coherent than you think. Start there.



