  <div class=3D"post-body">
    <p><em>Forget vague heuristics such as =E2=80=9CAI wrappers.=E2=80=9D <=
/em><strong><em>Dan Pupius</em></strong><em>, chief technology officer at T=
he General Partnership, argues that founders need a more robust framework t=
o understand the risks and opportunities of building with AI. He encourages=
 founders to look holistically at the implicit assumptions underneath their=
 AI strategy, from the cost of intelligence, model self-sufficiency, platfo=
rm lock-in, and the regulatory environment. I worked with Dan more than a d=
ecade ago at Medium, and the same quiet, thoughtful brilliance I knew him f=
or then shines in his nuanced analysis.=E2=80=94<u><a href=3D"https://icu.e=
very.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e6=
54f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiWW91ciBBSSBTdHJ=
hdGVneSBJcyBNYWtpbmcgQmV0cy4gRG8gWW91IEtub3cgV2hpY2ggT25lcz8gIiwicG9zdF9pZC=
I6NDMyNCwicG9zdF90eXBlIjoicG9zdCIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vZXZlcnkudG8vQGthdGVfM=
Tc2NyIsInBvc2l0aW9uIjo1fQ=3D=3D/1/0100019f197f77fc-7e38ae12-3145-4476-aa59-=
878b0c685637-000000/TAZRyVUE5mNaq7DsnhuF2nXBbNSm3fsPbgLdjEHnSzc=3D452" rel=
=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">Kate Lee</a></u></em></p>
<p></p>
<hr class=3D"quill-line">
<p></p>
<p>I=E2=80=99ve built products on ideas that people thought were wrong=E2=
=80=94and watched those same ideas become inevitable.</p>
<p>When I helped to rebuild Gmail at Google in 2005, we were betting that c=
ommunication was becoming faster, more conversational, and increasingly bro=
wser-native. So we built GChat, which put real-time chat inside your browse=
r for the first time, right next to your email. When I was running engineer=
ing at Medium, the bet was that social feeds were not enough for deeper thi=
nking and publishing, so even while signups to Twitter,  Snapchat, and Vine=
 were exploding, we championed long-form writing. </p>
<p>In each case, we started with an insight about where behavior, technolog=
y, and markets were moving=E2=80=94and built our bets on top of it. But now=
, the rapid pace of change in AI means that the assumptions and insights un=
derlying a strategy can shift mid-execution, causing those bets to crumble.=
</p>
<p>Founders need a more flexible way of thinking about which bets to take. =
Instead of asking =E2=80=9CWhat do we think will happen?=E2=80=9D, ask your=
self two fundamental questions. First: What assumptions are irreversible? I=
f you build deeply on top of one provider, such as one model provider, you =
need to rewire the product to move away from that provider. Second: What as=
sumptions can we still revise? Assuming tokens will stay expensive is a bet=
 you can hold loosely=E2=80=94if costs fall, you can change your approach w=
ithout rebuilding anything. </p>
<p>At The General Partnership, where I am the chief technology officer, we =
developed a framework to help founders understand which bets they=E2=80=99r=
e making, and which ones they can reverse when building with AI.  The four-=
axis framework moves the conversation away from broad labels like <a href=
=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95=
455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0Ij=
oiWW91ciBBSSBTdHJhdGVneSBJcyBNYWtpbmcgQmV0cy4gRG8gWW91IEtub3cgV2hpY2ggT25lc=
z8gIiwicG9zdF9pZCI6NDMyNCwicG9zdF90eXBlIjoicG9zdCIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vZXZl=
cnkudG8vcG9kY2FzdC9oZS1idWlsdC1hLWdwdC13cmFwcGVyLXRoYXQtaGFzLWhhbGYtYS1taWx=
saW9uLXVzZXJzLWFuZC1rZWVwcy1ncm93aW5nIiwicG9zaXRpb24iOjZ9/1/0100019f197f77f=
c-7e38ae12-3145-4476-aa59-878b0c685637-000000/z_2RJD-EKlk5wE9MRSUdH15gcQGvF=
tDuMr4xbPS2upA=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">=E2=80=
=9C</a><u><a href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails=
%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242=
