Here are the highlights:

 * The =E2=80=9CSaaSpocalypse=E2=80=9D narrative =
has it backwards. AI agents turn anyone into a vibe coder, kicking off =
investor panic that traditional software-as-a-service (SaaS) companies like=
 Figma would cease to justify their cost. Colyer isn=E2=80=99t worried: AI =
has exponentially expanded the developer base, while underscoring how =
difficult it is to create a vibe coded version of Figma that works as well =
or as reliably as the real thing. He=E2=80=99s vibe coded multiple agents =
to do stuff like handle his emails, but the maintenance costs piled up =
quickly and never seemed worth it. =E2=80=9CI=E2=80=99m buying more =
software these days than I ever did before,=E2=80=99=E2=80=9D he says. =
=E2=80=9C=E2=80=98I=E2=80=99m just going to pay somebody else to run my =
agent for me.=E2=80=99=E2=80=9D
 * Figma is embracing agents. The company =
has launched an MCP server=E2=80=94a standardized interface any AI tool can=
 plug into=E2=80=94that allows you to approach design work from two =
directions. =E2=80=9CCode to design=E2=80=9D takes a live web page and =
reconstructs it on the Figma canvas, so you can manipulate the elements =
directly; meanwhile, =E2=80=9Cdesign to code=E2=80=9D flips the process by =
packaging a Figma design and giving it to an agent, which makes changes for=
 you via pull request.
 * There=E2=80=99s a ceiling to chat-based =
generative design. Great design hinges on a diamond-shaped process: First =
you diverge, or generate lots of ideas, and only then do you converge =
around the most promising options. Text-based chats are inherently linear =
and therefore bad at divergence; the setup forces you to select an option =
https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce=
5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiT3B1cyA0LjggSXMgU21hcnQgRW5vdWdoIHRvIEd=
ldCBpbiBZb3VyIFdheSIsInBvc3RfaWQiOjQyODUsInBvc3RfdHlwZSI6InBvc3QiLCJ1cmwiOi=
JodHRwczovL2V2ZXJ5LnRvL2NvbnRleHQtd2luZG93L21pbmktdmliZS1jaGVjay1jbGF1ZGUtZ=
GVzaWduIiwicG9zaXRpb24iOjE1fQ=3D=3D and iterate on it. Agents are already =
good at the task-completion workflows Figma supports today, but the =
divergent, exploratory part of design remains unsolved across the industry.=
 Colyer is interested in dividing the process so specialized agents handle =
the divergence by pushing you to expand your thinking, while another set =
filters through the options to identify a single path forward. =
=E2=80=9CEven the best agents, the command-line agents, don=E2=80=99t have =
the ability to do those workflows,=E2=80=9D he says. =
=E2=80=9CThat=E2=80=99s where I see the future of design and product =
thinking.=E2=80=9D
 * Agents can produce so much so quickly. =
They=E2=80=99re less good at determining whether any of it meets a =
company=E2=80=99s values or design standards. Colyer isn=E2=80=99t sure the=
 best way to close this gap=E2=80=94maybe it=E2=80=99s a video walkthrough,=
 a screenshot, or a trusted review agent=E2=80=94but for good design to =
scale, AI needs to play a larger role in evaluations.

