<h4 id=3D"prds-dont-work-in-the-ai-era"><strong>PRDs don=E2=80=99t work in =
the AI era</strong></h4>
<p>You=E2=80=99re probably used to old product specs. You write acceptance =
criteria, engineers build according to it, and QA verifies that it shipped =
correctly. But AI doesn=E2=80=99t do that=E2=80=94it gives different result=
s every time. Braintrust just published =E2=80=9CEvals Are the New PRD=E2=
=80=9D=E2=80=94the argument is that, for AI products, evals replace the spe=
c, the acceptance criteria, and the roadmap all at once. While a PRD gather=
s dust in a Google Doc, an eval suite runs on every commit. The piece walks=
 through a four-stage flywheel: Observe, analyze, evaluate, improve. It=E2=
=80=99s based on how teams at Stripe, Zapier, and Vercel actually ship qual=
ity AI. Read it now.</p>
