jZ9/1/0100019ebd137585-f144a482-d4c6-4dd3-8e4a-97c6c3c1c921-000000/uagyGJIc=
XB0pokBt43CAZ-nAM5VN2BPr7z5mXYnHpso=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" targ=
et=3D"_blank">the best coding model in the world</a></u>?</p>
<p>For engineers, the case is easy to make. For many knowledge workers, tho=
ugh, Fable might feel incremental. You may have one-shotted an impressive d=
emo or two, but you=E2=80=99re probably not using it for your day-to-day wo=
rk. Why would you? It costs twice as much and the results aren=E2=80=99t th=
at much better.</p>
<p>But there is a certain class of developers who are feeling Fable=E2=80=
=99s full force. These are people like <strong><u><a href=3D"https://icu.ev=
ery.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e65=
4f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiVGhlIE1vcmFsIG9m=
IEZhYmxlIiwicG9zdF9pZCI6NDMwMCwicG9zdF90eXBlIjoicG9zdCIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8=
vY29yYS5jb21wdXRlciIsInBvc2l0aW9uIjo3fQ=3D=3D/1/0100019ebd137585-f144a482-d=
4c6-4dd3-8e4a-97c6c3c1c921-000000/9LYFDsJY_HUF9c-NmKBJ38KLC2cqvUYGBsxjeF1Vj=
pU=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">Cora</a></u></stron=
g> general manager <strong><u><a href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F=
%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adc=
e5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiVGhlIE1vcmFsIG9mIEZhYmxlIiwicG9zdF9p=
ZCI6NDMwMCwicG9zdF90eXBlIjoicG9zdCIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vZXZlcnkudG8vQGtpZXJ=
hbl8xMzU1IiwicG9zaXRpb24iOjh9/1/0100019ebd137585-f144a482-d4c6-4dd3-8e4a-97=
c6c3c1c921-000000/0mi29WHztlNf9RQ2Ils2ZRyYF109_FrIB-CXNvlHsEM=3D452" rel=3D=
"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">Kieran Klaassen</a></u></strong>, w=
ho are suddenly churning through his backlog of bug fixes and feature reque=
sts in hours instead of days. =E2=80=9CThis is my favorite model ever,=E2=
=80=9D he told me.</p>
<p>What=E2=80=99s the difference between Kieran and everyone else? The diff=
erence between Kieran and most people using Fable isn=E2=80=99t simply that=
 he=E2=80=99s a developer but that he=E2=80=99s at Level 7 or 8 on <u><a hr=
ef=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f=
95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0=
IjoiVGhlIE1vcmFsIG9mIEZhYmxlIiwicG9zdF9pZCI6NDMwMCwicG9zdF90eXBlIjoicG9zdCI=
sInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vZXZlcnkudG8vZ3VpZGVzL3RoZS1laWdodC1sZXZlbHMtb2YtYWktYW=
RvcHRpb24iLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6OX0=3D/1/0100019ebd137585-f144a482-d4c6-4dd3-8e4a=
-97c6c3c1c921-000000/EXC14l55xGNkVCPm1PP5zl1bz1A-dPQ8dh8b5zXvESo=3D452" rel=
=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">our scale of AI use</a></u>: He =
delegates whole projects, lets agents work asynchronously, reviews the resu=
lts, and feeds what he learns into the next run. In other words he writes=
=E2=80=94dare I say it, <u><a href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2F=
every.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5e=
befcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiVGhlIE1vcmFsIG9mIEZhYmxlIiwicG9zdF9pZCI=
6NDMwMCwicG9zdF90eXBlIjoicG9zdCIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8veC5jb20vc3RlaXBldGUvc3=
RhdHVzLzIwNjM2OTcxNjI3NDgyNjA2MjciLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6MTB9/1/0100019ebd137585-f=
144a482-d4c6-4dd3-8e4a-97c6c3c1c921-000000/p5_RwHZfMqCr3lgF7hIgGnlphq_CUf-o=
bITuO28F9b8=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">loops</a><=
/u>=E2=80=94not prompts.</p>
<p>For now, this might make Fable seem like a tool for developers. But in A=
I, developer workflows <u><a href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fe=
very.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5eb=
