<hr class=3D"quill-line">
<p></p>
<p>Claude Opus 5 had a strange first week at Every. It argued with instruct=
ions, stopped before the work was done, and fought the systems we=E2=80=99d=
 built for earlier Claude models.</p>
<p>Then we deleted them.</p>
<p>With less process, Opus 5 sometimes got dramatically better. It built st=
rong software, worked through bugs for hours, and produced more rigorous kn=
owledge work. The less we told it how to work, the more capable it looked.<=
/p>
<p>Our <a href=3D"https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f4=
54c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiVmliZSBDaGVjazogQ2xhd=
