<p></p>
<p>Claude Opus 5 is a hard model to love. In its first week at Every, it ar=
gued with instructions, stopped before the work was finished, and fought th=
e skills and plugins we built for earlier Claude models.</p>
<p>Then we deleted those instructions.</p>
<p>With less process, Opus 5 sometimes got dramatically better. It built st=
rong software, worked through bugs for hours, and produced rigorous writing=
 and knowledge work. Low and medium thinking effort also brought out more o=
f its strengths in coding while reducing some of its annoying quirks.</p>
<p>The reversal left us with a harder question than whether Opus 5 is good:=
 Is the model disappointing, or are we judging it with systems built for it=
s predecessors? We get into:</p>


