ALIGNMENT

Old scars. Silicon Valley has traditionally placed a premium on the =
outsider because those with fresh eyes see the absurdities that industry =
veterans have begrudgingly accepted. Occasionally, that naivety is worth =
billions to venture capitalists who have spent years scouting for the next =
Patrick and John Collisons=E2=80=94both programmers, not payments =
executives, when they started Stripe.

But AI is changing what investors =
need from founders. In its H1 2026 funding report https://every.=
to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e1896=
6e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiWW91ciBBSSBJcyBhIFRlYW0gb2YgU3BlY2lhbGlzdHMiLCJwb3N0X=
2lkIjo0Mzk2LCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly9yb2NraGVhbHRoLmNv=
bS9pbnNpZ2h0cy9oMS0yMDI2LWZ1bmRpbmctYW5kLW1hcmtldC1vdmVydmlldy1kdXJhYmxlLXJ=
vb3RzLXNoaWZ0aW5nLXJvdXRlcy8iLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6NTV9, digital-health venture =
fund Rock Health says it has stopped describing startups as =
=E2=80=9CAI-enabled=E2=80=9D because the technology is too ubiquitous to =
distinguish one company from another. Investors and buyers have moved on to=
 asking: =E2=80=9CWho has something AI alone can=E2=80=99t provide?=
=E2=80=9D

One answer is deep domain expertise. Rock Health found that =
founders who have worked inside the healthcare organizations they sell to =
are better able to identify solvable problems and =E2=80=9Csee through the =
buyer=E2=80=99s eyes.=E2=80=9D This is hardly rocket science: A clinician =
or administrator knows which apparently ridiculous constraint cannot simply=
 be designed away. More importantly, they know which questions are worth =
asking and which problems are worth spending years trying to solve.

Healthcare is making the value of expertise more visible, but I doubt that =
value will remain confined to this domain. Law, finance, manufacturing, and=
 education all run on tacit knowledge that never appears in a =
model=E2=80=99s training data=E2=80=94and selling into them takes people =
who understand the unofficial workflows and the competing incentives.

While we still need people with fresh eyes, I believe the best founders =
will need old scars.=E2=80=94Ashwin Sharma https://every.=
