<h2 id=3D"alignment">Alignment</h2>
<p><strong>Old scars.</strong> Silicon Valley has traditionally placed a pr=
emium on the outsider because those with fresh eyes see the absurdities tha=
t industry veterans have begrudgingly accepted. Occasionally, that naivety =
is worth billions to venture capitalists who have spent years scouting for =
the next <strong>Patrick</strong> and <strong>John Collison</strong>s<stron=
g>=E2=80=94</strong>both programmers, not payments executives, when they st=
arted Stripe. </p>
<p>But AI is changing what investors need from founders. In its <u><a href=
=3D"https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687=
adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiWW91ciBBSSBJcyBhIFRlYW0gb2YgU3BlY2l=
hbGlzdHMiLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0Mzk2LCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly=
9yb2NraGVhbHRoLmNvbS9pbnNpZ2h0cy9oMS0yMDI2LWZ1bmRpbmctYW5kLW1hcmtldC1vdmVyd=
mlldy1kdXJhYmxlLXJvb3RzLXNoaWZ0aW5nLXJvdXRlcy8iLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6NTV9" rel=3D=
"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">H1 2026 funding report</a></u>, dig=
ital-health venture fund Rock Health says it has stopped describing startup=
s as =E2=80=9CAI-enabled=E2=80=9D because the technology is too ubiquitous =
to distinguish one company from another. Investors and buyers have moved on=
 to asking: =E2=80=9CWho has something AI alone can=E2=80=99t provide?=E2=
=80=9D</p>
<p>One answer is deep domain expertise. Rock Health found that founders who=
 have worked inside the healthcare organizations they sell to are better ab=
le to identify solvable problems and =E2=80=9Csee through the buyer=E2=80=
=99s eyes.=E2=80=9D This is hardly rocket science: A clinician or administr=
ator knows which apparently ridiculous constraint cannot simply be designed=
 away. More importantly, they know which questions are worth asking and whi=
ch problems are worth spending years trying to solve. </p>
<p>Healthcare is making the value of expertise more visible, but I doubt th=
at value will remain confined to this domain. Law, finance, manufacturing, =
and education all run on tacit knowledge that never appears in a model=E2=
=80=99s training data=E2=80=94and selling into them takes people who unders=
tand the unofficial workflows and the competing incentives. </p>
<p>While we still need people with fresh eyes, I believe the best founders =
will need old scars.=E2=80=94<em><u><a href=3D"https://every.to/emails/clic=
k/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJq=
