1cmwiOiJodHRwczovL2V2ZXJ5LnRvL2FjY291bnQiLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6NX0=3D/1/0100019fe=
c95c59b-eb9c0ab8-0631-4c6a-9bdb-a20be7e56190-000000/TSX6tb7_wxsv84dCqki-Lvw=
0IXWZCp3l8cyCEphNUDQ=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">S=
ign up</a></u> to get it in your inbox.</em></p>
<p></p>
<hr class=3D"quill-line">
<p></p>
<p>=E2=80=9CThe feature is live lol.=E2=80=9D </p>
<p>This sentence is not a combination of words I thought I=E2=80=99d ever u=
se, especially about something I built. That =E2=80=9Clol=E2=80=9D is a 100=
 percent organic, all-natural millennial nervous lol. I wasn=E2=80=99t laug=
hing. The agent reviewing my code wasn=E2=80=99t either. It had just told m=
e that the feature I had put into my app had to come down while we figured =
out whether it had exposed a security problem.</p>
<p>Hi, I=E2=80=99m a <u><a href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Feve=
ry.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebef=
cc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiSSBWaWJlIENvZGVkIGEgU2VjdXJpdHkgUmlzayIsIn=
Bvc3RfaWQiOjQ0MDUsInBvc3RfdHlwZSI6InBvc3QiLCJ1cmwiOiJodHRwczovL2V2ZXJ5LnRvL=
3dvcmtpbmctb3ZlcnRpbWUvaXQtcy1tZS1oaS1pLW0tdGhlLXZpYmUtY29kZXIiLCJwb3NpdGlv=
biI6Nn0=3D/1/0100019fec95c59b-eb9c0ab8-0631-4c6a-9bdb-a20be7e56190-000000/G=
bAtDOkta-kPz9v20wK2NorBlaThg9aHyqcAp5L9bSU=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferre=
r" target=3D"_blank">baby vibe coder</a></u>. You=E2=80=99re probably wonde=
ring how I got here. The answer is a rich stew of factors: imagination and =
ignorance, hubris and=E2=80=94because how could it not=E2=80=94AI.</p>
<p>This past January, as Claude <u><a href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/http=
s:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce6=
87adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiSSBWaWJlIENvZGVkIGEgU2VjdXJpdHk=
gUmlzayIsInBvc3RfaWQiOjQ0MDUsInBvc3RfdHlwZSI6InBvc3QiLCJ1cmwiOiJodHRwczovL2=
V2ZXJ5LnRvL3ZpYmUtY2hlY2svdmliZS1jaGVjay1vcHVzLTQtNS1pcy10aGUtY29kaW5nLW1vZ=
GVsLXdlLXZlLWJlZW4td2FpdGluZy1mb3IiLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6N30=3D/1/0100019fec95c59=
b-eb9c0ab8-0631-4c6a-9bdb-a20be7e56190-000000/eUv8eMuGvkGb0gGVajqPot0yOqt2-=
glmi1ZHuPxFY_A=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">Opus 4.=
5</a></u> was blowing everyone=E2=80=99s minds and <u><a href=3D"https://ic=
u.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f8769=
8e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiSSBWaWJlIENv=
ZGVkIGEgU2VjdXJpdHkgUmlzayIsInBvc3RfaWQiOjQ0MDUsInBvc3RfdHlwZSI6InBvc3QiLCJ=
1cmwiOiJodHRwczovL2V2ZXJ5LnRvL2d1aWRlcy9hZ2VudC1uYXRpdmUiLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6OH=
0=3D/1/0100019fec95c59b-eb9c0ab8-0631-4c6a-9bdb-a20be7e56190-000000/n3WMdpk=
O28IKpmkW7xY91wLQGcd9xs3wHSIWwRZGcT4=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" tar=
get=3D"_blank">agent-native architecture</a></u> was starting to emerge as =
a new paradigm for building software, I felt the urge to vibe code: What if=
 <em>I</em> built an app designed to work directly with AI agents?</p>
<p>Reader, I did. My app Tastemaker lets you collect clips from writing you=
 admire, describe what you like about them, and generate a <u><a href=3D"ht=
tps://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05=
e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiSSBW=
aWJlIENvZGVkIGEgU2VjdXJpdHkgUmlzayIsInBvc3RfaWQiOjQ0MDUsInBvc3RfdHlwZSI6InB=
vc3QiLCJ1cmwiOiJodHRwczovL2V2ZXJ5LnRvL2d1aWRlcy9ob3ctdG8tYnVpbGQtYW4tYWktc3=
R5bGUtZ3VpZGUiLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6OX0=3D/1/0100019fec95c59b-eb9c0ab8-0631-4c6a-=
9bdb-a20be7e56190-000000/ah3_dOc5KE9Pz1Q0b2T8KmuAiBdAtELCIoFY64jFpCc=3D452"=
 rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">style guide</a></u> from the=
 patterns. Once it appeared to be working, with all the pride of a preschoo=
ler bringing her fingerpainting home for mom to put on the fridge, I bought=
 a domain and unleashed it into the world.</p>
<p>The app worked. People could use it. To my astonishment, a handful of pe=
ople actually did. It became a small, live monument to my multi-hyphenate a=
bilities: proof that I had become a writer-builder with a real-live product=
, rather than a writer with product ideas.</p>
<p>And then, like a preschooler left alone with her creation and an open bo=
ttle of paint, I went and ruined the whole thing.</p>
<p>Researchers at OpenAI have a name for what I was doing as I fiddled with=
 API keys, Supabase (a backend database service I barely understand), and a=
 whole basket of vocabulary words I=E2=80=99d first heard a year ago. They =
call it <u><a href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femail=
s%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e24=
2%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiSSBWaWJlIENvZGVkIGEgU2VjdXJpdHkgUmlzayIsInBvc3RfaWQiOjQ=
0MDUsInBvc3RfdHlwZSI6InBvc3QiLCJ1cmwiOiJodHRwczovL29wZW5haS5jb20vaW5kZXgvaG=
93LWFpLWlzLWV4cGFuZGluZy13aGF0LXBlb3BsZS1kby1hdC13b3JrLyIsInBvc2l0aW9uIjoxM=
H0=3D/1/0100019fec95c59b-eb9c0ab8-0631-4c6a-9bdb-a20be7e56190-000000/JTACrf=
cBy4UMMTEpmeqr8YGfnmwBOenutzP3wFp3QOY=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" ta=
rget=3D"_blank">task crossover</a></u>: using AI to do work historically as=
sociated with another occupation. In their analysis of more than 800,000 wo=
rk-related ChatGPT messages, 16.8 percent involved task crossover.</p>
<p>Somewhere, there are marketers debugging websites, small-business owners=
 reviewing contracts, and other writers looking at a working app and thinki=
ng: Well, if I can do <em>this</em>, what else can I do?</p>
<p>For me, the answer turned out to be: enough to get myself into trouble.<=
/p>
<p>You can see the appeal. A person with a specific problem no longer has t=
o find the specialist who might solve it, make the case that the problem de=
serves their time, and wait for it to make its way to the top of their to-d=
o list. AI can help us make something before it gives us the ability to tel=
l whether it is safe or ready for other people.</p>
<p>Let me tell you my tale of woe.</p>
<h2 id=3D"the-beginners-hubris"><strong>The beginner=E2=80=99s hubris</stro=
ng></h2>
<p>Tastemaker was a place to collect writing I loved and turn my opinions a=
bout it into something I could use. I had spent years doing versions of thi=
s manually: copying sentences into notes apps, underlining lines in books, =
and trying to explain why one paragraph had electricity and another had the=
 emotional texture of an onboarding email.</p>
<p>Then I had one more idea.</p>
<p>I wanted people to connect their Tastemaker profile directly to Claude C=
ode, Codex, or whatever agent they were using, so the agent could retrieve =
their style guide, once they had one, and add new samples without sending t=
hem from their agent back to Tastemaker. The technical word for this, which=
 I was just aware enough of to ask for by name, is an MCP: a way for an AI =
agent to connect to an outside service. (I want it on the record that I tho=
ught of it before I knew we were adding something similar to Every=E2=80=99=
s <u><a href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fcl=
ick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2Fey=
JzdWJqZWN0IjoiSSBWaWJlIENvZGVkIGEgU2VjdXJpdHkgUmlzayIsInBvc3RfaWQiOjQ0MDUsI=
nBvc3RfdHlwZSI6InBvc3QiLCJ1cmwiOiJodHRwczovL2V2ZXJ5LnRvL29uLWV2ZXJ5L3NwaXJh=
bC00LTAtZ29lcy1hZ2VudC1uYXRpdmUiLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6MTF9/1/0100019fec95c59b-eb9=
c0ab8-0631-4c6a-9bdb-a20be7e56190-000000/RznRvJfL3gN-iVNACQQiw3CJ6nfFe5WVqB=
7fNGVNiHc=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">writing agen=
t, Spiral</a></u>.)</p>
<p>The idea made immediate sense, which should perhaps have been my first w=
arning sign. Tastemaker knew what you liked, and your agent was where you d=
id the writing. A direct connection would spare people the annoying trip be=
tween the two. I could make the app more useful and more like the kind of s=
ophisticated product I now believed myself to be capable of building.</p>
<p>I=E2=80=99m not an idiot, though. I did ask a friend who is an experienc=
ed software engineer whether this was a security nightmare waiting to happe=
n.</p>
<p>He told me that an authenticated API wouldn=E2=80=99t get riskier just b=
ecause an agent was using it=E2=80=94it only ever does what it=E2=80=99s as=
ked. A backend agent that managed user access was another matter: It decide=
s who gets in, so a wrong or manipulated call could open doors it shouldn=
=E2=80=99t. It was good advice, but not a security review of what I built.<=
/p>
<p>I took his explanation back to Claude and gave it the rough technical eq=
uivalent of: Make sure you do the safe version.</p>
<p>Claude built the connector. It ran its checks. It described the feature =
as done. I tested it and it worked, and because my coding-toddler brain equ=
ated =E2=80=9Cworks=E2=80=9D with =E2=80=9Cis safe,=E2=80=9D I said what I=
=E2=80=99ve come to see as among the most perilous words a vibe coder can s=
ay: =E2=80=9CCommit and deploy.=E2=80=9D </p>
<p>Later, I got access to <u><a href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%=
2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce=
5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiSSBWaWJlIENvZGVkIGEgU2VjdXJpdHkgUmlza=
yIsInBvc3RfaWQiOjQ0MDUsInBvc3RfdHlwZSI6InBvc3QiLCJ1cmwiOiJodHRwczovL2V2ZXJ5=
LnRvL3ZpYmUtY2hlY2svZ3B0LTUtNi1zb2wiLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6MTJ9/1/0100019fec95c59b=
-eb9c0ab8-0631-4c6a-9bdb-a20be7e56190-000000/H49FswroyVtTp-Tfm0dxg-307z7JR9=
X82AJb5FnrDC4=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">GPT-5.6 =
Sol</a></u> and pointed it at Tastemaker to see what an even newer model wo=
uld think of my code. I expected criticism of the structure or a recommenda=
tion to prune old code.</p>
<p>Instead, it found that the live connector had a public registration rout=
e=E2=80=94an open door anyone could walk through=E2=80=94that should not ha=
ve been public.</p>
<p>Mercifully, there was no evidence that anyone had accessed user data. Bu=
t the feature was live, the vulnerability waiting to be exploited, and the =
review found enough risk that Sol asked for permission to shut down the con=
nector and invalidate its active sessions while it was investigated.</p>
<p>I approved it immediately.</p>
<p>Sol offered to build a safer version, but I declined. I had touched the =
stove and been burned. I needed some time to recover before I could decide =
if it was safe to touch it again.</p>
<h2 id=3D"when-human-cognition-gets-you-in-trouble">When human cognition ge=
ts you in trouble </h2>
<p>My first instinct was to make this a story about a nontechnical person g=
etting a little too high on her own supply. But I don=E2=80=99t think my ow=
n hubris is the whole story=E2=80=94nor do I think I am uniquely susceptibl=
e to the siren song of task crossover. </p>
<p>If you asked me, =E2=80=9CAre you a security engineer?=E2=80=9D I would =
have said no, of course not. I fell into a much subtler, more dangerous tra=
p: overestimating my own ability to understand. After all, <em>I </em>wasn=
