ZGVzL2NvZGV4LWZvci1rbm93bGVkZ2Utd29yaz9zb3VyY2U9cG9zdF9idXR0b24iLCJwb3NpdGl=
vbiI6MTJ9 offers one opinionated perspective on how to get the most out of =
Codex.

We published the guide less than a month ago, but because so much =
keeps changing with Codex, we expedited an update, including:

 1. A new map of how projects, threads, Goals, plugins, and Sites fit =
together
 2. A deeper explanation of how Codex reaches your work through =
local files, connected apps, skills, MCP servers, browser use, and computer=
 control
 3. Stronger guidance on mobile control, team handoffs, =
permissions, human review, and workflow ownership
 4. A 30-day plan for =
moving from one reliable personal workflow to more advanced uses such as =
plugins, Sites, and automation

This guide is a jump start for Codex, not =
the definitive way to use the tool. The more you work with Codex, the more =
you learn to ask it what it needs from you=E2=80=94and the more you =
discover it can do. One insider tip: Give the whole guide to Codex, tell it=
 about your role and tools, and ask it to help you choose your first =
workflow.=E2=80=94Katie Parrott https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e=
