Here are the highlights:

 1. More work is happening overnight. Fable 5 is =
the first model capable enough that you can hand it a complex task, walk =
away, and trust it will be completed by morning. When it hits an =
obstacle=E2=80=94a remote service goes down, say, or a tool stops =
working=E2=80=94it writes a workaround and forges ahead. That resilience =
has changed the daily rhythm of Krieger=E2=80=99s work: He now ends his =
workday by briefing the model on what needs to get done while he sleeps, =
rather than sitting down to do it himself.
 2. The gap between =
what=E2=80=99s in your head and what exists in the world is closing. Given =
access to Fable 5 and a set of internal MCPs, an Anthropic recruiter =
described the experience as, =E2=80=9CThe first time in my life where I =
feel like the thing that=E2=80=99s in my head and the thing that exists in =
the world are right next to each other. I can just do it.=E2=80=9D This is =
the most meaningful thing about the new model class, Krieger =
says=E2=80=94it allows non-engineers to create the exact products they need=
 to get more done.
 3. Software engineering is dead. Long live software =
engineering. Engineers now spend less time writing code and more time =
setting direction, reviewing what their AI agents have built, and making =
judgment calls when something breaks in production. The divide between =
product managers and engineers has blurred. =E2=80=9CThere is a feeling of =
loss, I think, in some of the better engineers that I talk to, as well as =
the feeling of, =E2=80=98Oh my God, but I can do insane amounts of work now=
 at the same time.=E2=80=99 We=E2=80=99re holding both ideas in our heads =
at once,=E2=80=9D Krieger says.
 4. All eyes are on verification. If we can=
 delegate more to the model, it becomes more important to check what it has=
 built works in practice. Krieger=E2=80=99s approach combines regression =
testing on known workflows, visual checks=E2=80=94including giving the =
model video captures of its own work so it can catch animation glitches =
screenshots would miss=E2=80=94and mock backends for anything too complex =
to test live. When a bug arrives via Slack, Fable 5 makes the fix, posts =
the pull request, then follows up hours later.

