ble 5 with Mike Krieger</h2>
<p>Today, we=E2=80=99re releasing a new episode of our podcast <em><u><a hr=
ef=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f=
95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0=
IjoiSG93IHRvIEdldCB0aGUgTW9zdCBPdXQgb2YgRmFibGUgNSIsInBvc3RfaWQiOjQyOTQsInB=
vc3RfdHlwZSI6InBvc3QiLCJ1cmwiOiJodHRwczovL2V2ZXJ5LnRvL3BvZGNhc3QiLCJwb3NpdG=
lvbiI6OX0=3D/1/0100019eb2c73e08-e17d9e2b-d639-4250-9ff2-29e86f7e343e-000000=
/ybmXljwuuqWnDcne86c1jfkTR4YEWq57TPjQwUIB6lU=3D452" rel=3D"noopener norefer=
rer" target=3D"_blank">AI &amp; I</a></u></em>. <strong><u><a href=3D"https=
://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60=
f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiSG93IHR=
vIEdldCB0aGUgTW9zdCBPdXQgb2YgRmFibGUgNSIsInBvc3RfaWQiOjQyOTQsInBvc3RfdHlwZS=
I6InBvc3QiLCJ1cmwiOiJodHRwczovL2V2ZXJ5LnRvL0BkYW5zaGlwcGVyIiwicG9zaXRpb24iO=
jEwfQ=3D=3D/1/0100019eb2c73e08-e17d9e2b-d639-4250-9ff2-29e86f7e343e-000000/=
YIy03y-q59FNqZEPm2KDzT56iejw4p2lk7TiU3RQWGI=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferr=
er" target=3D"_blank">Dan Shipper</a></u></strong> sits down with <strong>M=
ike Krieger</strong>, the cofounder of Instagram and head of Anthropic Labs=
, to discuss what it feels like to build with <u><a href=3D"https://icu.eve=
ry.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654=
f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiSG93IHRvIEdldCB0a=
GUgTW9zdCBPdXQgb2YgRmFibGUgNSIsInBvc3RfaWQiOjQyOTQsInBvc3RfdHlwZSI6InBvc3Qi=
LCJ1cmwiOiJodHRwczovL2V2ZXJ5LnRvL3ZpYmUtY2hlY2svYW50aHJvcGljLW15dGhvcy1vdXI=
tZmFibGUtdmliZS1jaGVjayIsInBvc2l0aW9uIjoxMX0=3D/1/0100019eb2c73e08-e17d9e2b=
-d639-4250-9ff2-29e86f7e343e-000000/IzLDCHS22KAILUdSkK-ed83afOgTD7BhnZx9HS5=
924s=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">Fable 5</a></u>, =
a model powerful enough that it=E2=80=99s forcing him to rethink the very d=
efinition of productivity, engineering, and creative agency.</p>
<p>As someone who built one of the most popular consumer apps in the pre-GP=
T era and has had access to Fable 5 for months, Krieger has a rare vantage =
