el capable enough that you can hand it a complex task, walk away, and trust=
 it will be completed by morning. When it hits an obstacle=E2=80=94a remote=
 service goes down, say, or a tool stops working=E2=80=94it writes a workar=
ound and forges ahead. That resilience has changed the daily rhythm of Krie=
ger=E2=80=99s work: He now ends his workday by briefing the model on what n=
eeds to get done while he sleeps, rather than sitting down to do it himself=
.</li>
<li>
<strong>The gap between what=E2=80=99s in your head and what exists in the =
world is closing.</strong> Given access to Fable 5 and a set of internal MC=
Ps, an Anthropic recruiter described the experience as, =E2=80=9CThe first =
time in my life where I feel like the thing that=E2=80=99s in my head and t=
he thing that exists in the world are right next to each other. I can just =
do it.=E2=80=9D <em>This</em> is the most meaningful thing about the new mo=
del class, Krieger says=E2=80=94it allows non-engineers to create the exact=
 products they need to get more done.</li>
<li>
<strong>Software engineering is dead. Long live software engineering.</stro=
ng> Engineers now spend less time writing code and more time setting direct=
ion, reviewing what their AI agents have built, and making judgment calls w=
hen something breaks in production. The divide between product managers and=
 engineers has blurred. =E2=80=9CThere is a feeling of loss, I think, in so=
me of the better engineers that I talk to, as well as the feeling of, =E2=
=80=98Oh my God, but I can do insane amounts of work now at the same time.=
=E2=80=99 We=E2=80=99re holding both ideas in our heads at once,=E2=80=9D K=
rieger says.</li>
<li>
<strong>All eyes are on verification.</strong> If we can delegate more to t=
he model, it becomes more important to check what it has built works in pra=
ctice. Krieger=E2=80=99s approach combines regression testing on known work=
flows, visual checks=E2=80=94including giving the model video captures of i=
ts own work so it can catch animation glitches screenshots would miss=E2=80=
=94and mock backends for anything too complex to test live. When a bug arri=
ves via Slack, Fable 5 makes the fix, posts the pull request, then follows =
