<h4 id=3D"example-1-fix-a-broken-workflow"><strong>Example 1: Fix a broken =
workflow</strong></h4>
<p>Senior engineer <strong><u><a href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F=
%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adc=
e5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiSG93IHRvIEdldCB0aGUgTW9zdCBPdXQgb2Yg=
RmFibGUgNSIsInBvc3RfaWQiOjQyOTQsInBvc3RfdHlwZSI6InBvc3QiLCJ1cmwiOiJodHRwczo=
vL2V2ZXJ5LnRvL0BuaXR5ZXNoIiwicG9zaXRpb24iOjMwfQ=3D=3D/1/0100019eb2c73e08-e1=
7d9e2b-d639-4250-9ff2-29e86f7e343e-000000/cA0AlREO9_Ho1LO7FQ55EsN2nhmWgEkx_=
143ceznAHI=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">Nityesh Aga=
rwal</a></u></strong> built a Claude Code skill to help Every=E2=80=99s con=
sulting team create first drafts of PowerPoint decks. It worked, but it kep=
t hitting the same snags: Boxes were slightly misaligned, images weren=E2=
=80=99t the right size, and sometimes a footer would be updated on one slid=
e but not another. One run with Claude Code took about 30 minutes, used rou=
ghly 100 million tokens, and still came back with errors.</p>
<p>Nityesh pointed Fable 5 at the Claude Code session log and asked it to r=
eview where the PowerPoint skill was breaking down.</p>
<p>Fable 5 found the root problem. Under the hood, a PowerPoint file is a b=
undle of XML files that store the position, size, styling, and order of eve=
rything on a slide. Claude was being asked to edit those hidden files direc=
tly, so a simple request like =E2=80=9Cchange this phrase=E2=80=9D or =E2=
=80=9Cmove this image two inches left=E2=80=9D required the model to find t=
he right hidden text and rewrite the surrounding layout code without distur=
bing anything else.</p>
<p>Fable 5 built a command-line tool that gives agents a more natural way t=
o work with PowerPoint=E2=80=94 if the text on a specific slide needs to be=
 updated, for example, or an image has to be resized, the agent can use the=
 tool to make these targeted changes instead of having to rewrite the entir=
e XML file.   </p>
<p><strong>Nityesh=E2=80=99s takeaway: Use Fable 5 to diagnose broken workf=
lows, create the tools or skills that fix them, and then let cheaper models=
 use that infrastructure going forward.</strong></p>
