<h4 id=3D"example-2-create-a-go-to-market-strategy"><strong>Example 2: Crea=
te a go-to-market strategy</strong></h4>
<p><strong><u><a href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Fem=
ails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966=
e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiSG93IHRvIEdldCB0aGUgTW9zdCBPdXQgb2YgRmFibGUgNSIsInBv=
c3RfaWQiOjQyOTQsInBvc3RfdHlwZSI6InBvc3QiLCJ1cmwiOiJodHRwczovL2V2ZXJ5LnRvL29=
uLWV2ZXJ5L2F1c3Rpbi10ZWRlc2NvLWpvaW5zLWV2ZXJ5LWFzLWhlYWQtb2YtZ3Jvd3RoIiwicG=
9zaXRpb24iOjMxfQ=3D=3D/1/0100019eb2c73e08-e17d9e2b-d639-4250-9ff2-29e86f7e3=
43e-000000/eludkZw_ViPh4fNqBi0MPdBzk-F_He-i1ocmF_R7Vpo=3D452" rel=3D"noopen=
er noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">Austin Tedesco</a></u></strong>, Every=E2=
=80=99s head of growth, had a lackluster first experience using Fable 5 to =
generate a go-to-market strategy for this week=E2=80=99s model launch. He a=
sked it to look across Slack and Notion for relevant context, but the outpu=
t didn=E2=80=99t feel meaningfully better than what he might have gotten fr=
om GPT-5.5 or Opus 4.8. =E2=80=9CIt did a good job of synthesizing what we =
had all said and compiling it. But I thought, =E2=80=98This plan isn=E2=80=
=99t any better than what we would have done,=E2=80=99=E2=80=9D he says. =
=E2=80=9CIt=E2=80=99s acting as a very expensive, verbose executive assista=
nt.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p>For his next attempt, Austin put more effort into framing a more complex=
 problem, asking Fable to look at a large set of Every audience insights=E2=
=80=94survey results, PostHog data, brand positioning work=E2=80=94and audi=
t them against the actual <u><a href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%=
2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce=
5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiSG93IHRvIEdldCB0aGUgTW9zdCBPdXQgb2YgR=
mFibGUgNSIsInBvc3RfaWQiOjQyOTQsInBvc3RfdHlwZSI6InBvc3QiLCJ1cmwiOiJodHRwOi8v=
ZXZlcnkudG8iLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6MzJ9/1/0100019eb2c73e08-e17d9e2b-d639-4250-9ff2=
-29e86f7e343e-000000/0WgUcutBecmC7bLcX47guMlNp9RpLAEqBjp6STYnoMw=3D452" rel=
=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">Every.to</a></u> website experie=
nce, while considering the team=E2=80=99s quarterly plans and internal goal=
s. Then he gave it a clear business objective=E2=80=94increase paid subscri=
ptions among those target customer profiles.</p>
<p>He was also more specific in what he wanted back: a Notion report with 1=
0 data insights that might change how the team operated, plus a stack-ranke=
d list of 10 things Every should ship or try.</p>
<p>The difference was striking. =E2=80=9C<strong><u><a href=3D"https://icu.=
every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e=
654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiSG93IHRvIEdldC=
B0aGUgTW9zdCBPdXQgb2YgRmFibGUgNSIsInBvc3RfaWQiOjQyOTQsInBvc3RfdHlwZSI6InBvc=
3QiLCJ1cmwiOiJodHRwczovL2V2ZXJ5LnRvL0BkYW5zaGlwcGVyIiwicG9zaXRpb24iOjMzfQ=
=3D=3D/1/0100019eb2c73e08-e17d9e2b-d639-4250-9ff2-29e86f7e343e-000000/vk1PU=
_GvexEj_yz2qhX5psxUddkCfIxKn3Ik_p9StZw=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" t=
arget=3D"_blank">Dan [Shipper]</a></u></strong> and I kept saying, =E2=80=
=98This is nuts,=E2=80=99=E2=80=9D Austin says. =E2=80=9CIf we hired a go-t=
o-market engineer to do this and they turned this around in two weeks, we w=
ould say, =E2=80=98This was an incredible hire.=E2=80=99=E2=80=9D</p>
<p><strong>Austin=E2=80=99s takeaway: Fable 5 performs much better on knowl=
edge work when you give it a complex problem, full access to relevant sourc=
es of truth, a clear goal, and a specific output.</strong> If you ask it to=
 =E2=80=9Cmake a plan,=E2=80=9D it may summarize what people already agree =
on. If you ask it to use data to test assumptions and produce a ranked set =
of decisions, the results are much sharper.</p>
