Ob30lNujwLVoE=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">Sonnet 4=
.6</a></u>.) </p>
<p>But cost is only one part of the decision. Fable 5 is also slow, especia=
lly when you run it at higher effort levels, so it makes the most sense for=
 large, complex, delegable jobs you can trust the model to complete and rev=
iew later, such as fixing a broken workflow, building a feature or app, syn=
thesizing a lot of source material, or reviewing a codebase. For quick edit=
s, small bugs, and back-and-forth brainstorming, faster and cheaper models =
remain the better option. Read more about the model=E2=80=99s strengths and=
 weaknesses in <u><a href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%=
2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e1=
