ALIGNMENT

The worried well. I=E2=80=99m a Midjourney fanboy. I pay for it, I defend =
it at dinner against people who think AI can=E2=80=99t make art, and I =
think it makes the most beautiful images on the internet. So I am the wrong=
 person to ask whether the AI image generator=E2=80=99s next idea is a good=
 one, but given the fever pitch discussions on X last week about its latest=
 venture, I=E2=80=99m going to try.

Midjourney wants to lower you into a =
warm pool ringed with half a million ultrasound sensors that map your whole=
 body in 60 seconds without using radiation or the magnets commonly used in=
 big and clunky, and sometimes scary, CT and MRI scans.

The company=E2=80=99s aim is to change imaging from being a dramatic event =
requiring a hospital visit and make it ambient and cheap, the way a blood =
test is. This is the kind of catch-it-early screening tool that sets the =
longevity crowd salivating=E2=80=94a path to preventing disease and, dare I=
 say, living forever.

Doctors, however, are right to push back on the =
underlying premise that healthy people should be getting scanned at all. =
The trouble with scanning healthy people more often is that you find weird =
little things that may mean nothing but can=E2=80=99t be ignored. These are=
 called incidentalomas, and while they=E2=80=99re manageable when patient =
volume is low, they=E2=80=99re not when these scans are done at a =
mega-scale. Midjourney=E2=80=99s stated ambition is to do 1 billion scans a=
 month. If you point that many healthy, anxious people at a health system =
already buckling under demand, you don=E2=80=99t catch disease early so =
much as manufacture a tidal wave of follow-up scans, referrals, biopsies, =
and clinics clogged with people who were perfectly well until someone at a =
medical spa=E2=80=94where the scans are launching first=E2=80=94told them =
otherwise.

But it=E2=80=99s a charged topic, and I understand why. If a =
scan catches the lump that turns out to be cancer, that is worth every =
false alarm in the world to the person it happened to=E2=80=94and the =
testimonies you hear are always from that person. You never hear from the =
thousands who got a biopsy and two weeks of anxiety-inducing dread over =
something that turned out to be nothing.

None of this is meant to take =
away from what Midjourney has built. The scan gives a detailed map of fat, =
visceral fat, liver fat, and lean mass that can be tracked over =
time=E2=80=94very useful for GLP-1 users, who=E2=80=99re increasingly =
fixated on their fat mass to lean mass ratio.

So would I do it? For body =
composition, gladly. To go hunting for what might be hiding inside me, no, =
because I=E2=80=99ve seen where that road leads, and it is paved with =
prickly biopsies. The worried well don=E2=80=99t need another reason to =
worry; they do, however, need to know what they=E2=80=99re made of, and on =
that, the scan delivers.=E2=80=94Ashwin Sharma https://every.=
