452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">380,000 GitHub stars</a>=
</u>. But when I dug into the codebase, I found complexity that created mor=
e problems than it solved.</p>
<h4 id=3D"the-session-problem">The session problem</h4>
<p>OpenClaw keeps a single session running for each user, for as long as it=
 can. Every message you send during the day lands in that same session, pil=
ing up context as it goes. Use OpenClaw for a lot of tasks, and by midday, =
the session can be carrying more than 50,000 tokens=E2=80=94roughly a long =
document=E2=80=99s worth of text. It=E2=80=99s supposed to reset every day =
at 4 a.m., but it can be unreliable. So you might type a simple =E2=80=9Chi=
=E2=80=9D in the morning and get billed for 50,000 tokens=E2=80=94about $0.=
25 on <u><a href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%=
2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%=
