<h2 id=3D"inside-every">Inside Every</h2>
<h4 id=3D"dan-is-cloning-kate-but-not-in-a-weird-way">Dan is cloning Kate, =
but not in a weird way</h4>
<p>For as long as I=E2=80=99ve been at Every, Dan has been chasing the same=
 white whale: cloning our editor in chief, <strong><u><a href=3D"https://ic=
u.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f8769=
8e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiQ2FuIEFJIExl=
YXJuIEdvb2QgSnVkZ21lbnQ_IiwicG9zdF9pZCI6NDMxNywicG9zdF90eXBlIjoicG9zdCIsInV=
ybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vZXZlcnkudG8vb24tZXZlcnkva2F0ZS1sZWUtam9pbnMtZXZlcnktYXMtZW=
RpdG9yLWluLWNoaWVmIiwicG9zaXRpb24iOjI3fQ=3D=3D/1/0100019efa6704bf-07115146-=
17ef-4626-b9e1-cc83ade58e4e-000000/4qQyCJrLgzDtdC6voILeRM54I8ttcaw0TpDEC5U_=
duA=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">Kate Lee</a></u></=
strong>.</p>
<p>Only a narrow slice of her, to be clear. He wants an AI copy editor that=
 can identify the sentence-level problems Kate would catch before she ever =
sees a draft. Copy editing is indispensable, tedious work, and every hour K=
ate spends repairing links and cleaning sentences is an hour she can=E2=80=
=99t spend shaping arguments or developing writers.</p>
<p>Dan=E2=80=99s previous attempts relied on prompts, style guides, and ski=
lls. Those approaches could teach a general-purpose model the rules Kate wa=
s able to articulate, but they couldn=E2=80=99t reproduce the judgment she =
uses when rules collide. The same repetition can feel lazy in one paragraph=
 and essential to the rhythm of another; a hedge can weaken a claim or keep=
 the writer from saying something untrue. Adding more instructions produced=
 an ever-longer list of exceptions, but not Kate-like results.</p>
<p>This time, Dan is changing the model itself. Using <u><a href=3D"https:/=
/icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f8=
7698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiQ2FuIEFJI=
ExlYXJuIEdvb2QgSnVkZ21lbnQ_IiwicG9zdF9pZCI6NDMxNywicG9zdF90eXBlIjoicG9zdCIs=
InVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vdGhpbmtpbmdtYWNoaW5lcy5haS90aW5rZXIvIiwicG9zaXRpb24iOjI=
4fQ=3D=3D/1/0100019efa6704bf-07115146-17ef-4626-b9e1-cc83ade58e4e-000000/uv=
kh0nbt5U9fBn_ZW3Tn4B-EXDZQ0Viwn3Tc9CyrGBA=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer=
" target=3D"_blank">Tinker</a></u>, an API from Thinking Machines that lets=
 builders and programmers train models from their own machine, he has fine-=
tuned three or four candidate models on 30,027 of Kate=E2=80=99s historical=
 suggestions. The models learn Kate=E2=80=99s patterns across thousands of =
real-life examples instead of trying to reconstruct her judgment from promp=
ts and rules..</p>
<p>Dan gives each version of a candidate model the sentences that Kate has =
already edited, but hides her changes. He then compares the model=E2=80=99s=
 suggestions with hers. Anything it misses=E2=80=94or makes worse=E2=80=94b=
ecomes another problem for the next version to solve. He=E2=80=99ll conside=
r a model successful when it catches nine out of every 10 edits Kate would =
make, <em>and</em> Kate can accept nine out of 10 of its suggestions as wri=
tten, without the model ever introducing a serious error. If it works, Kate=
 gets hours back for the editorial decisions that require all of her=E2=80=
=94not only the slice Dan is trying to clone.</p>
<h2><hr class=3D"quill-line"></h2>
<h2 id=3D"steal-this-workflow">Steal this workflow</h2>
<h4 id=3D"agent-see-agent-do">Agent see, agent do </h4>
<p>Here=E2=80=99s a scenario that may sound familiar: You have a recurring =
computer task an agent could handle, but documenting every click, field, an=
d exception would take longer than doing it yourself.</p>
<p>Every=E2=80=99s head of operations <strong>Arielle Shipper</strong> foun=
d a shortcut: She recorded a Slack video of herself completing the task, do=
wnloaded it, and gave it to an LLM to turn the demonstration into reusable =
instructions.</p>
<p>OpenAI=E2=80=99s new <u><a href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2F=
every.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5e=
befcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiQ2FuIEFJIExlYXJuIEdvb2QgSnVkZ21lbnQ_Iiw=
icG9zdF9pZCI6NDMxNywicG9zdF90eXBlIjoicG9zdCIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vZGV2ZWxvcG=
Vycy5vcGVuYWkuY29tL2NvZGV4L3JlY29yZC1hbmQtcmVwbGF5IiwicG9zaXRpb24iOjI5fQ=3D=
=3D/1/0100019efa6704bf-07115146-17ef-4626-b9e1-cc83ade58e4e-000000/6WTqV_fw=
SjhxWAb7DI3Q8IxCS_0LP3VCcms72wHU6EU=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" targ=
et=3D"_blank">Record &amp; Replay</a></u> feature builds that method into C=
odex. It watches you complete a workflow on your Mac, then drafts an editab=
le skill explaining when to use it, what integrations or context it needs t=
o execute the task, what steps to follow, and how to check the result.</p>
<p><strong>The workflow:</strong></p>
<ol>
<li>
<strong>Choose one stable task.</strong> Pick something that=E2=80=99s easi=
er to show than explain: filing an expense, configuring an issue, or downlo=
ading a recurring report. Use realistic inputs without exposing secrets.</l=
i>
<li>
<strong>Perform it for the agent.</strong> Use Record &amp; Replay, or foll=
ow Arielle=E2=80=99s process and upload a screen recording with this prompt=
: =E2=80=9CTurn this demonstration into a reusable skill. Include its trigg=
er, required inputs, steps, and success checks. Flag any decisions you coul=
dn=E2=80=99t infer.=E2=80=9D</li>
<li>
<strong>Add what the recording couldn=E2=80=99t see.</strong> Review the ge=
nerated skill for hidden preferences, naming conventions, defaults, and exc=
eptions. Test it on fresh inputs and correct the instructions where it goes=
 astray.</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Try it this week:</strong> Record the two-minute task you=E2=80=
=99ve avoided documenting because writing the instructions would take longe=
r than doing it.</p>
