t=3D"_blank">Sign up</a></u> to get it in your inbox.</em></p>
<p></p>
<hr class=3D"quill-line">
<p></p>
<p>Most knowledge work still starts with an act of translation. You finish =
a customer call and turn it into a bug report. You think through a story id=
ea on a walk, then wait until you=E2=80=99re back at your laptop to organiz=
e it. Before the real work can begin, you=E2=80=99ve already spent time cle=
aning up the context.</p>
<p>Paired with an AI agent, voice can remove that intermediate step. You ca=
n <u><a href=3D"https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454=
c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiVGhlIERlZmluaXRpdmUgR3V=
pZGUgdG8gVXNpbmcgVm9pY2UgV2l0aCBBSSIsInBvc3RfaWQiOjQzOTUsInBvc3RfdHlwZSI6In=
Bvc3QiLCJ1cmwiOiJodHRwczovL3d3dy5tb25vbG9ndWUudG8iLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6OH0=3D" r=
el=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">speak while the details are fr=
esh</a></u>, point the agent toward the relevant transcripts, code, documen=
ts, or messages, define the outcome you want, and review what it produces.<=
/p>
<p>A useful way to start is with a five-step loop:</p>
<p><strong>Capture =E2=86=92 retrieve and ground =E2=86=92 define the outco=
me =E2=86=92 act =E2=86=92 review and redirect</strong></p>
<p>Today we=E2=80=99re publishing <u><a href=3D"https://every.to/emails/cli=
ck/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJ=
qZWN0IjoiVGhlIERlZmluaXRpdmUgR3VpZGUgdG8gVXNpbmcgVm9pY2UgV2l0aCBBSSIsInBvc3=
RfaWQiOjQzOTUsInBvc3RfdHlwZSI6InBvc3QiLCJ1cmwiOiJodHRwczovL2V2ZXJ5LnRvL2d1a=
WRlcy9idWlsZC1mYXN0ZXItd2l0aC12b2ljZSIsInBvc2l0aW9uIjo5fQ=3D=3D" rel=3D"noo=
pener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">=E2=80=9CBuild Faster With Voice,=E2=80=
=9D</a></u> a practical guide to using that loop across writing, planning, =
software, communication, and ongoing memory systems.</p>
<p><strong>The full guide is available to paid and All Access Every members=
.</strong> It includes:</p>
<ul>
<li>More than a dozen workflows based on how people at Every use voice with=
 agents</li>
<li>Copyable prompts for turning recordings into article outlines, project =
plans, bug patches, emails, meeting follow-ups, and more</li>
<li>Setup instructions for connecting your notes and transcripts to Codex o=
r Claude</li>
<li>The context, safeguards, and review steps each workflow needs</li>
</ul>
<p>If you=E2=80=99re reading Every for free, the five-step loop above is yo=
urs to try. <strong>To get the complete prompts, setup instructions, and wo=
rkflow library, you=E2=80=99ll need to upgrade to a paid Every subscription=
.</strong></p>
<p>Voice doesn=E2=80=99t eliminate the need for good sources or careful rev=
iew. Agents still need access to the material that has the final say, and c=
onsequential actions should still require your approval. The advantage is t=
hat you no longer have to turn every messy thought into polished instructio=
ns before the work can start.</p>
