  <div class=3D"post-body">
    <p><em>Was this newsletter forwarded to you? <u><a href=3D"https://icu.=
every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e=
654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiSG93IEkgUG9saX=
NoIFNvZnR3YXJlIFRoYXQgQWdlbnRzIEJ1aWx0IiwicG9zdF9pZCI6NDMzOCwicG9zdF90eXBlI=
joicG9zdCIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vZXZlcnkudG8vYWNjb3VudCIsInBvc2l0aW9uIjo1fQ=
=3D=3D/1/0100019f5c62b378-5f5f2946-1d99-4571-81ef-e5290e38f1ce-000000/adT_3=
l5Xydhr-Gwim3p9BFmyQSFUZSiy_Zl7iPf7JI4=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" t=
arget=3D"_blank">Sign up</a></u> to get it in your inbox.</em></p>
<p></p>
<hr class=3D"quill-line">
<p></p>
<p>For most of the history of making software, writing code <em>was</em> th=
e work. You spent your days typing out functions, fighting errors, debuggin=
g migrations, and reading through other people=E2=80=99s code to figure out=
 why a function did what it did. Another day in the code factory. </p>
<p>That=E2=80=99s mostly over. With a good brainstorm and a <u><a href=3D"h=
ttps://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f0=
5e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiSG9=
3IEkgUG9saXNoIFNvZnR3YXJlIFRoYXQgQWdlbnRzIEJ1aWx0IiwicG9zdF9pZCI6NDMzOCwicG=
9zdF90eXBlIjoicG9zdCIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vZXZlcnkudG8vc291cmNlLWNvZGUvc3Rvc=
C1jb2RpbmctYW5kLXN0YXJ0LXBsYW5uaW5nIiwicG9zaXRpb24iOjZ9/1/0100019f5c62b378-=
5f5f2946-1d99-4571-81ef-e5290e38f1ce-000000/_NwyhbBhJUxD5D5fOitnrCT6FUNeLn9=
ax-gvA3naXSs=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">well-stru=
ctured plan</a></u>, today=E2=80=99s models will write code, run tests, fix=
 failures, and hand you back a clean pull request with code changes ready f=
or review. I=E2=80=99ll open my laptop in the morning to a stack of green p=
ull requests that agents shipped overnight, with features ready to merge be=
fore my first meeting. The factory has been automated. </p>
<p>What I=E2=80=99m left to do is sit with the result and decide whether it=
=E2=80=99s any good=E2=80=94and then push it further than the agent could t=
ake it itself. A model doesn=E2=80=99t know what <em>I</em> would call good=
, sitting in front of <em>this</em> feature in <em>this</em> product I=E2=
=80=99m building for <em>these</em> users. Without that final human judgmen=
t, everything the agent produces is functional, but forgettable. A few week=
s ago I clicked on an email card in <strong><u><a href=3D"https://icu.every=
.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f4=
54c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiSG93IEkgUG9saXNoIFN=
vZnR3YXJlIFRoYXQgQWdlbnRzIEJ1aWx0IiwicG9zdF9pZCI6NDMzOCwicG9zdF90eXBlIjoicG=
9zdCIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vY29yYS5jb21wdXRlciIsInBvc2l0aW9uIjo3fQ=3D=3D/1/01=
00019f5c62b378-5f5f2946-1d99-4571-81ef-e5290e38f1ce-000000/akxZu5ELfcFsvk3U=
nXGkw510Hcb8b0FyQPnqcD39SmM=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_b=
lank">Cora</a></u></strong> and knew instantly the animation was wrong=E2=
=80=94it slid in from the top of the screen instead of opening from where I=
=E2=80=99d clicked mid-screen. I told the agent, it fixed it, and I clicked=
 again=E2=80=94better. </p>
<p>Polish is the final step in <u><a href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https=
:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce68=
7adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiSG93IEkgUG9saXNoIFNvZnR3YXJlIFRo=
YXQgQWdlbnRzIEJ1aWx0IiwicG9zdF9pZCI6NDMzOCwicG9zdF90eXBlIjoicG9zdCIsInVybCI=
6Imh0dHBzOi8vZXZlcnkudG8vZ3VpZGVzL2NvbXBvdW5kLWVuZ2luZWVyaW5nIiwicG9zaXRpb2=
4iOjh9/1/0100019f5c62b378-5f5f2946-1d99-4571-81ef-e5290e38f1ce-000000/ZEcra=
_eXJh6fGpXnmt9t7yXTOJkQ1gmeALkZ1XgJxMg=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" t=
arget=3D"_blank">compound engineering</a></u>=E2=80=94the discipline I=E2=
=80=99ve been developing over the past year for building software in a way =
that gets smarter with every iteration. As more of the <u><a href=3D"https:=
//icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f=
87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiSG93IEkg=
UG9saXNoIFNvZnR3YXJlIFRoYXQgQWdlbnRzIEJ1aWx0IiwicG9zdF9pZCI6NDMzOCwicG9zdF9=
0eXBlIjoicG9zdCIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vd3d3LnlvdXR1YmUuY29tL3dhdGNoP3Y9RzBMVH=
Y4aFE1Q3MiLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6OX0=3D/1/0100019f5c62b378-5f5f2946-1d99-4571-81ef=
-e5290e38f1ce-000000/KvHRCjDkmrn8xh8De2_XgyRKLAZIFpaFULdhKJupRqQ=3D452" rel=
=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">middle parts of the process</a><=
/u> gets automated, polish matters more now, because it=E2=80=99s the part =
of the work that=E2=80=99s still yours. Instead of the assembly line worker=
 putting the code together, you=E2=80=99re the person at the end of the lin=
e who decides whether it=E2=80=99s good enough to put your name on. <strong=
> </strong></p>
<h2 id=3D"polish-in-practice"><strong>Polish in practice</strong></h2>
<p>The card animation that looked wrong is a good example of how polish wor=
ks, because animation is something that agents still struggle with (althoug=
h it will improve over time). </p>
<p>The pull request had passed every automated check. The review agents had=
 nothing left to flag for me. I ran /ce-polish=E2=80=94part of the <u><a hr=
ef=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f=
95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0=
IjoiSG93IEkgUG9saXNoIFNvZnR3YXJlIFRoYXQgQWdlbnRzIEJ1aWx0IiwicG9zdF9pZCI6NDM=
zOCwicG9zdF90eXBlIjoicG9zdCIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vZ2l0aHViLmNvbS9FdmVyeUluYy=
9jb21wb3VuZC1lbmdpbmVlcmluZy1wbHVnaW4iLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6MTB9/1/0100019f5c62b3=
78-5f5f2946-1d99-4571-81ef-e5290e38f1ce-000000/AnoH-_JeUY6LH0FcO-OZaloq94qW=
US6KRFHuTUo9Flo=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">compou=
nd engineering plugin</a></u>=E2=80=94which does three things and then gets=
 out of my way. It checks out the branch I want to polish, starts the devel=
opment server in the background, and opens the running app inside my editor=
, right next to the agent. From there, I clicked on an email card to open i=
t and started my assessment. </p>
