<p><br></p>
<p>Once the new design was open beside the agent, I could see that it still=
 felt too loose. There was too much whitespace, and the cards needed to be =
more compact. I said so out loud via <strong><u><a href=3D"https://icu.ever=
y.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f=
454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiSG93IEkgUG9saXNoIF=
NvZnR3YXJlIFRoYXQgQWdlbnRzIEJ1aWx0IiwicG9zdF9pZCI6NDMzOCwicG9zdF90eXBlIjoic=
G9zdCIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vbW9ub2xvZ3VlLnRvIiwicG9zaXRpb24iOjEyfQ=3D=3D/1/0=
100019f5c62b378-5f5f2946-1d99-4571-81ef-e5290e38f1ce-000000/0HYcWcQSIViyFyJ=
r2d2Mkkw3P-WZgDYTIzvhyO9PdQE=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_=
blank">Monologue</a></u></strong>. The agent tightened the layout; the app =
hot-reloaded; I looked again=E2=80=94better. A plan could tell the agent to=
 make the Brief feel like a magazine. It couldn=E2=80=99t tell the agent wh=
en the page had the right density. I had to see it and decide for myself.</=
p>
<p>This is what polish looks like:...</p>
