 * AI is great at making =
better versions of the products you already pay for. Mod=E2=80=99s been =
using LLMs=E2=80=94primarily Opus, more recently Fable=E2=80=94 to =
vibe-code alternatives to SaaS products like the email marketing platform =
Campaign Monitor and personal finance software Quicken. The benefit is =
twofold: He can tailor the service to his exact specifications, and a $1,=
200-a-year Claude fee is way cheaper than paying for multiple subscriptions=
. =E2=80=9CI think we=E2=80=99re going to enter this golden age of tool =
building,=E2=80=9D Mod says. =E2=80=9CThere=E2=80=99s going to be more =
competition in the marketplace forcing more innovation=E2=80=9D=E2=80=94a =
net-positive =E2=80=9Cexcept for incumbents.=E2=80=9D
 * It puts a higher premium on intent. AI allows you to attempt all sorts =
of things that previously required years of expertise and training. The =
possibilities are dizzying, which makes it easy to lose sight of what you =
want to devote your energy toward in the rush of endless production.

Somewhat counterintuitively, the ease with which software can be made now =
has reaffirmed Mod=E2=80=99s commitment to writing. =E2=80=9CThere are =
plenty of people playing around with this stuff,=E2=80=9D he says. =
=E2=80=9CBut there aren=E2=80=99t that many people who are going to think =
about or write the weird books I feel drawn to write, and as a human, that =
feels like the valuable thing for me to put my effort into.=E2=80=9D

While he=E2=80=99ll use AI for research and fact-checking, he still writes =
every word himself. Outsourcing that process to an LLM would defeat the =
purpose when =E2=80=9Cbeing in the mess of writing=E2=80=9D is the =
point=E2=80=94and the way to get the results he=E2=80=99s looking for.

 * Mod creates intentional barriers to maintain focus. He keeps his phone =
on a separate floor from where he sleeps=E2=80=94and does his best not to =
check it until after lunch=E2=80=94and writes on a dedicated MacBook that =
isn=E2=80=99t connected to the internet. As soon as his brain encounters =
WiFi, he says, =E2=80=9CI feel the chemicals shift and I can=E2=80=99t go =
into any kind of deep thinking place, deep attention, deep focus.=E2=80=9D

