I asked Codex to assemble the brief, including an outline=
, plus my voice rules, then sent that packet to Deft via the API. The first=
 two attempts returned drafting instructions instead of the essay. On the =
third, I used Deft=E2=80=99s highest-quality setting. It wrote half the =
piece, stopped, and invented dates, dialogue, product history, screenshots,=
 behaviors, and emotions that weren=E2=80=99t in my sources=E2=80=94even =
though I set the model to strict. I paid $0.49 and got no usable draft.


WHAT=E2=80=99S LEFT FOR DEFT

Deft has shown that it can produce writing =
that is less predictable than most models. What it hasn=E2=80=99t proven =
yet is that it can generate writing that is better. Writing produced by =
models like GPT-5.6 Sol or Sonnet 5 https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455=
f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiSSB=
UcmllZCB0aGUgQUkgTW9kZWwgQnVpbHQgdG8gRml4IEFJIFdyaXRpbmciLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0ND=
UwLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly9ldmVyeS50by92aWJlLWNoZWNrL=
3Nvbm5ldC01IiwicG9zaXRpb24iOjE1fQ=3D=3D may have =E2=80=9CAI smell,=
=E2=80=9D but the telltale signs are predictable enough at this point that =
I know how to spot them and how to break them up. The editing lift with DFT=
 v1=E2=80=99s prose is similar=E2=80=94but with less clarity about where to=
 start.

The model needs a better grasp of information hierarchy, =
sequencing, and reader theory of mind. A strong draft does more than vary =
its syntax. Good writing directs attention. It knows when a term needs =
explaining, when evidence needs context, and how to order information in a =
way that makes the reader lean in. Deft often seemed to make those =
decisions locally, sentence by sentence, without a stable model of the =
whole piece.

I also want the ability to iterate with the model. Deft is =
oriented around complete-document generation, but my writing process =
