<p><br></p>
<p>I asked Codex to assemble the brief, including an outline, plus my voice=
 rules, then sent that packet to Deft via the API. The first two attempts r=
eturned drafting instructions instead of the essay. On the third, I used De=
ft=E2=80=99s highest-quality setting. It wrote half the piece, stopped, and=
 invented dates, dialogue, product history, screenshots, behaviors, and emo=
tions that weren=E2=80=99t in my sources=E2=80=94even though I set the mode=
l to strict. I paid $0.49 and got no usable draft.</p>
<h2 id=3D"whats-left-for-deft">What=E2=80=99s left for Deft</h2>
<p>Deft has shown that it can produce writing that is less predictable than=
 most models. What it hasn=E2=80=99t proven yet is that it can generate wri=
ting that is <em>better</em>. Writing produced by models like GPT-5.6 Sol o=
r <u><a href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fcl=
ick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2Fey=
JzdWJqZWN0IjoiSSBUcmllZCB0aGUgQUkgTW9kZWwgQnVpbHQgdG8gRml4IEFJIFdyaXRpbmciL=
CJwb3N0X2lkIjo0NDUwLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly9ldmVyeS50=
by92aWJlLWNoZWNrL3Nvbm5ldC01IiwicG9zaXRpb24iOjE1fQ=3D=3D/1/010001a035684ea4=
-48bc57a3-952b-405f-9466-b0944c302653-000000/dWoSnuR0QklueTmjFPSj1SyGbyke0w=
efqdA_D0zK4s0=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">Sonnet 5=
</a></u> may have =E2=80=9CAI smell,=E2=80=9D but the telltale signs are pr=
edictable enough at this point that I know how to spot them and how to brea=
k them up. The editing lift with DFT v1=E2=80=99s prose is similar=E2=80=94=
but with less clarity about where to start. </p>
<p>The model needs a better grasp of information hierarchy, sequencing, and=
 reader theory of mind. A strong draft does more than vary its syntax. Good=
 writing directs attention. It knows when a term needs explaining, when evi=
dence needs context, and how to order information in a way that makes the r=
eader lean in. Deft often seemed to make those decisions locally, sentence =
by sentence, without a stable model of the whole piece.</p>
<p>I also want the ability to iterate with the model. Deft is oriented arou=
nd complete-document generation, but <u><a href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0=
/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619e=
afce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiSSBUcmllZCB0aGUgQUkgTW9kZW=
wgQnVpbHQgdG8gRml4IEFJIFdyaXRpbmciLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0NDUwLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb=
3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly9ldmVyeS50by93b3JraW5nLW92ZXJ0aW1lL3dyaXRpbmctd2l0=
aC1haS1pcy1oYXJkZXItdGhhbi15b3UtdGhpbmsiLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6MTZ9/1/010001a03568=
4ea4-48bc57a3-952b-405f-9466-b0944c302653-000000/sv6qDWWDdug35ZGmmDhdQMZTol=
eUbeY93ApsUtzxJDs=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">my w=
riting process</a></u> rarely moves from brief to finished draft in one jum=
p. I want to go back and forth with the model, keep certain parts of its ou=
tput and <u><a href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femai=
ls%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e2=
42%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiSSBUcmllZCB0aGUgQUkgTW9kZWwgQnVpbHQgdG8gRml4IEFJIFdyaX=
RpbmciLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0NDUwLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly9ld=
mVyeS50by93b3JraW5nLW92ZXJ0aW1lL2hvdy10by1rZWVwLXlvdXItd3JpdGluZy13ZWlyZC1p=
bi10aGUtYWdlLW9mLWFpIiwicG9zaXRpb24iOjE3fQ=3D=3D/1/010001a035684ea4-48bc57a=
3-952b-405f-9466-b0944c302653-000000/yXN4qHd1mVydyrPgkOdPwoShkuEbyC4AUWu72b=
2BLkA=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">rework others</a=
></u>, and use the whole arsenal of tools I=E2=80=99ve built to help models=
 write more like me. </p>
<p>Strict mode also needs to mean strict. I want clear rules about sources,=
 instructions that persist, and a way to distinguish facts the model must p=
reserve from possibilities it has permission to develop. Deft already offer=
s an API. I want it to work inside my compound writing workflow. I should b=
e able to say, =E2=80=9CKeep this claim exactly as written, move the jobs s=
ection up, and rewrite only the transition,=E2=80=9D without Deft returning=
 an entirely new essay.</p>
<h2 id=3D"more-stochastic-is-a-start">More stochastic is a start </h2>
<p>Five years ago, researchers <strong>Emily M. Bender</strong>, <strong>Ti=
mnit Gebru</strong>, <strong>Agnelina McMillan-Major</strong>, and =E2=80=
=9C<strong>Schmargaret Schmitchell=E2=80=9D</strong> <u><a href=3D"https://=
icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87=
698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiSSBUcmllZC=
B0aGUgQUkgTW9kZWwgQnVpbHQgdG8gRml4IEFJIFdyaXRpbmciLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0NDUwLCJwb=
3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly9kbC5hY20ub3JnL2RvaS8xMC4xMTQ1LzM0=
NDIxODguMzQ0NTkyMiIsInBvc2l0aW9uIjoxOH0=3D/1/010001a035684ea4-48bc57a3-952b=
-405f-9466-b0944c302653-000000/E1lh7XHjQ-6HQUpCY8qycmwh364lRfJ11Ace2ECD0XE=
=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">coined the term =E2=
=80=9Cstochastic parrot=E2=80=9D</a></u> to describe LLMs=E2=80=94=E2=80=9C=
stochastic=E2=80=9D because language models generate from probabilities, an=
d =E2=80=9Cparrot=E2=80=9D because they can mimic linguistic form without k=
nowing the meaning of the words. Even today, LLMs produce text that is not =
grounded in communicative intent, a model of the world, or a model of the r=
eader.</p>
<p>Deft intervenes in the stochastic half of the metaphor. DFT changes the =
distribution of patterns a model reaches for across a batch of outputs, giv=
ing the parrot a broader repertoire; the results are still probabilistic, b=
ut less probable. DFT=E2=80=99s writing can sound more surprising, but base=
d on my testing, variety alone can=E2=80=99t fix what ails AI writing.</p>
<p>Deft is a promising demonstration that the sameness of AI prose can be t=
reated as a training problem. For a brand-new lab working with an experimen=
tal model, isolating one tractable layer of that stack is a strong start. I=
 wouldn=E2=80=99t yet use Deft for day-to-day work, but I=E2=80=99m curious=
 to see where the model goes, what the lab tackles next, and what other lab=
s may follow. </p>
