<p><strong>What works: </strong>There=E2=80=99s a lot to love about voice m=
ode, which allows you to get work done without having to sit at a keyboard.=
</p>
<p>One of its biggest strengths is that it lets you read and ask questions =
aloud or connect what you=E2=80=99re reading to another file or project. En=
gineer <strong>Lee Knowlton</strong> uploaded a PDF of <em><u><a href=3D"ht=
tps://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05=
e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiTWlu=
aS1WaWJlIENoZWNrOiBDaGF0R1BUIFZvaWNlIE1vZGUiLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0NDAwLCJwb3N0X3R=
5cGUiOiJwcm9tbyIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vd3d3Lm9yZWlsbHkuY29tL2xpYnJhcnkvdmlldy=
9kZXNpZ25pbmctZGF0YS1pbnRlbnNpdmUtYXBwbGljYXRpb25zLzk3ODE0OTE5MDMwNjMvIiwic=
G9zaXRpb24iOjE4fQ=3D=3D/1/0100019fd3267c6e-c81ceb58-9243-414d-9cac-6081ee7d=
a1e1-000000/G1y9vJ_nGCM7ptuQcb41279wKY-ZDvZVh-cssJE1VU0=3D452" rel=3D"noope=
ner noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">Designing Data-Intensive Applications</a>=
</u></em>, a book about building large-scale data systems, while voice mode=
 had access to the codebase he was working on. As a result, he could <u><a =
href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c=
3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZW=
N0IjoiTWluaS1WaWJlIENoZWNrOiBDaGF0R1BUIFZvaWNlIE1vZGUiLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0NDAwL=
CJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwcm9tbyIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8veC5jb20vbGVla25vd2x0b24vc3Rh=
dHVzLzIwODIzODk1ODgyMzczMDM4OTEiLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6MTl9/1/0100019fd3267c6e-c81=
ceb58-9243-414d-9cac-6081ee7da1e1-000000/Fo6zY2J8EjJHhBLhKpOhNt7bfsegbXlVR8=
WA8XLd4xU=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">keep reading=
</a></u> while asking questions aloud, exploring unfamiliar ideas, and conn=
ecting the book=E2=80=99s insights to his own code. The result was a more f=
luid way to learn.</p>
<p>=E2=80=9CShifting from text to voice is different from shifting from tex=
t to text for me,=E2=80=9D he says. =E2=80=9CReading something and then hav=
ing a conversation, or asking a quick question, is different from typing so=
mething and then having to parse more text.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p><strong>What could be better: </strong>During a walk, COO <strong><u><a =
href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c=
3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZW=
N0IjoiTWluaS1WaWJlIENoZWNrOiBDaGF0R1BUIFZvaWNlIE1vZGUiLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0NDAwL=
CJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwcm9tbyIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vZXZlcnkudG8vQGJyYW5kb25fNTI2=
MyIsInBvc2l0aW9uIjoyMH0=3D/1/0100019fd3267c6e-c81ceb58-9243-414d-9cac-6081e=
e7da1e1-000000/c5K8skp9uVJGZBpzym1FXLohwA8dxTtH6eqUfgktm9k=3D452" rel=3D"no=
opener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">Brandon Gell</a></u></strong> found th=
at the mobile app=E2=80=99s voice mode could read a thread=E2=80=99s visibl=
e history but didn=E2=80=99t have access to important context outside the t=
hread. Currently, voice can control local Codex work through <u><a href=3D"=
https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f=
05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiTW=
