7da1e1-000000/Ba3IWcnZpVJsVNNdLpp5ocgc8rL6z6uCz7ahaGWqQPI=3D452" rel=3D"noo=
pener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">Codex</a></u> projects, files, or tools=
.</p>
<p>Further complicating matters, the mobile app also has an =E2=80=9Cordina=
ry voice mode,=E2=80=9D which can use the current cloud conversation but no=
t the local context available through Remote. Are you confused? We=E2=80=99=
re confused.</p>
<p>The model=E2=80=99s ability to distinguish between speech intended for i=
t and ambient conversation was also inconsistent. Lee found it good at filt=
ering out exchanges with his wife, while engineer <strong>Tyler Nishida</st=
rong> had the exact opposite experience. And the lag time can make it hard =
to use as a writing or editing partner (I found voice mode impressive but f=
unctionally too laggy to help me write this piece, for example). Finally, a=
lthough GPT=E2=80=91Live can delegate complex tasks to a frontier model in =
the background, some responses still felt shallow compared with responses f=
rom a text chat set to <u><a href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fe=
very.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5eb=
efcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiTWluaS1WaWJlIENoZWNrOiBDaGF0R1BUIFZvaWNl=
IE1vZGUiLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0NDAwLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwcm9tbyIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8=
vZXZlcnkudG8vdmliZS1jaGVjay9ncHQtNS02LXNvbCIsInBvc2l0aW9uIjoyM30=3D/1/01000=
19fd3267c6e-c81ceb58-9243-414d-9cac-6081ee7da1e1-000000/VfpftRQs14T4gOPoGPz=
QyzawkwY5Hht99Z_iCHPtb8Y=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blan=
k">GPT-5.6 Sol</a></u>. </p>
<p><strong>Final verdict: </strong>Voice mode is, as Dan puts it, =E2=80=9C=
a whole new world=E2=80=9D=E2=80=94one in which you can direct agents away =
from a computer. But there are kinks to work out. </p>
<p>=E2=80=9CIt=E2=80=99s both not quite there yet and obviously the future,=
=E2=80=9D Lee says. =E2=80=9CA week ago, I couldn=E2=80=99t imagine a versi=
