AI has a measurement problem. Companies know how much they spend on models =
and how those models score on public benchmarks. What they often =
don=E2=80=99t know is whether the models save employees time or produce =
work people can trust without rechecking. In today=E2=80=99s Context Window=
 is a look at how companies can answer those questions for themselves: We =
explain why organizations need tests built around real work, show what =
cloning our editor in chief has taught Every about evals, and meet the =
six-agent crew helping an Every engineer decide whether his family can run =
the dryer.



----------------------------------------




SIGNAL

VIBES DON=E2=80=99T SCALE

Suppose your company is spending $100 million a =
year on AI. You know how much you=E2=80=99re paying=E2=80=94and you know =
where the models you=E2=80=99re paying for sit on the public leaderboards. =
But you may still have no idea whether they are doing the jobs you bought =
them for, or whether a cheaper model would do them just as well. This is a =
strange way to spend $100 million.

Mercor cofounder and CEO Brendan Foody =
says https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce68=
7adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiQmVuY2htYXJrcyBEb27igJl0IEtub3cgWW=
91ciBKb2IiLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0NDUxLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6L=
y94LmNvbS9CcmVuZGFuRm9vZHkvc3RhdHVzLzIwOTA1MDA5NDQ5NzkyNDMxODEiLCJwb3NpdGlv=
biI6Nn0=3D he meets executives at companies in exactly this position: They =
spend as much as $100 million a year running models without =
=E2=80=9Coffline evals,=E2=80=9D a fixed set of real tasks used to test and=
 compare models before they touch live work. Box CEO Aaron Levie =
quote-posted Foody https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f=
454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiQmVuY2htYXJrcyBEb27i=
gJl0IEtub3cgWW91ciBKb2IiLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0NDUxLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJ=
sIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly94LmNvbS9sZXZpZS9zdGF0dXMvMjA5MTM1OTIyMzM2ODMxNTA1MCIsInBvc2=
l0aW9uIjo3fQ=3D=3D with the line: =E2=80=9CEnterprises will not be able to =
go just on vibes.=E2=80=9D

Public benchmarks can tell you that one model =
is generally more capable than another. They can=E2=80=99t tell you whether=
 it caught the clause your lawyers care about, preserved your house style, =
or spared an employee another round of checking. A useful eval starts with =
the work your company already does: representative cases, failures =
employees know to look for, and a count of what humans still have to fix.

Meanwhile, the number of plausible choices is multiplying. Investor Gavin =
Baker points to a chart https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698=
e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiQmVuY2htYXJrcyB=
Eb27igJl0IEtub3cgWW91ciBKb2IiLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0NDUxLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0Ii=
widXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly94LmNvbS9HYXZpblNCYWtlci9zdGF0dXMvMjA5MTU0MjAyNjA3MjMzO=
DYyMyIsInBvc2l0aW9uIjo4fQ=3D=3D from Vercel CEO Guillermo Rauch showing =
open-source models growing from 28 percent to 62 percent of token share on =
the frontend cloud platform in two months. Andreessen Horowitz=E2=80=99s =
charts of the week https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f=
454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiQmVuY2htYXJrcyBEb27i=
gJl0IEtub3cgWW91ciBKb2IiLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0NDUxLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJ=
