INSIDE EVERY

WHAT 86 PERCENT DOESN=E2=80=99T TELL YOU

To use KateBench, an editor tags @every to invoke the Every agent, and asks=
 for a Kate copyedit pass. The agent leaves suggestions directly in the =
Google Doc, where the editor decides whether to accept or reject each one.

Across recent runs, editors have accepted about 85 to 90 percent of its =
suggestions. Jannik Jung https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f8769=
8e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiQmVuY2htYXJrcy=
BEb27igJl0IEtub3cgWW91ciBKb2IiLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0NDUxLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0I=
iwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly9ldmVyeS50by90ZWFtIiwicG9zaXRpb24iOjE1fQ=3D=3D, the =
engineer who owns KateBench, showed us two reasons to distrust that number.=
 The tool stopped after filing 40 suggestions, so on long essays it could =
find a good edit and throw it away before the editor saw it. The cap is now=
 80.

https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce6=
87adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiQmVuY2htYXJrcyBEb27igJl0IEtub3cgW=
W91ciBKb2IiLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0NDUxLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6=
Ly9kMjRvdmhndThzNzM0MS5jbG91ZGZyb250Lm5ldC91cGxvYWRzL2VkaXRvci9wb3N0LzQ0NTE=
vb3B0aW1pemVkXzY3ZmQ1NzA2LTA0MTQtNDgzYy1hZWMzLTYxNjM3ZGFjZTczNC5qcGciLCJwb3=
NpdGlvbiI6MTZ9A dashboard view of recent edits completed by the Kate =
copyeditor showing ~90 percent acceptance of edits. (Image courtesy of Dan =
Shipper.)




KateBench also doesn=E2=80=99t produce exactly the same edits=
 every time it reads a document. That means its acceptance rate can rise or=
 fall even when Jannik hasn=E2=80=99t changed anything. A new prompt might =
score higher once without being consistently better, so he has to run each =
version several times before calling it an improvement.


