COUNTERPOINT

DIMINISHING RETURNS, MEASURED HOW?

Olivia Moore, another Andreessen Horowitz partner, tweeted https://every.=
to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e1896=
6e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiQmVuY2htYXJrcyBEb27igJl0IEtub3cgWW91ciBKb2IiLCJwb3N0X=
2lkIjo0NDUxLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly94LmNvbS9vbW9vcmV0=
d2VldHMvc3RhdHVzLzIwOTE2NDc3MTkxNDg1MDMxMDMiLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6MjJ9 on =
Saturday: =E2=80=9CIt feels like we=E2=80=99ve hit diminishing returns on =
intelligence for many tasks. We may no longer see every product auto-switch=
 to the next frontier model upon release.=E2=80=9D For companies building =
products atop models, she argued, slower gains create opportunities to cut =
costs.

Where we agree: Moore is right about many tasks. Mike says Opus 4.8=
 https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adc=
e5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiQmVuY2htYXJrcyBEb27igJl0IEtub3cgWW91ci=
BKb2IiLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0NDUxLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly9ld=
mVyeS50by92aWJlLWNoZWNrL29wdXMtNC04LXZpYmVjaGVjayIsInBvc2l0aW9uIjoyM30=3D =
was the last frontier model Every adopted without hesitation on price or =
quality.

Where we disagree: =E2=80=9CDiminishing returns on =
intelligence=E2=80=9D risks treating today=E2=80=99s task list as a =
comprehensive list of everything models will be capable of, ever. Public =
benchmarks measure a narrow set of capabilities; they can=E2=80=99t tell a =
company whether a model is improving at its own work. KateBench shows how =
easy it is to reach the wrong conclusion. Its high acceptance rate makes =
the tool look nearly finished, but that number changes across identical =
runs and ignores the edits Kate still has to make afterward. Until =
companies build evals that capture that residual work=E2=80=94the work a =
human has to do after the agent completes its task=E2=80=94they cannot tell=
 whether progress has slowed or their measurements are missing it.

What=E2=80=99s missing: Builders still lack a task-specific tool. They =
should cut costs=E2=80=94and keep an eval running, so they can see when the=
 cheaper model fails at the job.


