-G_R95S4B_o0Hx7MGzK6x0=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank"=
>Sign up</a></u> to get it in your inbox.</em></p>
<p></p>
<hr class=3D"quill-line">
<p></p>
<p>AI has a measurement problem. Companies know how much they spend on mode=
ls and how those models score on public benchmarks. What they often don=E2=
=80=99t know is whether the models save employees time or produce work peop=
le can trust without rechecking. In today=E2=80=99s Context Window is a loo=
k at how companies can answer those questions for themselves: We explain wh=
y organizations need tests built around real work, show what cloning our ed=
itor in chief has taught Every about evals, and meet the six-agent crew hel=
ping an Every engineer decide whether his family can run the dryer.</p>
<p></p>
<hr class=3D"quill-line">
<p></p>
<h2 id=3D"signal">Signal</h2>
<h4 id=3D"vibes-dont-scale">Vibes don=E2=80=99t scale</h4>
<p>Suppose your company is spending $100 million a year on AI. You know how=
 much you=E2=80=99re paying=E2=80=94and you know where the models you=E2=80=
=99re paying for sit on the public leaderboards. But you may still have no =
idea whether they are doing the jobs you bought them for, or whether a chea=
per model would do them just as well. This is a strange way to spend $100 m=
illion.</p>
<p>Mercor cofounder and CEO <strong>Brendan Foody</strong> <u><a href=3D"ht=
tps://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05=
e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiQmVu=
Y2htYXJrcyBEb27igJl0IEtub3cgWW91ciBKb2IiLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0NDUxLCJwb3N0X3R5cGU=
iOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly94LmNvbS9CcmVuZGFuRm9vZHkvc3RhdHVzLzIwOTA1MD=
A5NDQ5NzkyNDMxODEiLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6Nn0=3D/1/010001a03a6c3493-c00ebefb-975f-4=
dda-ae37-c5b8f6ba32b6-000000/jrC9U427LmMo1ADQoapdfIlXn-5DJp-Mds3hpQ5zu1A=3D=
452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">says</a></u> he meets ex=
ecutives at companies in exactly this position: They spend as much as $100 =
million a year running models without =E2=80=9Coffline evals,=E2=80=9D a fi=
xed set of real tasks used to test and compare models before they touch liv=
e work. Box CEO <strong>Aaron Levie</strong> <u><a href=3D"https://icu.ever=
y.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f=
454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiQmVuY2htYXJrcyBEb2=
7igJl0IEtub3cgWW91ciBKb2IiLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0NDUxLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0Iiwid=
XJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly94LmNvbS9sZXZpZS9zdGF0dXMvMjA5MTM1OTIyMzM2ODMxNTA1MCIsInBv=
c2l0aW9uIjo3fQ=3D=3D/1/010001a03a6c3493-c00ebefb-975f-4dda-ae37-c5b8f6ba32b=
6-000000/EuP4ConFvExZmwqS1XzbJ0_Na_VHX2sMUHI2xQQsCLM=3D452" rel=3D"noopener=
 noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">quote-posted Foody</a></u> with the line: =
=E2=80=9CEnterprises will not be able to go just on vibes.=E2=80=9D </p>
<p>Public benchmarks can tell you that one model is generally more capable =
than another. They can=E2=80=99t tell you whether it caught the clause your=
 lawyers care about, preserved your house style, or spared an employee anot=
her round of checking. A useful eval starts with the work your company alre=
ady does: representative cases, failures employees know to look for, and a =
count of what humans still have to fix.</p>
<p>Meanwhile, the number of plausible choices is multiplying. Investor <str=
ong>Gavin Baker</strong> <u><a href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2=
Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5=
ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiQmVuY2htYXJrcyBEb27igJl0IEtub3cgWW91ci=
BKb2IiLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0NDUxLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly94L=
mNvbS9HYXZpblNCYWtlci9zdGF0dXMvMjA5MTU0MjAyNjA3MjMzODYyMyIsInBvc2l0aW9uIjo4=
fQ=3D=3D/1/010001a03a6c3493-c00ebefb-975f-4dda-ae37-c5b8f6ba32b6-000000/2tB=
qScil2R7s3NBBlSbBNNtxiOFehhjI4bW8hdWdHZU=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer"=
 target=3D"_blank">points to a chart</a></u> from Vercel CEO <strong>Guille=
rmo Rauch</strong> showing open-source models growing from 28 percent to 62=
 percent of token share on the frontend cloud platform in two months. Andre=
essen Horowitz=E2=80=99s <u><a href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2=
Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5=
ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiQmVuY2htYXJrcyBEb27igJl0IEtub3cgWW91ci=
BKb2IiLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0NDUxLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly93d=
3cuYTE2ei5uZXdzL3AvY2hhcnRzLW9mLXRoZS13ZWVrLXdpbmRzLW9mLXRoZW1hdGljIiwicG9z=
aXRpb24iOjl9/1/010001a03a6c3493-c00ebefb-975f-4dda-ae37-c5b8f6ba32b6-000000=
/7zN5XGWA_Dm9yOsHvZHuxsF73Bjg04yUTiEvy9ke2HE=3D452" rel=3D"noopener norefer=
rer" target=3D"_blank">charts of the week</a></u> report that legal workers=
 have increased Codex adoption 108-fold since February. More models are bec=
oming good enough for more work. Picking the highest-scoring one is no long=
er much of a buying strategy.</p>
<p>A reusable eval gives you a tool for determining whether a model can do =
your company=E2=80=99s work the way you want it done. Run the same set of t=
asks against each candidate, measure the work left for humans, and compare =
the savings. You can test a new model without starting from scratch or trus=
ting the vendor=E2=80=99s favorite score.</p>
<p>At Every, we test each new model against the coding, writing, and knowle=
dge-work tasks our team does every day in our <u><a href=3D"https://icu.eve=
ry.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654=
f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiQmVuY2htYXJrcyBEb=
27igJl0IEtub3cgWW91ciBKb2IiLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0NDUxLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0Iiwi=
dXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly9ldmVyeS50by92aWJlLWNoZWNrIiwicG9zaXRpb24iOjEwfQ=3D=3D/1/=
010001a03a6c3493-c00ebefb-975f-4dda-ae37-c5b8f6ba32b6-000000/h8tSIpszLkKWiN=
ofS9fuUiipu29Sgff-u4lHa5XBONw=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"=
_blank">Vibe Checks</a></u>. Now we=E2=80=99re going a step further: buildi=
ng internal evals that let us compare models over time, and see how wide th=
e gap is between what a model does and what we need it to do. KateBench is =
an AI copyeditor trained on roughly 30,000 of editor in chief <strong><a hr=
ef=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f=
95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0=
IjoiQmVuY2htYXJrcyBEb27igJl0IEtub3cgWW91ciBKb2IiLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0NDUxLCJwb3N=
0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly9ldmVyeS50by9Aa2F0ZV8xNzY3IiwicG9zaX=
Rpb24iOjExfQ=3D=3D/1/010001a03a6c3493-c00ebefb-975f-4dda-ae37-c5b8f6ba32b6-=
000000/sSmdrVobyBNTnfIPjAwO_2fSoQT_CJl5l54--oQ9OSg=3D452" rel=3D"noopener n=
oreferrer" target=3D"_blank">Kate Lee</a>=E2=80=99s </strong>past edits. It=
 suggests changes in a Google Doc, then tracks which ones editors accept or=
 reject, and what they still rewrite afterward. Evals help us determine how=
 close the model=E2=80=99s judgments are to ones Kate might make. </p>
<p><strong>What to do this week:</strong> Choose one recurring job, like co=
mpiling a weekly report or producing a slide deck. Write down five ways the=
 current model gets it wrong, with one example of each (a gold-standard ver=
sion of a report or deck), and run the models you are considering against t=
hose cases. That is the beginning of an eval. It will tell you more about w=
hat to buy than another afternoon spent comparing leaderboards.</p>  <div c=
lass=3D"ea-block normal">
