<p><br></p>
<p>KateBench also doesn=E2=80=99t produce exactly the same edits every time=
 it reads a document. That means its acceptance rate can rise or fall even =
when Jannik hasn=E2=80=99t changed anything. A new prompt might score highe=
r once without being consistently better, so he has to run each version sev=
eral times before calling it an improvement.</p>
<h2 id=3D"links-worth-a-click">Links worth a click</h2>
<p>Software engineer <strong>Steve Yegge </strong><u><a href=3D"https://icu=
.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698=
e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiQmVuY2htYXJrc=
yBEb27igJl0IEtub3cgWW91ciBKb2IiLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0NDUxLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0=
IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly95ZWdnZS5haS9lc3NheXMvZmVuY2VzLW5vdC1zYW5kYm94ZXMiLCJ=
