ive attempts.</p>
<h2 id=3D"counterpoint">Counterpoint</h2>
<h4 id=3D"diminishing-returns-measured-how">Diminishing returns, measured h=
ow?</h4>
<p><strong>Olivia Moore</strong>, another Andreessen Horowitz partner, <u><=
a href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F=
7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJq=
ZWN0IjoiQmVuY2htYXJrcyBEb27igJl0IEtub3cgWW91ciBKb2IiLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0NDUxLCJ=
wb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly94LmNvbS9vbW9vcmV0d2VldHMvc3RhdH=
VzLzIwOTE2NDc3MTkxNDg1MDMxMDMiLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6MjJ9/1/010001a03a6c3493-c00eb=
efb-975f-4dda-ae37-c5b8f6ba32b6-000000/5UnH1Mtkis3WwttT0rEhdo-afGkSKp4aQIKq=
ZETNrfY=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">tweeted</a></u=
> on Saturday: =E2=80=9CIt feels like we=E2=80=99ve hit diminishing returns=
 on intelligence for many tasks. We may no longer see every product auto-sw=
itch to the next frontier model upon release.=E2=80=9D For companies buildi=
ng products atop models, she argued, slower gains create opportunities to c=
ut costs.</p>
<p><strong>Where we agree:</strong> Moore is right about many tasks. Mike s=
ays <u><a href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2F=
click%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2F=
eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiQmVuY2htYXJrcyBEb27igJl0IEtub3cgWW91ciBKb2IiLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo=
0NDUxLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly9ldmVyeS50by92aWJlLWNoZW=
NrL29wdXMtNC04LXZpYmVjaGVjayIsInBvc2l0aW9uIjoyM30=3D/1/010001a03a6c3493-c00=
ebefb-975f-4dda-ae37-c5b8f6ba32b6-000000/R4R-59SOK6mjEsqjCPaERu0I9ibxZC33zf=
KH5ue38TE=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">Opus 4.8</a>=
</u> was the last frontier model Every adopted without hesitation on price =
or quality.</p>
<p><strong>Where we disagree:</strong> =E2=80=9CDiminishing returns on inte=
lligence=E2=80=9D risks treating today=E2=80=99s task list as a comprehensi=
ve list of everything models will be capable of, ever. Public benchmarks me=
asure a narrow set of capabilities; they can=E2=80=99t tell a company wheth=
er a model is improving at its own work. KateBench shows how easy it is to =
reach the wrong conclusion. Its high acceptance rate makes the tool look ne=
arly finished, but that number changes across identical runs and ignores th=
e edits Kate still has to make afterward. Until companies build evals that =
capture that residual work=E2=80=94the work a human has to do after the age=
nt completes its task=E2=80=94they cannot tell whether progress has slowed =
or their measurements are missing it.</p>
<p><strong>What=E2=80=99s missing:</strong> Builders still lack a task-spec=
ific tool. They should cut costs=E2=80=94and keep an eval running, so they =
can see when the cheaper model fails at the job.</p>
<h2 id=3D"one-last-thing">One last thing</h2>
<h4 id=3D"the-dryer-has-an-agent-team">The dryer has an agent team</h4>
<p>Every designer <strong><u><a href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%=
2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce=
5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiQmVuY2htYXJrcyBEb27igJl0IEtub3cgWW91c=
iBKb2IiLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0NDUxLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly9l=
dmVyeS50by90ZWFtIiwicG9zaXRpb24iOjI0fQ=3D=3D/1/010001a03a6c3493-c00ebefb-97=
5f-4dda-ae37-c5b8f6ba32b6-000000/Yr540V3jlYYi01K_ATMjVDgjyAVfsB_fqgNfacL7vQ=
M=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">Tyler Nishida</a></u=
></strong> wanted his family=E2=80=99s off-grid solar system to answer one =
question: Is there enough power to run the dryer?</p>
<p>His family=E2=80=99s place on Hawaii=E2=80=99s Big Island sits in a rain=
forest, so the forecast can=E2=80=99t assume stereotypical Hawaii sunlight.=
 Tyler used Grok Bot to connect a Raspberry Pi=E2=80=94an inexpensive compu=
ter the size of a credit card=E2=80=94 to connect the system. From his phon=
e, he can now check pack voltage and monitor the devices that regulate how =
much electricity flows from the solar panels into the batteries, plus forec=
ast how much energy the system will produce based on the weather, and get a=
n alert when it is time to turn on the generator. </p>
<p>Grok Bot created a channel of six agents to work on the setup. Tyler wat=
ched them message one another. One agent told another what he needed to buy=
; later, an agent sent Tyler the Amazon link in a direct message.</p>
<p>The crew didn=E2=80=99t finish the job alone. Tyler used Grok Build for =
the last steps. His family=E2=80=99s dryer now has a six-agent operations t=
eam.</p>
