<h4 id=3D"a-simple-way-to-make-your-fable-runs-more-token-efficient"><stron=
g>A simple way to make your Fable runs more token-efficient</strong></h4>
<p><strong><u><a href=3D"https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f8769=
8e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiSG93IEV2ZXJ5J3=
MgVGVhbSBVc2VkIEFJIHRvIFNoaXAgSXRzIEJpZ2dlc3QgTGF1bmNoIEV2ZXIiLCJwb3N0X2lkI=
jo0MzUzLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly93cml0ZXdpdGhzcGlyYWwu=
Y29tLz91dG1fc291cmNlPWV2ZXJ5d2Vic2l0ZSIsInBvc2l0aW9uIjozOH0=3D" rel=3D"noop=
ener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">Spiral</a></u> </strong>general manager =
Marcus Moretti wanted to make Every=E2=80=99s internal Slack agent faster a=
nd less token-hungry. After reviewing its slowest sessions, he compiled rou=
ghly 20 changes that could improve its efficiency.</p>
<p>Marcus handed the full list to Fable, asked it to work through the chang=
es as one coordinated run, and went to sleep. Nine hours later, the model h=
ad combined overlapping tasks, dropped ones it judged unnecessary, investig=
ated problems without obvious solutions, opened 10 pull requests, and teste=
d their impact. =E2=80=9CThe PRs themselves were basically ready to go and =
merge,=E2=80=9D Marcus says. (Great!)</p>
<p>The less-great part: Fable had spent roughly 20 millions of tokens to ch=
ange about 5,000 lines of code. Those tokens covered more than writing code=
. Fable also read context, coordinated agents, conducted research, and chec=
ked their work=E2=80=94tasks cheaper models could have handled.</p>
<p>For his next large run, Marcus added an instruction <u><a href=3D"https:=
//every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefc=
c02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiSG93IEV2ZXJ5J3MgVGVhbSBVc2VkIEFJIHRvIFNoaXAgS=
XRzIEJpZ2dlc3QgTGF1bmNoIEV2ZXIiLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0MzUzLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0=
IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly9zaW1vbndpbGxpc29uLm5ldC8yMDI2L0p1bC8zL2p1ZGdlbWVudC8=
iLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6Mzl9" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">shared=
 by independent developer </a></u><strong><u><a href=3D"https://every.to/em=
ails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242=
/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiSG93IEV2ZXJ5J3MgVGVhbSBVc2VkIEFJIHRvIFNoaXAgSXRzIEJpZ2dlc3=
QgTGF1bmNoIEV2ZXIiLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0MzUzLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoia=
HR0cHM6Ly9zaW1vbndpbGxpc29uLm5ldC8yMDI2L0p1bC8zL2p1ZGdlbWVudC8iLCJwb3NpdGlv=
biI6NDB9" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">Simon Willison</a><=
/u></strong>, who credits developer <strong>Jesse Vincent</strong> with the=
 tip:</p>
<blockquote>For all coding tasks use your judgment to decide an appropriate=
 lower-power model and run that in a subagent</blockquote>
<p>The prompt leaves Fable in charge of planning, delegation, and review wh=
ile letting it assign implementation to cheaper models. On Marcus=E2=80=99s=
 second run, Fable chose Sonnet for some jobs and <u><a href=3D"https://eve=
ry.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e1=
8966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiSG93IEV2ZXJ5J3MgVGVhbSBVc2VkIEFJIHRvIFNoaXAgSXRzIE=
JpZ2dlc3QgTGF1bmNoIEV2ZXIiLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0MzUzLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0Iiwid=
XJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly9ldmVyeS50by92aWJlLWNoZWNrL29wdXMtNC04LXZpYmVjaGVjayIsInBv=
c2l0aW9uIjo0MX0=3D" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">Opus</a><=
/u> for others, using fewer Fable tokens.</p>
<p>=E2=80=9CYou don=E2=80=99t need the Fable model itself doing a lot of th=
e nitty-gritty implementation,=E2=80=9D Marcus says. =E2=80=9CYou need it t=
o be the CEO of the run.=E2=80=9D</p>
