<p><br></p>
<p>For personal projects, Nityesh=E2=80=99s entire development loop now hap=
pens in Slack. He assigns a task to Luo Ji, the agent writes the code and p=
osts screenshots, Nityesh requests revisions, and Luo Ji executes and retur=
ns updated screenshots=E2=80=94all within the same thread. (Luo Ji also ope=
ns pull requests, which Nityesh leaves Slack to review=E2=80=94<em>gasp</em=
>=E2=80=94on GitHub.)</p>
<p>Slack was made for work in parallel, separating conversations while maki=
ng sure nothing that needs a response gets buried. Those same features work=
 remarkably well when your colleagues are coding agents. </p>
<p>=E2=80=9CThat challenge is what Slack is built for,=E2=80=9D he says. =
=E2=80=9CThey=E2=80=99ve spent years working on this.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p>If you want your own version of a Slack AI command center, Nityesh creat=
ed <u><a href=3D"https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f45=
4c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiV2hhdCBJZiBTbGFjayBXYX=
MgWW91ciBBSSBDb21tYW5kIENlbnRlciIsInBvc3RfaWQiOjQzNjAsInBvc3RfdHlwZSI6InBvc=
3QiLCJ1cmwiOiJodHRwczovL2dpdGh1Yi5jb20vbml0eWVzaGFnYS9jbGF1ZGUtaG9tZS1iYXNl=
IiwicG9zaXRpb24iOjE3fQ=3D=3D" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank"=
>Claude Home Base</a></u>, an open-source starter kit based on his setup. I=
t includes code for creating a Slack bot, instructions for connecting it to=
 Claude Code, and reusable workflows you can use to build your own Luo Ji.<=
/p>
<h3><hr class=3D"quill-line"></h3>
<h2 id=3D"signal">Signal </h2>
<h4 id=3D"in-which-block-ceo-jack-dorsey-also-has-slack-on-the-brain"><stro=
ng>In which Block CEO Jack Dorsey also has Slack on the brain </strong></h4=
>
<p><strong>What happened: </strong>On July 21, the financial services compa=
ny Block released <u><a href=3D"https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e=
60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiV2hhdCB=
JZiBTbGFjayBXYXMgWW91ciBBSSBDb21tYW5kIENlbnRlciIsInBvc3RfaWQiOjQzNjAsInBvc3=
RfdHlwZSI6InBvc3QiLCJ1cmwiOiJodHRwczovL2J1enoueHl6LyIsInBvc2l0aW9uIjoxOH0=
=3D" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">Buzz</a></u>, which it b=
ills as an =E2=80=9Copen-source collaboration platform where humans and AI =
agents work together in a shared workspace.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p>Buzz conspicuously avoids any mention of Slack=E2=80=94the launch post d=
escribes its interface as one that =E2=80=9Cwill feel familiar to anyone wh=
o=E2=80=99s used a modern team communication tool=E2=80=9D=E2=80=94but the =
similarities are hard to ignore.</p>
<p>=E2=80=9CIt looks like a Slack clone with a different color,=E2=80=9D sa=
ys design engineer <strong>Tyler Nishida</strong>, who bounces between Code=
x, Claude Code, and <u><a href=3D"https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f0=
5e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiV2hhd=
