</div></div>
<p><br></p>
<p>They=E2=80=99re looking for judgment, which is something that you can re=
ally only build through experience. When I was writing those funding profil=
es, I learned how to tell good work from bad. The first 50 that I wrote wer=
e so bad that at one point, a client said I should be taken out back and sh=
ot. With AI in the mix, the bad ones wouldn=E2=80=99t have been bad enough =
to teach me anything.</p>
<p>The other way today=E2=80=99s job market is more intense for entry-level=
 workers is that employers are expecting competence in a technology that wo=
n=E2=80=99t stand still long enough for anyone to completely grasp. Agentic=
 tools are changing functions in months, <u><a href=3D"https://every.to/ema=
ils/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/=
eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiSG93IHRvIFN0YXJ0IGEgQ2FyZWVyIFdoZW4gQUkgSXMgRG9pbmcgWW91ciB=
FbnRyeS1sZXZlbCBKb2IiLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0MjYzLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIj=
oiaHR0cHM6Ly9pbnNpZ2h0cy5zb20ueWFsZS5lZHUvaW5zaWdodHMvdGhlLXJlYWwtam9iLWRlc=
3RydWN0aW9uLWZyb20tYWktaXMtaGl0dGluZy1iZWZvcmUtY2FyZWVycy1jYW4tc3RhcnQiLCJw=
b3NpdGlvbiI6MTN9" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">rather than=
 years</a></u>. There=E2=80=99s no canon to study or senior teammate to app=
rentice under. Everyone in the org chart is figuring it out on the fly, and=
 you=E2=80=99re expected to figure it out with them while learning how to n=
avigate office politics and pay your taxes.</p>
<p>What to do about it?</p>
<h2 id=3D"chase-problems-not-professions">Chase problems, not professions</=
h2>
<p>When you=E2=80=99re a kid and an adult asks what you want to be when you=
 grow up, the answer is always a job title. A firefighter. A doctor. A YouT=
ube creator. We carry that habit of thinking into the years when we start t=
o look for jobs. We pick a title, and we go after it.</p>
<p>The problem is that job titles aren=E2=80=99t as sure a target as they u=
sed to be. The role you=E2=80=99re chasing today might exist <u><a href=3D"=
https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce=
5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiSG93IHRvIFN0YXJ0IGEgQ2FyZWVyIFdoZW4gQUk=
gSXMgRG9pbmcgWW91ciBFbnRyeS1sZXZlbCBKb2IiLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0MjYzLCJwb3N0X3R5cG=
UiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly9ldmVyeS50by93b3JraW5nLW92ZXJ0aW1lL3RoZS0xO=
C1tb250aC1jYXJlZXItaXMtaGVyZSIsInBvc2l0aW9uIjoxNH0=3D" rel=3D"noopener nore=
ferrer" target=3D"_blank">18 months from now</a></u>. </p>
<p>Pick a problem you want to help work on=E2=80=94something happening in t=
he world that you find yourself thinking about, even when nobody is paying =
you to. The role of =E2=80=9Ccontent marketer=E2=80=9D or =E2=80=9Cdata ana=
lyst=E2=80=9D may shrink, split, or even vanish, but the problem behind tho=
se titles=E2=80=94how to get a stranger to pay attention to something they =
didn=E2=80=99t know they cared about, how to make sense of a pile of messy =
numbers=E2=80=94will still be there, and somebody will still be paid to sol=
ve it.</p>
<p>I=E2=80=99ve been bad at taking this advice myself. I spent a decade cha=
sing the title =E2=80=9Ccopywriter=E2=80=9D and then =E2=80=9Ccontent marke=
ter=E2=80=9D across a handful of industries that had nothing in common=E2=
=80=94oncology advertising, personal finance, even, God help me, crypto=E2=
=80=94without asking whether I cared about any of them. I had the high-scho=
ol overachiever=E2=80=99s mindset: You didn=E2=80=99t have to be passionate=
 about the subject to get an A. I=E2=80=99d been getting A=E2=80=99s in cla=
sses I had no feelings about for 16 years. Why would jobs be any different?=
</p>
<p>That strategy doesn=E2=80=99t work as well when AI can do the entry-leve=
l tasks. Your value to whomever hired you is whatever you bring on top of t=
hat=E2=80=94usually a deeper understanding of the problem than the model ha=
s. That kind of understanding is hard to build in a field you don=E2=80=99t=
 care about. </p>
<h2 id=3D"choose-one-discipline-to-protect">Choose one discipline to protec=
t</h2>
<p>Once you=E2=80=99ve picked your problem, pick your craft, whether it=E2=
=80=99s writing, building, researching, designing, strategizing, or operati=
ng. </p>
<p>You=E2=80=99ve probably heard the truism that it takes 10,000 hours to g=
ain mastery of a skill. The actual research is <u><a href=3D"https://every.=
to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e1896=
6e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiSG93IHRvIFN0YXJ0IGEgQ2FyZWVyIFdoZW4gQUkgSXMgRG9pbmcgW=
W91ciBFbnRyeS1sZXZlbCBKb2IiLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0MjYzLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0Iiwi=
dXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly93d3cubmV3eW9ya2VyLmNvbS9zcG9ydHMvc3BvcnRpbmctc2NlbmUvY29=
tcGxleGl0eS1hbmQtdGhlLXRlbi10aG91c2FuZC1ob3VyLXJ1bGUiLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6MTV9" =
rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">more complicated</a></u> than=
 the popularized version, but the underlying idea is right. You don=E2=80=
=99t get any good at anything until you=E2=80=99ve done it many, many times=
=2E </p>
<p>If you want to write for a living, write your own sentences. If you want=
 to be an engineer, write your own code. </p>
<p>Protect this craft from AI at all costs. AI can find resources, explain =
things, quiz you, and point out where your reasoning has gaps. But if you l=
et it write your sentences or do your research, you won=E2=80=99t get the h=
ours of doing things badly that you need in order to do them well. </p>
<p>It=E2=80=99s easy for me to say this when I=E2=80=99m writing this with =
AI open in another tab. Claude wrote the first draft of half the sentences =
in this section. I <u><a href=3D"https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05=
e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiSG93IH=
RvIFN0YXJ0IGEgQ2FyZWVyIFdoZW4gQUkgSXMgRG9pbmcgWW91ciBFbnRyeS1sZXZlbCBKb2IiL=
CJwb3N0X2lkIjo0MjYzLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly9ldmVyeS50=
by93b3JraW5nLW92ZXJ0aW1lL2hvdy10by1rZWVwLXlvdXItd3JpdGluZy13ZWlyZC1pbi10aGU=
tYWdlLW9mLWFpIiwicG9zaXRpb24iOjE2fQ=3D=3D" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" targ=
et=3D"_blank">rewrote them</a></u>. That rewriting is what the discipline i=
s for=E2=80=94noticing when something doesn=E2=80=99t pass muster. The reas=
on I can do that is that I=E2=80=99ve been writing sentences for 10 years. =
</p>
<p>I know all too well how tempting cutting corners gets when the shortcut =
is right there in another tab. Don=E2=80=99t take it, and in five years you=
=E2=80=99ll be running circles around the people who did. </p>
<h2 id=3D"make-things-before-anyone-asks-you-to">Make things before anyone =
asks you to </h2>
<p>When I was first applying to jobs out of college, my resume said almost =
nothing about what I could do in the =E2=80=9Creal world,=E2=80=9D unless t=
he employer happened to be looking for someone with an undergraduate=E2=80=
=99s grasp of the themes of <em>Wuthering Heights</em>. </p>
<p>A thin resume is less of a disadvantage than it used to be, particularly=
 since employers are increasingly shifting to <u><a href=3D"https://every.t=
o/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966=
e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiSG93IHRvIFN0YXJ0IGEgQ2FyZWVyIFdoZW4gQUkgSXMgRG9pbmcgWW=
91ciBFbnRyeS1sZXZlbCBKb2IiLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0MjYzLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0Iiwid=
XJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly93d3cubmFjZXdlYi5vcmcvam9iLW1hcmtldC90cmVuZHMtYW5kLXByZWRp=
Y3Rpb25zL3doYXQtc3R1ZGVudHMtbmVlZC10by1rbm93LWFib3V0LXRoZS1za2lsbHMtYmFzZWQ=
taGlyaW5nLXByb2Nlc3MiLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6MTd9" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" targ=
et=3D"_blank">skills-based hiring</a></u>=E2=80=94screening candidates by w=
hat they can do rather than where they=E2=80=99ve been. </p>
<p>What you need to do in that environment is make something, and that can =
be anything=E2=80=94<u><a href=3D"https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f0=
5e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiSG93I=
HRvIFN0YXJ0IGEgQ2FyZWVyIFdoZW4gQUkgSXMgRG9pbmcgWW91ciBFbnRyeS1sZXZlbCBKb2Ii=
LCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0MjYzLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly9ldmVyeS5=
0by9wL3doYXQtY29tZXMtYWZ0ZXItbGlua2VkaW4iLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6MTh9" rel=3D"noope=
ner noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">a small tool you wished existed</a></u>, =
a piece of writing on a question nobody is paying you to think about. Pick =
the thing you=E2=80=99d want to use yourself, and make it.</p>
<p>Once your work gets you in the door, the conversation that follows is go=
ing to be about how you made it. What you used AI for, and where you decide=
d not to=E2=80=94the moments where you looked at the model=E2=80=99s first =
answer and thought, =E2=80=9CNo, that=E2=80=99s not right.=E2=80=9D Being a=
ble to walk someone through those decisions is the second skill you=E2=80=
=99re building, alongside the work itself. That=E2=80=99s the judgement tha=
t I mentioned before.</p>
<h2 id=3D"build-the-career-coach-you-wish-you-had">Build the career coach y=
ou wish you had</h2>
<p>The last time I was job hunting, I built a <u><a href=3D"https://every.t=
o/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966=
e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiSG93IHRvIFN0YXJ0IGEgQ2FyZWVyIFdoZW4gQUkgSXMgRG9pbmcgWW=
91ciBFbnRyeS1sZXZlbCBKb2IiLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0MjYzLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0Iiwid=
XJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly9ldmVyeS50by93b3JraW5nLW92ZXJ0aW1lL2ktaGlyZWQtY2hhdGdwdC1h=
cy1teS1jYXJlZXItY29hY2giLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6MTl9" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" t=
arget=3D"_blank">career coach in ChatGPT</a></u> and used it to land the jo=
b I have now. It was a project with my resume, a few examples of writing I =
was proud of, and a long prompt telling the model how to talk to me. I chec=
ked in with it most weekdays for about a month. What it did, more than anyt=
hing, was give me somewhere to put my thinking. Instead of running the same=
 anxious loop in my head, I could lay the question out and have the model s=
uggest specific next steps, like a writing sample worth developing, or ques=
tions I could ask on that networking call that it encouraged me to seek out=
=2E By the end of that month, I had a job. </p>
<p>If I could hop in a time machine and travel back to talk to my 22-year-o=
ld self, I=E2=80=99d suggest that she make one too. It=E2=80=99s not even t=
hat hard: </p>
<ol>
<li>
<strong>Pick a tool.</strong> ChatGPT and Claude both have a project featur=
e that holds context, files, and conversation history across sessions. Eith=
er works. Free tiers are good enough to start. </li>
<li>
<strong>Create a project and give it a name.</strong> =E2=80=9CApprenticesh=
ip Coach,=E2=80=9D =E2=80=9CCareer Stuff,=E2=80=9D your friend=E2=80=99s ni=
ckname for you. </li>
<li>
<strong>Load it with context.</strong> Add examples of work you=E2=80=99re =
proud of and examples you wish were better=E2=80=94the model needs to see w=
hat you=E2=80=99re aiming at and where you=E2=80=99re starting from. Paste =
in a few job postings for roles you=E2=80=99d want, even if they might be t=
oo senior for you. Write a paragraph on the problem you care about and why.=
 </li>
<li>
<strong>Tell it how to behave.</strong> In your instructions, describe to t=
he model how you want it to deliver feedback. If you want a tough critic, s=
ay so. If you=E2=80=99re prone to self-doubt, give it more of a cheerleader=
 vibe. One thing to look out for: Models are infamous for sycophancy=E2=80=
=94telling you what you want to hear=E2=80=94so guard against that in your =
instructions, and even then, maintain a healthy skepticism of the outputs. =
It=E2=80=99s good practice for when you=E2=80=99re asked to work with AI in=
 the workplace. </li>
</ol>
<p>Here=E2=80=99s a starting template. Fill in the bracketed sections, adap=
t the feedback line to match your preference, and add it to the custom inst=
ructions in your project:</p>
<div style=3D"margin: 20px 0; border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: 8px=
; overflow: hidden; background: #f9fafb;">
<div style=3D"padding: 8px 14px; background: #f3f4f6; border-bottom: 1px so=
lid #e5e7eb; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Ro=
boto, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; color: #4b5563;">
<strong style=3D"color: #111827; font-weight: 600;">Career coach prompt</st=
rong><span style=3D"margin-left: 10px; font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Re=
gular, Menlo, monospace; font-size: 12px; color: #6b7280;">JavaScript</span=
>
</div>
<pre style=3D"margin: 0; padding: 14px 16px; font-family: ui-monospace, SFM=
ono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.5;=
 color: #111827; white-space: pre; overflow-x: auto; background: #f9fafb;">=
</pre>
</div>
<p>I want you to act as my career coach. My goal is to use AI to get feedba=
ck, build judgment, and create visible proof of skill, while still doing th=
e central work myself.</p>
<p>Here is my context:</p>
<ul>
<li>Problem I care about: [Examples: climate, education, public policy, med=
ia, health care, local business, creator economy]</li>
<li>The kind of work that addresses it: [Examples: writing, building softwa=
re, running operations, teaching, designing, researching]</li>
<li>My background: [College major, jobs or internships, projects, communiti=
es, life experience]</li>
<li>Skills I=E2=80=99m most confident in: [List 3-5]</li>
<li>Skills I=E2=80=99m least confident in: [List 3-5]</li>
<li>My current technical fluency: [Beginner/comfortable with common AI tool=
s/can code a little/technical but not expert/highly technical]</li>
<li>The core practice I want to develop: [The specific thing the work above=
 requires=E2=80=94writing sentences, writing code, reading sources, designi=
ng experiments, etc.]</li>
<li>The parts of that practice I want to keep doing manually: [The reps I w=
ant to protect from automation, and why]</li>
<li>How I want you to deliver feedback: [Warm and encouraging/rigorous and =
direct/strategic and pragmatic/<u><a href=3D"https://every.to/emails/click/=
7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZW=
N0IjoiSG93IHRvIFN0YXJ0IGEgQ2FyZWVyIFdoZW4gQUkgSXMgRG9pbmcgWW91ciBFbnRyeS1sZ=
XZlbCBKb2IiLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0MjYzLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6=
Ly9ldmVyeS50by9wL3NvY3JhdGVzLWFzLWEtc2VydmljZSIsInBvc2l0aW9uIjoyMH0=3D" rel=
=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">Socratic</a></u> and question-le=
d/blunt but constructive]</li>
</ul>
<p>Important: Be honest. Push back when my plan is vague, my reasoning is t=
hin, or my project doesn=E2=80=99t teach me the practice I said I want. Ask=
 me a clarifying question rather than guessing.</p>
<p>Design an apprenticeship plan that includes:</p>
<ol>
<li>The tasks I should practice manually (the things I shouldn=E2=80=99t ou=
tsource yet)</li>
<li>How I should use AI as a coach, critic, tutor, and research assistant</=
li>
<li>Readings, people to follow, tools to try, and projects to build</li>
<li>Feedback loops I can use to improve</li>
<li>Portfolio artifacts or public outputs I should create</li>
<li>Mistakes and shortcuts I should watch for</li>
</ol>
<p>After giving me the plan, narrow it down: What is one concrete thing I c=
an do this week to move toward this goal?</p>
<h2 id=3D"the-beginners-advantage">The beginner=E2=80=99s advantage </h2>
<p>When I was an undergraduate, my strategy for dealing with the uncertaint=
y of what came next was to pretend it wasn=E2=80=99t happening. I paid for =
that in the form of angst and existential dread. So if I could give one pie=
ce of advice to the class of 2026, it would be this: Don=E2=80=99t wait. AI=
 is reshaping the workforce in real time, and no amount of pretending other=
wise will slow it down.</p>
<p>I=E2=80=99d love to tell you that the senior people in your field are go=
ing to wake up tomorrow and remember that someone once trained them, too. T=
hat employers will realize, en masse, that the entry-level folks they don=
=E2=80=99t hire today are the senior-level folks they won=E2=80=99t have 10=
 years out. But the market doesn=E2=80=99t reorganize itself around what yo=
u wish it would do, and you don=E2=80=99t get a career by waiting for it to=
=2E</p>
<p>The things AI rewards happen to be the things young people have in surpl=
us, like curiosity, willingness to ask why something is done a certain way,=
 and a little bit of idealism about what work could look like if you weren=
=E2=80=99t bound by the =E2=80=9Cbest practices=E2=80=9D of a time before C=
hatGPT was a glimmer in <strong>Sam Altman</strong>=E2=80=99s eye. </p>
<p>I don=E2=80=99t know exactly what work is going to look like by the time=
 you=E2=80=99re my age. Nobody does. But if I had to bet on anyone, it=E2=
=80=99d be the people who are curious about what=E2=80=99s possible. That=
=E2=80=99s most of you, whether you know it yet or not.</p>
