WHAT IS THESIS?

Thesis is a one-day gathering for the people inventing the future of work =
with AI.

We=E2=80=99re bringing together leaders from frontier AI labs, =
builders creating new tools and ways of working, and operators applying AI =
inside companies across industries. We=E2=80=99ll ask everyone to call =
their shot: Tell us what great human work looks like after automation.

It will be a conference filled with people who can see the future because =
they=E2=80=99re already living in it.


WHO WILL BE THERE

Our first speakers include:

 * Ivan Zhao=E2=80=94founder and CEO, Notion
 * Andrew Ambrosino=E2=80=94member of technical staff, Codex, OpenAI
 * Cat de Jong=E2=80=94head of applied AI, Anthropic
 * Nick Thompson=E2=80=94CEO, the Atlantic
 * Josh Miller=E2=80=94CEO and =
cofounder, The Browser Company
 * Cristobal Valenzuela=E2=80=94co-CEO and =
cofounder, Runway
 * Lauren Reeder=E2=80=94partner, Sequoia
 * Sahil Lavingia=E2=80=94founder, Gumroad
 * Natalie =
Fratto=E2=80=94founder and creator, Charts & Crafts
 * Allie Garfinkle=E2=80=94senior writer and editor, Fortune
 * Kane Kallaway=E2=80=94founder, Wavy Labs
 * Nat Eliason=E2=80=94head of =
Founders School, Alpha School
 * Riley Brown=E2=80=94cofounder, Vibecode
 * Kate Lee=E2=80=94editor in chief, Every
 * Katie Parrott=E2=80=94staff =
writer, Every
 * Kieran Klaassen=E2=80=94general manager of Cora, Every

We=E2=80=99ll announce more speakers soon.

The day will feature talks, =
demonstrations, working sessions, office hours, and small-group =
conversations. You=E2=80=99ll see how people are actually working with =
AI=E2=80=94not just what they think might happen next.

And, of course, you can bring your agent.


WHY NEW YORK

New York is where the AI wave hits the beach: It=E2=80=99s where new model =
capabilities meet real-world work. Because of this, it=E2=80=99s the best =
place in the world to see what happens when frontier technology leaves the =
lab and enters everyday life.

That=E2=80=99s why we=E2=80=99re holding =
Thesis at Pioneer Works, a cultural center in Red Hook dedicated to =
blending art, science, music, and technology.

It=E2=80=99s the perfect =
setting for an intimate, cross-disciplinary gathering.


JOIN US

Thesis is happening on Thursday, November 5, 2026.

Space is limited. If you are building with AI, applying it inside an =
organization, or trying to understand what great human work becomes when =
intelligence is abundant, we want you there.

Human work has a bright =
future after automation. If you believe that, you should join us at Thesis.

