<h2 id=3D"what-is-thesis"><strong>What is Thesis?</strong></h2>
<p>Thesis is a one-day gathering for the people inventing the future of wor=
k with AI.</p>
<p>We=E2=80=99re bringing together leaders from frontier AI labs, builders =
creating new tools and ways of working, and operators applying AI inside co=
mpanies across industries. We=E2=80=99ll ask everyone to call their shot: T=
ell us what great human work looks like after automation.</p>
<p>It will be a conference filled with people who can see the future becaus=
e they=E2=80=99re already living in it.</p>
<h2 id=3D"who-will-be-there"><strong>Who will be there</strong></h2>
<p>Our first speakers include:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<strong>Ivan Zhao</strong>=E2=80=94founder and CEO, Notion</li>
<li>
<strong>Andrew Ambrosino</strong>=E2=80=94member of technical staff, Codex,=
 OpenAI</li>
<li>
<strong>Cat de Jong</strong>=E2=80=94head of applied AI, Anthropic</li>
<li>
<strong>Nick Thompson</strong>=E2=80=94CEO, the <em>Atlantic</em>
</li>
<li>
<strong>Josh Miller</strong>=E2=80=94CEO and cofounder, The Browser Company=
</li>
<li>
<strong>Cristobal Valenzuela</strong>=E2=80=94co-CEO and cofounder, Runway<=
/li>
<li>
<strong>Lauren Reeder</strong>=E2=80=94partner, Sequoia </li>
<li>
<strong>Sahil Lavingia</strong>=E2=80=94founder, Gumroad</li>
<li>
<strong>Natalie Fratto</strong>=E2=80=94founder and creator, Charts &amp; C=
rafts</li>
<li>
<strong>Allie Garfinkle</strong>=E2=80=94senior writer and editor, Fortune<=
/li>
<li>
<strong>Kane Kallaway</strong>=E2=80=94founder, Wavy Labs</li>
<li>
<strong>Nat Eliason</strong>=E2=80=94head of Founders School, Alpha School<=
/li>
<li>
<strong>Riley Brown</strong>=E2=80=94cofounder, Vibecode</li>
<li>
<strong>Kate Lee</strong>=E2=80=94editor in chief, Every</li>
<li>
<strong>Katie Parrott</strong>=E2=80=94staff writer, Every</li>
<li>
<strong>Kieran Klaassen</strong>=E2=80=94general manager of Cora, Every</li=
>
</ul>
<p>We=E2=80=99ll announce more speakers soon.</p>
<p>The day will feature talks, demonstrations, working sessions, office hou=
rs, and small-group conversations. You=E2=80=99ll see how people are actual=
ly working with AI=E2=80=94not just what they think might happen next.</p>
<p>And, of course, you can bring your agent.</p>
<h2 id=3D"why-new-york"><strong>Why New York</strong></h2>
<p>New York is where the AI wave hits the beach: It=E2=80=99s where new mod=
el capabilities meet real-world work. Because of this, it=E2=80=99s the bes=
t place in the world to see what happens when frontier technology leaves th=
e lab and enters everyday life.</p>
<p>That=E2=80=99s why we=E2=80=99re holding Thesis at Pioneer Works, a cult=
ural center in Red Hook dedicated to blending art, science, music, and tech=
nology.</p>
<p>It=E2=80=99s the perfect setting for an intimate, cross-disciplinary gat=
hering.</p>
<h2 id=3D"join-us"><strong>Join us</strong></h2>
<p>Thesis is happening on Thursday, November 5, 2026.</p>
<p>Space is limited. If you are building with AI, applying it inside an org=
anization, or trying to understand what great human work becomes when intel=
ligence is abundant, we want you there.</p>
<p>Human work has a bright future after automation. If you believe that, yo=
u should join us at Thesis.</p>
