<p>A second- and third-order consequence of this new landscape is that even=
 U.S. biotech firms may start asking whether it makes sense to take their d=
rugs to China first, at least to complete phase 1 and phase 2 trials. </p>
<p>For now, any drug seeking approval in the U.S. still needs evidence that=
 regulators believe applies to American patients=E2=80=94and in many cases =
that means later-stage global or Western trials. But it may be inevitable t=
hat a Chinese biotech develops a China-originated drug that was licensed in=
to the west without such a step.  </p>
<p>If this change happens=E2=80=94and many believe it will=E2=80=94the next=
