As a consultant, I spend a lot=
 of time in PowerPoint. Data doesn=E2=80=99t drive decisions, narrative =
does, and, love it or hate it, a slide deck presented on a glowing screen =
is the closest thing we have to our ancestors gathering around a campfire =
to tell stories.

The slides I made early in my career were ugly on purpose=
 to show that my ideas were good enough=E2=80=94I didn=E2=80=99t need fancy=
 formatting to convince. But if you won=E2=80=99t last long with that =
attitude in finance or consulting.

Clients see any lack of attention to =
detail as a sign that you can=E2=80=99t be trusted. Analysts pull =
all-nighters making slides pixel-perfect because they could get fired for =
using the wrong font or logo. Natalia Quintero https://every.=
to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e1896=
6e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiQUkgQ291bGQgRG8gQW55dGhpbmcuIFRoZW4gSXQgTWV0IFBvd2VyU=
G9pbnQuIiwicG9zdF9pZCI6NDMyMywicG9zdF90eXBlIjoicG9zdCIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8v=
ZXZlcnkudG8vQG5hdGFsaWFfMjk0NCIsInBvc2l0aW9uIjo2fQ=3D=3D, who leads the =
consulting practice at Every, learned this the hard way just weeks into her=
 first job, when a company=E2=80=99s executive rejected the presentation =
her team was making over colors that didn=E2=80=99t match. If the colors =
were sloppy, he reasoned, the numbers were too.

We=E2=80=99re no Goldman =
Sachs or McKinsey, but at Every, we still have to communicate competency in=
 our presentations. At the same time, we wouldn=E2=80=99t be a very =
credible AI enablement partner if we weren=E2=80=99t using AI to help us. =
The challenge is that AI-created decks often don=E2=80=99t tell a strong =
story https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce6=
87adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiQUkgQ291bGQgRG8gQW55dGhpbmcuIFRoZ=
W4gSXQgTWV0IFBvd2VyUG9pbnQuIiwicG9zdF9pZCI6NDMyMywicG9zdF90eXBlIjoicG9zdCIs=
InVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8veC5jb20vYmVhcmx5YWkvc3RhdHVzLzIwNDU5MDEyODQ1NTgxNjAzNDM=
vcGhvdG8vMSIsInBvc2l0aW9uIjo3fQ=3D=3D=E2=80=94and that lack of narrative =
cohesion communicates the same thing as sloppy design: You didn=E2=80=99t =
care enough to pay attention to detail.

What follows is the story of our =
attempt to create the perfect PowerPoint with AI. We started with =
Claude=E2=80=99s and Codex=E2=80=99s PowerPoint skills, but neither could =
automate the process to the level of quality we needed. So we built our own=
. If you=E2=80=99re creating enough presentations=E2=80=94or your quality =
bar is similarly high=E2=80=94it may be worth following the same path.


CLAUDE GETS CLOSE, BUT CAN=E2=80=99T CLOSE EVERY DEAL

When I joined Every in February, our consulting team was still making all =
our slides manually in Figma=E2=80=94about two to three decks per week. The=
 first thing I tried was asking Claude Code to create PowerPoint slides for=
 an upcoming presentation.

It didn=E2=80=99t go well:

