To make Claude work at all with PowerPoint, Anthropic had to invest =
a lot into creating its official pptx skill https://every.=
to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e1896=
6e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiQUkgQ291bGQgRG8gQW55dGhpbmcuIFRoZW4gSXQgTWV0IFBvd2VyU=
G9pbnQuIiwicG9zdF9pZCI6NDMyMywicG9zdF90eXBlIjoicG9zdCIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8v=
Z2l0aHViLmNvbS9hbnRocm9waWNzL3NraWxscy9ibG9iL21haW4vc2tpbGxzL3BwdHgvU0tJTEw=
ubWQiLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6OX0=3D. A single markdown file doesn=E2=80=99t cut it.=
 Its skill has 59 different files in the folder, 16 of them Python scripts =
for interacting with PowerPoint. The skill.md file itself is over 4,000 =
words, and there are an additional 3,000 words in reference files.

Claude is surprisingly good at building slides from scratch=E2=80=94not =
because it knows PowerPoint, but because a slide is fundamentally a layout =
problem. Arranging text blocks, images, and shapes on a page is the same =
thing HTML was built to do, and Claude writes HTML fluently. So it can lay =
out a polished deck and hand it back ready to present better than any of =
the dedicated AI deck creation tools on the market.

But the minute you use a company template, it goes off the rails. Matching =
an existing design and writing style https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f9545=
