<p><br></p>
<p>To make Claude work at all with PowerPoint, Anthropic had to invest a lo=
t into creating its <u><a href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fever=
y.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefc=
c02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiQUkgQ291bGQgRG8gQW55dGhpbmcuIFRoZW4gSXQgTWV=
0IFBvd2VyUG9pbnQuIiwicG9zdF9pZCI6NDMyMywicG9zdF90eXBlIjoicG9zdCIsInVybCI6Im=
h0dHBzOi8vZ2l0aHViLmNvbS9hbnRocm9waWNzL3NraWxscy9ibG9iL21haW4vc2tpbGxzL3Bwd=
HgvU0tJTEwubWQiLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6OX0=3D/1/0100019f13ec1823-ec827cfd-269d-4c5d=
-854a-491abef87169-000000/qQQOEqnRrzVesOq1S2gkMGkfNAHP5esozTs1CjjBfLE=3D452=
" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">official pptx skill</a></u>=
. A single markdown file doesn=E2=80=99t cut it. Its skill has 59 different=
 files in the folder, 16 of them Python scripts for interacting with PowerP=
oint. The skill.md file itself is over 4,000 words, and there are an additi=
onal 3,000 words in reference files. </p>
<p>Claude is surprisingly good at building slides from scratch=E2=80=94not =
because it knows PowerPoint, but because a slide is fundamentally a layout =
problem. Arranging text blocks, images, and shapes on a page is the same th=
ing HTML was built to do, and Claude writes HTML fluently. So it can lay ou=
t a polished deck and hand it back ready to present better than any of the =
dedicated AI deck creation tools on the market. </p>
<p>But the minute you use a company template, it goes off the rails. Matchi=
ng an existing design and <u><a href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%=
2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce=
5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiQUkgQ291bGQgRG8gQW55dGhpbmcuIFRoZW4gS=
XQgTWV0IFBvd2VyUG9pbnQuIiwicG9zdF9pZCI6NDMyMywicG9zdF90eXBlIjoicG9zdCIsInVy=
bCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vZXZlcnkudG8vZ3VpZGVzL2FpLXN0eWxlLWd1aWRlIiwicG9zaXRpb24iOjE=
wfQ=3D=3D/1/0100019f13ec1823-ec827cfd-269d-4c5d-854a-491abef87169-000000/xJ=
bUHUnqu8RC4tkI1MCcJ9jWOI5P7ZqqLeDM6QeoMdA=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer=
" target=3D"_blank">writing style</a></u> is a hard task for AI because it =
requires spatial awareness, narrative structure, research diligence, design=
 aesthetics, and good taste=E2=80=94all domains where humans still have the=
 edge. For a well-researched presentation, you need to feed Claude a lot of=
 material, and everything you give it counts against its context window, th=
e amount of text it can read in one chat session. Pile in more than 200,000=
 tokens (roughly 150,000 words) and you hit <u><a href=3D"https://icu.every=
.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f4=
54c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiQUkgQ291bGQgRG8gQW5=
5dGhpbmcuIFRoZW4gSXQgTWV0IFBvd2VyUG9pbnQuIiwicG9zdF9pZCI6NDMyMywicG9zdF90eX=
BlIjoicG9zdCIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vd3d3LnRyeWNocm9tYS5jb20vcmVzZWFyY2gvY29ud=
GV4dC1yb3QiLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6MTF9/1/0100019f13ec1823-ec827cfd-269d-4c5d-854a-=
491abef87169-000000/Efyj2mlxrIWVx6Gj37hUArm7E5Dib5DZA7JncRihG8A=3D452" rel=
=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">context rot</a></u>: The model s=
tarts to get confused and make dumb mistakes. Furthermore, Microsoft=E2=80=
=99s .pptx file format was never designed with agents in mind=E2=80=93=E2=
=80=93it=E2=80=99s messy, token-inefficient, and hard to manipulate reliabl=
y. </p>
<p>An AI-generated deck that=E2=80=99s 80 percent right is often worse than=
 one using no AI at all. Reviewing a polished-looking presentation for hidd=
en errors is harder than building the right one yourself, and people <u><a =
href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c=
3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZW=
N0IjoiQUkgQ291bGQgRG8gQW55dGhpbmcuIFRoZW4gSXQgTWV0IFBvd2VyUG9pbnQuIiwicG9zd=
F9pZCI6NDMyMywicG9zdF90eXBlIjoicG9zdCIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vcHVibGlrYXRpb25l=
bi5yZXV0bGluZ2VuLXVuaXZlcnNpdHkuZGUvZnJvbnRkb29yL2RlbGl2ZXIvaW5kZXgvZG9jSWQ=
vNTkyOS9maWxlLzU5MjkucGRmIiwicG9zaXRpb24iOjEyfQ=3D=3D/1/0100019f13ec1823-ec=
827cfd-269d-4c5d-854a-491abef87169-000000/8WwuUHiYOixxU2vJ5F-khC7X11nJunrPL=
0E9W7O_vxc=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">over-trust =
AI outputs</a></u>. In our pursuit of the perfect PowerPoint, we=E2=80=99ve=
 found that automation only becomes genuinely useful when it gets you close=
 to a zero-percent defect rate. Reaching that standard is possible=E2=80=94=
but only after an outrageous amount of work writing, testing, and orchestra=
ting skill.md files.</p>
<p>The Anthropic skill also does a poor job of updating or editing old deck=
s. Because .pptx files are stored as XML and Claude is trained on millions =
of times more HTML than XML, the model struggles to mentally render what it=
=E2=80=99s working on. It can=E2=80=99t reliably predict where text will wr=
ap or images will overlap, so it=E2=80=99s making changes without really se=
eing the slide. </p>
<h2 id=3D"training-a-superagent-on-slides">Training a superagent on slides<=
/h2>
<p>Our senior applied AI engineer <strong><u><a href=3D"https://icu.every.t=
o/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454=
c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiQUkgQ291bGQgRG8gQW55d=
GhpbmcuIFRoZW4gSXQgTWV0IFBvd2VyUG9pbnQuIiwicG9zdF9pZCI6NDMyMywicG9zdF90eXBl=
IjoicG9zdCIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vZXZlcnkudG8vQG5pdHllc2giLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6MTN=
9/1/0100019f13ec1823-ec827cfd-269d-4c5d-854a-491abef87169-000000/f7LiiDgW8r=
Hk656W-gVNkBpMxivBDuItr5hMA7T_WSU=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=
=3D"_blank">Nityesh Agarwal</a></u></strong> took it upon himself to solve =
the PowerPoint problem. He adapted the Anthropic PowerPoint skill by adding=
 several key features and incorporating it into our AI assistant, <u><a hre=
f=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f9=
5455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0I=
joiQUkgQ291bGQgRG8gQW55dGhpbmcuIFRoZW4gSXQgTWV0IFBvd2VyUG9pbnQuIiwicG9zdF9p=
ZCI6NDMyMywicG9zdF90eXBlIjoicG9zdCIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vZXZlcnkudG8vcC93aGF=
0LWktbGVhcm5lZC1vbmJvYXJkaW5nLW91ci1haS1wcm9qZWN0LW1hbmFnZXIiLCJwb3NpdGlvbi=
I6MTR9/1/0100019f13ec1823-ec827cfd-269d-4c5d-854a-491abef87169-000000/aEVu7=
Umt6KADBIxmSylavn3raf-L-V2nLbgnN13lY3I=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" t=
arget=3D"_blank">Claudie</a></u>. </p>
<p>The biggest improvement came from adopting a blueprint-first approach. I=
nstead of immediately generating a final deck, Claudie would first create a=
 plan for what slides were needed and write detailed visual direction notes=
 for each one. It drew on two inputs: an agenda built from Granola client-c=
all notes, and a table of contents laying out the main narrative points for=
 the session. Then Claudie would wait for my approval in Slack before proce=
eding. This human-in-the-loop process saved us at several points and helped=
 avoid wasting a lot of tokens on decks that would have been too shallow to=
 present. Because the agenda input detailed the order of events and bullet =
points on each topic, it rarely missed a slide. </p>
<p>At the time, slide preparation was about 80 percent of my work, and I wa=
s traveling around the country to do three or four workshops for our client=
s about AI adoption and implementation a week. I couldn=E2=80=99t make deck=
s without AI because I had no time to do it all manually. With Claudie and =
her new PowerPoint skill, I could hop on a plane and have the slides done f=
or me by the time I arrived=E2=80=94Claudie, who runs on a Mac Mini in our =
New York office, could be working even if I was offline. After checking int=
o my hotel, I could make manual edits and be ready to present the next day.=
 We also built skills for Claudie to synthesize call notes into an agenda f=
or each workshop, draft proposals for new engagements, and build the exerci=
ses for participants to work through on the day. </p>
<p>To create images that aligned with Every=E2=80=99s <u><a href=3D"https:/=
/icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f8=
7698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiQUkgQ291b=
GQgRG8gQW55dGhpbmcuIFRoZW4gSXQgTWV0IFBvd2VyUG9pbnQuIiwicG9zdF9pZCI6NDMyMywi=
cG9zdF90eXBlIjoicG9zdCIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vZXZlcnkudG8vcG9kY2FzdC9hbi1pbnN=
pZGUtbG9vay1hdC1ldmVyeS1zLWRlc2lnbi1waGlsb3NvcGh5IiwicG9zaXRpb24iOjE1fQ=3D=
=3D/1/0100019f13ec1823-ec827cfd-269d-4c5d-854a-491abef87169-000000/wzp3DBsB=
RNh0ZgA2ArZjpVL1-b0tyAu_vx4kOmSLTxY=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" targ=
et=3D"_blank">Greco-Roman-pop-art brand</a></u>, we gave Claudie an image-g=
eneration skill powered by GPT Image 2 and wired it into our slide-creation=
