<h2 id=3D"the-world-we-were-trained-for">The world we were trained for</h2>
<p>School rewarded execution. You were graded on the essays you wrote and t=
he projects you turned in on time. Careers rewarded it the same way. Perfor=
mance reviews measured output, and promotions often went to those who produ=
ced the most, the fastest, at the highest quality.</p>
<p>At first, AI seems like a boon to someone who grew up this way. If I=E2=
=80=99m doing X, then I should be able to do it much better, and much faste=
r, with AI augmenting me. This leads you to chase every new tool and techni=
que, because even incremental improvements are still improvements.</p>
<p>But the next thing is just around the corner. Fine-tuning an AI model us=
ing smaller, specialized data sets was =E2=80=9Cthe thing=E2=80=9D for mayb=
e eight months before <u><a href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fev=
