<h2 id=3D"steal-this-workflow">Steal this workflow</h2>
<h3 id=3D"run-your-x-posts-past-grok-before-you-post">Run your X posts past=
 Grok before you post</h3>
<p>xAI <u><a href=3D"https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e65=
4f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiSW5zaWRlIHRoZSAxMD=
AtYWdlbnQgU29mdHdhcmUgRmFjdG9yeSIsInBvc3RfaWQiOjQyNjYsInBvc3RfdHlwZSI6InBvc=
3QiLCJ1cmwiOiJodHRwczovL2dpdGh1Yi5jb20veGFpLW9yZy94LWFsZ29yaXRobSIsInBvc2l0=
aW9uIjoxN30=3D" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">open-sourced =
its ranking algorithm</a></u> last week, which shows the factors X consider=
s when deciding which posts to surface in users=E2=80=99 For You feed. It i=
ncludes a Grok-powered =E2=80=9Cbanger classifier=E2=80=9D that decides whe=
ther your post gets better distribution by scoring every post on quality an=
d slop. So why not run the same check on yourself before you hit publish?</=
p>
<ol>
<li>
<strong>Paste your draft into Grok with X=E2=80=99s scoring prompt.</strong=
> Ask Grok to return four things: quality_score, slop_score, isHighQuality =
(a true-or-false verdict on whether a post clears the quality bar), and top=
ic tags. The classifier reads text, image, and video. Use this prompt: =E2=
=80=9CScore this X post the way the xai-org/x-algorithm banger classifier w=
ould: return quality_score (0=E2=80=931), slop_score (1=E2=80=933), isHighQ=
uality boolean, and topic tags.=E2=80=9D </li>
<li>
<strong>Rewrite anything that scores below 0.4 on quality (which can receiv=
e a score of between zero and one) or above one on slop (which is rated bet=
ween one and three). </strong>Posts that users scroll past quickly or repor=
t get penalized, while posts that drive replies and dwell time get rewarded=
=2E To move the score, lead with a stop=
-the-scroll first line, name a specifi=
c experience, event, or number, and cut anything readers would skim. As soo=
n as a user scrolls past, the algorithm ranks the post as =E2=80=9Cnot_dwel=
led=E2=80=9D and it gets pushed down the recommendation pile.</li>
<li>
<strong>Limit yourself to two to three posts a day.</strong> The algorithm =
heavily discounts your fourth post and your eighth to near zero in the rank=
ing system. It=E2=80=99s better to invest in fewer, scroll-stopping, engage=
ment-generating posts than many forgettable ones.</li>
</ol>
