WHY NOT JUST PROMPT?

Graphical interfaces were built to replace cumbersome command-line syntax =
with direct, visible, reversible manipulation https://every.=
to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e1896=
6e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiRGVzaWduaW5nIFdpdGggQUk_IE1ha2UgYSBKaWcuIiwicG9zdF9pZ=
CI6NDQwMiwicG9zdF90eXBlIjoicG9zdCIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vd3d3LmNzLnVtZC5lZHUv=
dXNlcnMvYmVuL3BhcGVycy9TaG5laWRlcm1hbjE5ODNEaXJlY3QucGRmIiwicG9zaXRpb24iOjI=
1fQ=3D=3D of the thing at hand. Designers are relearning the lesson with =
chat interfaces, discovering that prompting is too coarse a method of =
adjustment compared with what they=E2=80=99re used to.

But that doesn=E2=80=99t mean simply replicating, whole cloth, the =
interfaces of existing design apps like Figma. =E2=80=9CThese tools have =
been around for a while and have become of a certain shape because of the =
technology that we have accessible to us,=E2=80=9D says designer Amelia =
Wattenberger https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c61=
9eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiRGVzaWduaW5nIFdpdGggQUk_IE=
1ha2UgYSBKaWcuIiwicG9zdF9pZCI6NDQwMiwicG9zdF90eXBlIjoicG9zdCIsInVybCI6Imh0d=
HBzOi8vd2F0dGVuYmVyZ2VyLmNvbS8iLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6MjZ9, a partner at Shutter =
Hill Ventures and former principal research engineer at GitHub Next. =
=E2=80=9C[Now] we=E2=80=99re working with different material, and we =
don=E2=80=99t yet have tools that make us feel like we=E2=80=99re in =
control of them because we=E2=80=99re still figuring out our relationship =
to them.=E2=80=9D

Wattenberger imagines agents creating https://every.=
to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e1896=
6e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiRGVzaWduaW5nIFdpdGggQUk_IE1ha2UgYSBKaWcuIiwicG9zdF9pZ=
CI6NDQwMiwicG9zdF90eXBlIjoicG9zdCIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vd2F0dGVuYmVyZ2VyLmNv=
bS90aG91Z2h0cy9jb2RlLWlzLWEtbWVkaXVtLWZvci10aG91Z2h0LyIsInBvc2l0aW9uIjoyN30=
=3D a custom whiteboard or playground as soon as you start working, =
complete with panels for any attributes you might want to adjust. Jigs like=
 these could bring back aspects from pre-AI workflows to our current ways =
of designing, like the kinds of immediate feedback that allow for iteration=
 and exploration. =E2=80=9CWhen you use a pencil to sketch, it=E2=80=99s =
this symbiotic thing where you sketch and you=E2=80=99re looking at it and =
you=E2=80=99re reacting to what it looks like after you=E2=80=99ve sketched=
 it,=E2=80=9D she told me. =E2=80=9CIf you sit there and only think about =
[what you=E2=80=99re making], you=E2=80=99re only going to get so far.=
=E2=80=9D

Until these jigs start appearing automatically, though, =
designers everywhere will just have to prompt their own.



