000000/kCw9XNUZXcDgQMcFyQYQJ4W9U8w8PvkDCiy0ZfGIj7I=3D452" rel=3D"noopener n=
oreferrer" target=3D"_blank">Every Consulting</a></u> client; we delivered =
its leadership team a paid executive AI workshop. Headway was given an oppo=
rtunity to fact-check details but had no editorial control over this articl=
e.</em></p>
<p><em>Was this newsletter forwarded to you? <u><a href=3D"https://icu.ever=
y.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f=
454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiVGhlIEhlYWx0aGNhcm=
UgQ29tcGFueSBUaGF0IEJ1aWx0IHRoZSBBSSBUb29sIEl0IENvdWxkbuKAmXQgQnV5IiwicG9zd=
F9pZCI6NDQ0NywicG9zdF90eXBlIjoicG9zdCIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vZXZlcnkudG8vYWNj=
b3VudCIsInBvc2l0aW9uIjo1fQ=3D=3D/1/010001a025c4fe05-11ae7e7d-26ac-47ad-8421=
-e4639cdcee54-000000/ukLf0fEHG9ijxVYJlSo0k71HjhbiW_mMU-mkqBVLzqY=3D452" rel=
=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">Sign up</a></u> to get it in you=
r inbox.</em></p>
<p></p>
<hr class=3D"quill-line">
<p></p>
<p>At mental healthcare company <u><a href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/http=
s:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce6=
87adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiVGhlIEhlYWx0aGNhcmUgQ29tcGFueSB=
UaGF0IEJ1aWx0IHRoZSBBSSBUb29sIEl0IENvdWxkbuKAmXQgQnV5IiwicG9zdF9pZCI6NDQ0Ny=
wicG9zdF90eXBlIjoicG9zdCIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vaGVhZHdheS5jby8iLCJwb3NpdGlvb=
iI6Nn0=3D/1/010001a025c4fe05-11ae7e7d-26ac-47ad-8421-e4639cdcee54-000000/cE=
EvV9l7vGn_4KUH740syuejgb0HTCcp4R1k-Lh06Cs=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer=
" target=3D"_blank">Headway</a></u>, an AI agent can act without asking per=
mission at every step. That might sound unexpected for a 900-person company=
 in an industry governed by strict rules for sensitive patient information.=
 But the autonomy is possible because of Headway=E2=80=99s tight controls a=
round the agent. Every conversation runs inside a sealed, disposable contai=
ner, with carefully limited connections to company tools and data.</p>
<p>That architecture underpins Eddy, the internal AI assistant Headway buil=
t when existing products couldn=E2=80=99t meet its particular combination o=
f security, compliance, and workflow requirements. Eddy is built on the <u>=
<a href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2=
F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJ=
qZWN0IjoiVGhlIEhlYWx0aGNhcmUgQ29tcGFueSBUaGF0IEJ1aWx0IHRoZSBBSSBUb29sIEl0IE=
NvdWxkbuKAmXQgQnV5IiwicG9zdF9pZCI6NDQ0NywicG9zdF90eXBlIjoicG9zdCIsInVybCI6I=
mh0dHBzOi8vY29kZS5jbGF1ZGUuY29tL2RvY3MvZW4vYWdlbnQtc2RrL292ZXJ2aWV3IiwicG9z=
aXRpb24iOjd9/1/010001a025c4fe05-11ae7e7d-26ac-47ad-8421-e4639cdcee54-000000=
/_xF9AKmX2iqSVlm2R1EsFhvNycT3uTreGbT9HWSdVBc=3D452" rel=3D"noopener norefer=
rer" target=3D"_blank">Claude Code SDK</a></u>, Anthropic=E2=80=99s toolkit=
 for teams developing products with Claude Code. It=E2=80=99s hosted in Hea=
dway=E2=80=99s Amazon Web Services environment and connected to the company=
=E2=80=99s tools and data.</p>
<p>Work on Eddy had barely begun six months ago. Headway initially wanted a=
n existing product and was preparing to sign a deal with a major AI vendor =
to give employees access to its desktop app. But relying on vendors to deli=
ver features that met Headway=E2=80=99s workflow and strict compliance requ=
irements for handling sensitive patient data =E2=80=9Cfelt like we were mis=
sing the train,=E2=80=9D says chief technology officer <strong>Arnaud Ferre=
ri</strong>.</p>
<p>The team=E2=80=99s decision to build its own solution runs counter to th=
e market trend: A November 2025 survey of 495 U.S. enterprise AI decision-m=
akers found that <u><a href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.t=
o%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02=
e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiVGhlIEhlYWx0aGNhcmUgQ29tcGFueSBUaGF0IEJ1aWx0IH=
RoZSBBSSBUb29sIEl0IENvdWxkbuKAmXQgQnV5IiwicG9zdF9pZCI6NDQ0NywicG9zdF90eXBlI=
joicG9zdCIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vbWVubG92Yy5jb20vcGVyc3BlY3RpdmUvMjAyNS10aGUt=
c3RhdGUtb2YtZ2VuZXJhdGl2ZS1haS1pbi10aGUtZW50ZXJwcmlzZS8iLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6OH0=
=3D/1/010001a025c4fe05-11ae7e7d-26ac-47ad-8421-e4639cdcee54-000000/p5j0Lx9J=
51mHfpCRUlLhxzrg_gi1pYqpDbTX0wVrkVU=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" targ=
et=3D"_blank">76 percent of AI use cases</a></u> were bought rather than bu=
ilt, up from 53 percent a year earlier.</p>
<p>That decision, though, appears to be paying off. Ferreri says that today=
, the whole company uses Eddy weekly=E2=80=94650 of those 900 employees dai=
ly=E2=80=94whether they=E2=80=99re in engineering, product, design, data, o=
perations, or clinical. The tool has run roughly 260,000 conversations sinc=
e developers committed its first lines of code on March 2.</p>
<p>General-purpose AI products are increasingly capable, but they often fai=
l to meet an organization=E2=80=99s specific needs=E2=80=94and if a company=
=E2=80=99s compliance rules, data boundaries, and workflows are unusual eno=
ugh, a vendor may not accommodate them soon enough or without unacceptable =
compromises. The challenge is knowing when to stop waiting and build it you=
rself.</p>
<h2 id=3D"balancing-security-with-utility">Balancing security with utility =
</h2>
<p>The task force exploring AI options for Headway didn=E2=80=99t want to p=
ay to train a model or compete with the labs on capabilities. Instead, they=
 proposed building a harness=E2=80=94a <u><a href=3D"https://icu.every.to/C=
L0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c61=
9eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiVGhlIEhlYWx0aGNhcmUgQ29t=
cGFueSBUaGF0IEJ1aWx0IHRoZSBBSSBUb29sIEl0IENvdWxkbuKAmXQgQnV5IiwicG9zdF9pZCI=
6NDQ0NywicG9zdF90eXBlIjoicG9zdCIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vZXZlcnkudG8vc291cmNlLW=
NvZGUvY2xhdWRlLWNvZGUtaXMtdGhlLW9wZW5jbGF3LWFsdGVybmF0aXZlLXlvdS1hbHJlYWR5L=
WhhdmUiLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6OX0=3D/1/010001a025c4fe05-11ae7e7d-26ac-47ad-8421-e4=
639cdcee54-000000/7LZXwVBNQp_V96iixoNuSRDARB5oOb4GChtSAFDHUAo=3D452" rel=3D=
"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">custom wrapper for an existing AI m=
odel</a></u> that controls what it can access and do=E2=80=94with boundarie=
s designed to meet Headway=E2=80=99s security and compliance requirements f=
or handling personally identifiable and protected health information. </p>
<p>Every Eddy conversation runs inside a fresh <u><a href=3D"https://icu.ev=
ery.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e65=
4f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiVGhlIEhlYWx0aGNh=
cmUgQ29tcGFueSBUaGF0IEJ1aWx0IHRoZSBBSSBUb29sIEl0IENvdWxkbuKAmXQgQnV5IiwicG9=
zdF9pZCI6NDQ0NywicG9zdF90eXBlIjoicG9zdCIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vd3d3LmRvY2tlci=
5jb20vIiwicG9zaXRpb24iOjEwfQ=3D=3D/1/010001a025c4fe05-11ae7e7d-26ac-47ad-84=
21-e4639cdcee54-000000/RXhS14B8Xz5qkwR0wnqD1AgKdt-vqjpyr10OJWiRuzY=3D452" r=
el=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">Docker</a></u> container, a se=
aled, disposable workspace isolated from the rest of Headway=E2=80=99s syst=
ems. When a conversation ends, the container is destroyed.</p>
<p>That container is why the compliance team could live with the agent taki=
ng action without asking the user to approve each step. =E2=80=9CClaude Cod=
e can decide to erase the entire hard drive,=E2=80=9D Ferreri says. =E2=80=
=9CIt doesn=E2=80=99t matter. This is a throwaway container of a conversati=
on.=E2=80=9D When an agent pulls sensitive data for analysis, it works from=
 a copy that=E2=80=99s wiped when the job ends: It can only read from Snowf=
lake=E2=80=94the company=E2=80=99s data warehouse=E2=80=94never write; it c=
annot browse the open internet directly, though it can use web search throu=
gh a strict proxy; and it can=E2=80=99t send emails.</p>
<p>The worst-case scenario would be a prompt injection attack, where a bad =
actor hides instructions inside content the AI is asked to read=E2=80=94an =
email, for example=E2=80=94telling it to collect sensitive company data and=
 send it elsewhere. Headway=E2=80=99s egress policy is designed to prevent =
even an agent with access to sensitive internal data from sending it out, F=
erreri says.</p>
<h2 id=3D"how-eddy-escaped-engineering">How Eddy escaped engineering</h2>
<p>Ferreri originally planned to run a 10-person alpha in the first week. B=
y week=E2=80=99s end, 30 or 40 people were knocking down his door to try Ed=
dy. =E2=80=9CI had to hold people off,=E2=80=9D he says. </p>
<p>The features weren=E2=80=99t ready, and sending Eddy into the wild prema=
turely could damage trust. So Ferreri=E2=80=99s team laid the groundwork fo=
r Eddy to spread organically when they opened it to the company=E2=80=94no =
managers forcing employees to use it. Two key product decisions drove adopt=
ion. </p>
<p>First, Headway added connectors that use Model Context Protocol (MCP)=E2=
=80=94an open standard for linking AI applications to external tools and da=
ta=E2=80=94so Eddy could work with software that employees already used. A =
connector for Figma lets an agent read and edit design files; one for Snowf=
lake lets it query the data warehouse.</p>
<p>A product manager can ask Eddy to draft a product requirements document =
and have it pull context from internal Slack threads and Google Drive. A da=
ta scientist can ask for a state-of-the-union dashboard, and Eddy can run S=
nowflake queries, generate <u><a href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F=
%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adc=
e5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiVGhlIEhlYWx0aGNhcmUgQ29tcGFueSBUaGF0=
IEJ1aWx0IHRoZSBBSSBUb29sIEl0IENvdWxkbuKAmXQgQnV5IiwicG9zdF9pZCI6NDQ0NywicG9=
zdF90eXBlIjoicG9zdCIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vZXZlcnkudG8vY29udGV4dC13aW5kb3cvaW=
5zaWRlLXRoZS0xMDAtYWdlbnQtc29mdHdhcmUtZmFjdG9yeSIsInBvc2l0aW9uIjoxMX0=3D/1/=
010001a025c4fe05-11ae7e7d-26ac-47ad-8421-e4639cdcee54-000000/wyizClxB3xG-E_=
3bvdmqV9gf5eXq2EqsJexV7cV6n18=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"=
_blank">an HTML artifact</a></u>, and write the narrative around the number=
s.</p>
<p>Figma and Snowflake MCPs exist for agents like Claude and Codex, but lar=
ger AI vendors can=E2=80=99t sell you the exact combination of custom conne=
ctors, permissions, and clinical access rules that a complex company like H=
eadway needs. Because Headway knows its own data, departments, and risks, i=
t can organize that context into a coherent system that satisfies its legal=
 and compliance teams.</p>
<p>Eddy=E2=80=99s output also drove its spread. Over time, people stopped c=
opying Eddy=E2=80=99s answers into Google Docs for patient billing investig=
ations because its HTML artifacts were richer and easier to share. Then the=
y wanted to comment on them the way they would on a document, so the team a=
dded inline commenting.</p>
<p>Those choices produced a remarkably sticky product for Headway=E2=80=99s=
 built-in audience of roughly 900 coworkers. Headway later set an AI token =
usage goal to encourage adoption. But by then, a majority of the company wa=
s already using Eddy daily. </p>
<h2 id=3D"the-cost-of-ownership">The cost of ownership</h2>
<p>Building Eddy gave Headway the product it couldn=E2=80=99t buy. It also =
left Headway responsible for work a vendor would normally handle: maintaini=
ng uptime, minimizing latency, responding to feature requests, and keeping =
pace with AI=E2=80=99s expanding capabilities. If the first week=E2=80=99s =
problem was holding users off, the problem three months in was keeping Eddy=
 running. </p>
<p>By May, Eddy was experiencing outages about twice a week, and two engine=
ers were working full time on reliability. Ferreri says the system has sinc=
e stabilized, with no major downtime, even as the team continues to ship fi=
ve to 10 features a day.</p>
<p>Startup time remains a problem. Because the system spins up a fresh cont=
ainer each time, a new Eddy conversation takes about 30 seconds to begin. T=
hat=E2=80=99s manageable if the task is =E2=80=9Cgo build this feature=E2=
=80=9D and the agent sets to work for 20 minutes, but frustrating when some=
one wants a quick answer. </p>
<p>Keeping up with new AI capabilities is another challenge. Because Eddy h=
as its own interface, features from outside AI tools don=E2=80=99t automati=
cally become available to Headway. If Cursor releases one, Headway has to d=
ecide whether to tell engineers to use Cursor or wait two weeks and build i=
t into Eddy. So far, building in-house has made the most sense, but every o=
utside innovation forces the team to reconsider whether its internal versio=
n is worth maintaining.</p>
<p>Another welcome problem is demand for more features. Engineering wants b=
etter Git integration, while product managers want richer product requireme=
nts document templates, and clinical teams need special data boundaries. </=
p>
<p>Each request makes sense alone, but Ferreri says, =E2=80=9CI don=E2=80=
=99t want this to become a Christmas tree where every feature comes in, and=
 then it just looks like nothing. Just because you can doesn=E2=80=99t mean=
 you should.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p>So far, Headway has decided to absorb the costs of building and maintain=
ing Eddy. Making the same choice requires staffing the product, owning its =
reliability, choosing between stability and feature requests, and continual=
ly deciding whether to reproduce what outside vendors ship. Headway became =
its own AI vendor, with the maintenance burden to match.</p>
<h2 id=3D"when-to-wait-buy-or-build"><strong>When to wait, buy, or build</s=
trong></h2>
<p>Not every company needs its own Eddy. Building is expensive, ongoing, an=
d easy to get wrong. Most companies shouldn=E2=80=99t build internal AI too=
ls like this, says <a href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to=
%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e=
18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiVGhlIEhlYWx0aGNhcmUgQ29tcGFueSBUaGF0IEJ1aWx0IHR=
oZSBBSSBUb29sIEl0IENvdWxkbuKAmXQgQnV5IiwicG9zdF9pZCI6NDQ0NywicG9zdF90eXBlIj=
oicG9zdCIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vZXZlcnkudG8vQG1pa2VfMjExNCIsInBvc2l0aW9uIjoxM=
n0=3D/1/010001a025c4fe05-11ae7e7d-26ac-47ad-8421-e4639cdcee54-000000/vJebJY=
PtpiG7E1U_f6x4QOINYFdzIUrXlKxRMRGTqFM=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" ta=
rget=3D"_blank">Mike Taylor</a>, head of technology consulting at Every. =
=E2=80=9CIf you can get away with off-the-shelf software, save yourself the=
 maintenance costs and risk of guessing wrong. But if it=E2=80=99s core to =
your strategy to be ahead of the market on AI, sometimes you=E2=80=99ve got=
 to roll up your sleeves and build what=E2=80=99s missing.=E2=80=9D The dec=
ision depends on what the constraint is, how quickly a vendor is likely to =
close the gap, what the company loses while it waits, and whether it is pre=
pared to own what it creates. Headway=E2=80=99s experience suggests a three=
-part framework:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<strong>Wait</strong> when the missing capability is likely to arrive soon =
and the cost of delay is lower than the cost of building and maintaining a =
substitute</li>
<li>
<strong>Buy</strong> when a vendor can meet the company=E2=80=99s security,=
 data, and workflow requirements without forcing it to give up something st=
rategically important</li>
<li>
<strong>Build</strong> when the constraint is durable, unusual, and importa=
nt enough to justify owning reliability, security, training, and product de=
cisions indefinitely</li>
</ul>
<p>For companies that decide to build, here=E2=80=99s Ferreri=E2=80=99s adv=
ice: </p>
<ul>
<li>
<strong>Find the three or four engineers</strong> closest to the edge of AI=
 and give them a quarter to explore rather than a fixed roadmap </li>
<li>
<strong>Pair the group with an executive sponsor</strong> and bring legal, =
compliance, and security into the work early to establish what the product =
can access and do. But don=E2=80=99t give the group free rein in a vacuum. =
</li>
<li>
<strong>Broaden access only after the team has built <a href=3D"https://icu=
.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698=
e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiVGhlIEhlYWx0a=
GNhcmUgQ29tcGFueSBUaGF0IEJ1aWx0IHRoZSBBSSBUb29sIEl0IENvdWxkbuKAmXQgQnV5Iiwi=
cG9zdF9pZCI6NDQ0NywicG9zdF90eXBlIjoicG9zdCIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vZXZlcnkudG8=
vZ3VpZGVzL3NlY3VyaW5nLWFuLWFsd2F5cy1vbi1haS1lbXBsb3llZSIsInBvc2l0aW9uIjoxM3=
0=3D/1/010001a025c4fe05-11ae7e7d-26ac-47ad-8421-e4639cdcee54-000000/BcKqifq=
yicbSfCrldfM27gwHABKMxRBqYiOCVM27RdE=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" tar=
get=3D"_blank">safe permission boundaries</a></strong> and an architecture =
it can reuse. An engineering-only pilot may be the responsible place to sta=
rt. Eddy spread because Headway eventually made Eddy=E2=80=99s connectors, =
permissions, and artifacts useful outside engineering=E2=80=94not because e=
very department received an unrestricted version on day one.</li>
<li>
<strong>Connect the AI-native builders with everyone else.</strong> Managem=
ent, documentation, training, examples, and internal distribution remain im=
portant for lasting adoption.</li>
</ul>
<p>Headway=E2=80=99s stack isn=E2=80=99t more functionally sophisticated th=
an what=E2=80=99s commercially available. Eddy=E2=80=99s advantage is its s=
ecurity setup, its connections to Headway=E2=80=99s systems, and a product =
plan tailored to the company rather than a vendor=E2=80=99s other 10,000 cu=
stomers. Waiting for a vendor to put those pieces together would have cost =
Headway more than building Eddy. Other companies have to decide whether the=
 tool they can=E2=80=99t buy is worth building=E2=80=94and maintaining=E2=
=80=94themselves.</p>
