ALIGNMENT

The expertise trap. How does arguably the most brilliant mathematician of =
this century use AI?

Quite simply.

I opened Terence Tao https://every.=
to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e1896=
6e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiU29tZXRpbWVzIFlvdSBIYXZlIHRvIERlbGV0ZSBFdmVyeXRoaW5nI=
iwicG9zdF9pZCI6NDM1NiwicG9zdF90eXBlIjoicG9zdCIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vY2hhdGdw=
dC5jb20vc2hhcmUvNmE1ZmRjN2EtZDZmOC04M2U4LWJiZWEtOGRlYjQyY2ZlZDU2IiwicG9zaXR=
pb24iOjM5fQ=3D=3D=E2=80=99s conversation with ChatGPT https://every.=
to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e1896=
6e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiU29tZXRpbWVzIFlvdSBIYXZlIHRvIERlbGV0ZSBFdmVyeXRoaW5nI=
iwicG9zdF9pZCI6NDM1NiwicG9zdF90eXBlIjoicG9zdCIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vY2hhdGdw=
dC5jb20vc2hhcmUvNmE1ZmRjN2EtZDZmOC04M2U4LWJiZWEtOGRlYjQyY2ZlZDU2IiwicG9zaXR=
pb24iOjQwfQ=3D=3D about Fable=E2=80=99s counterexample to the notorious =
Jacobian conjecture https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654=
f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiU29tZXRpbWVzIFlvdSB=
IYXZlIHRvIERlbGV0ZSBFdmVyeXRoaW5nIiwicG9zdF9pZCI6NDM1NiwicG9zdF90eXBlIjoicG=
9zdCIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vZXZlcnkudG8vY29udGV4dC13aW5kb3cvaG93LWV2ZXJ5LXMtd=
GVhbS11c2VkLWFpLXRvLXNoaXAtaXRzLWJpZ2dlc3QtbGF1bmNoLWV2ZXIiLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6=
NDF9, an 87-year-old problem that has long stumped the mathematical =
community. I half-expected beautiful, elaborate prompts I could steal for =
my own AI use. Instead, Tao asks short, precise questions, dense with =
mathematical jargon, and pushes the frontier AI model on reasoning that =
doesn=E2=80=99t make sense. It was like watching a 10-year-old genius being=
 schooled by a much older, wiser genius.

I quickly learned that I could =
copy every prompt Tao used and still never, not in a million years, =
reproduce what he did. This sort of mathematical sorcery can only happen =
when someone has deep knowledge of their craft, because Tao can do the one =
thing a non-expert cannot: Evaluate the response. Without that expertise, =
you don=E2=80=99t know whether the answer coming back to you is correct or =
confidently delivered gibberish.

What irritates me is that I fell for the =
most charlatan-like advice about =E2=80=9Clearning AI=E2=80=9D from =
LinkedIn AI influencers who screenshot the latest prompts promising =
=E2=80=9Coutputs like a McKinsey consultant=E2=80=9D or =E2=80=9Cgrowth =
strategy from a world-class CMO=E2=80=9D=E2=80=94as if expertise is just a =
few sentences you could press the enter key on.

It=E2=80=99s so easy to =
get a seductive answer from AI that I=E2=80=99m afraid more and more of us =
will revert to cognitive offloading and skip the hardship and =
=E2=80=9Cstuckness=E2=80=9D necessary to develop expertise. In =
Anthropic=E2=80=99s study https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f876=
98e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiU29tZXRpbWVzI=
FlvdSBIYXZlIHRvIERlbGV0ZSBFdmVyeXRoaW5nIiwicG9zdF9pZCI6NDM1NiwicG9zdF90eXBl=
IjoicG9zdCIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vd3d3LmFudGhyb3BpYy5jb20vcmVzZWFyY2gvQUktYXN=
zaXN0YW5jZS1jb2Rpbmctc2tpbGxzIiwicG9zaXRpb24iOjQyfQ=3D=3D of 52 mostly =
junior developers learning a new Python library, the AI-assisted group =
scored 50 percent on a subsequent quiz, versus 67 percent for those coding =
by hand. The largest gap between the two groups was in debugging, the skill=
 required to catch the model when it is wrong.

It is a small study, and AI=
 can help people learn. But I now think AI will make expertise more =
valuable and experts harder to produce.

This has irrevocably changed how I=
 use AI. Before reading its answer, I force myself to clarify what I =
already understand. Sometimes I ask, =E2=80=9CWhat is a better question =
here, and why?=E2=80=9D before seeking the answer. The machine is always =
ready to rescue me, but watching Tao, I realized expertise is knowing when =
it hasn=E2=80=99t.=E2=80=94Ashwin Sharma https://every.=
