Software development is about =
to change in ways many teams outside the frontier labs haven=E2=80=99t had =
to think about yet. Our new interactive piece, =E2=80=9CBefore the Deluge,=
=E2=80=9D shows what that looks like from the inside.

We spoke with six members of OpenAI=E2=80=99s infrastructure =
team=E2=80=94including its vice president of applied infrastructure =
engineering=E2=80=94about three converging pressures: an overwhelming surge=
 of AI-generated code, software-development infrastructure pushed to its =
limits, and a fundamental redesign of how code gets reviewed and kept =
reliable.

What they=E2=80=99re working through now is a preview of =
what=E2=80=99s coming for software development everywhere.

=E2=80=9CBefore the Deluge=E2=80=9D reveals how those pressures interact, =
what the engineers are doing to hold the system together, and what the =
broader software community will need to reckon with as AI-generated code =
becomes routine. It=E2=80=99s a close look at a stress test already =
underway=E2=80=94at one of the organizations most responsible for =
accelerating it.

