<p></p>
<p>Software development is about to change in ways many teams outside the f=
rontier labs haven=E2=80=99t had to think about yet. Our new interactive pi=
ece, =E2=80=9CBefore the Deluge,=E2=80=9D shows what that looks like from t=
he inside.</p>
<p>We spoke with six members of OpenAI=E2=80=99s infrastructure team=E2=80=
=94including its vice president of applied infrastructure engineering=E2=80=
=94about three converging pressures: an overwhelming surge of AI-generated =
code, software-development infrastructure pushed to its limits, and a funda=
mental redesign of how code gets reviewed and kept reliable.</p>
<p>What they=E2=80=99re working through now is a preview of what=E2=80=99s =
coming for software development everywhere.</p>
<p>=E2=80=9CBefore the Deluge=E2=80=9D reveals how those pressures interact=
, what the engineers are doing to hold the system together, and what the br=
oader software community will need to reckon with as AI-generated code beco=
mes routine. It=E2=80=99s a close look at a stress test already underway=E2=
=80=94at one of the organizations most responsible for accelerating it.</p>
