<p>Rather than backtracking on billing, Microsoft used the conference stage=
 in California to make the case for using AI more pragmatically in the face=
 of rising costs. I came away from the event thinking that Microsoft is the=
 first company to get real about a world where intelligence is available on=
 tap, but constrained by how many coins you can put in the meter. Here is w=
hat the company=E2=80=99s vision looks like in practice, and what it might =
tell us about how we=E2=80=99ll be paying for and pricing AI in the future.=
 </p>
