cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly9ldmVyeS50by90ZW5kIiwicG9zaXRpb24iOjE2fQ=
=3D=3D, Dan=E2=80=99s open-source productivity tool, check email and Slack =
every 15 minutes. That one wasn=E2=80=99t worth it; we changed the cadence =
that day. Same spend, different answer.

My process is still =
case-by-case=E2=80=94and I expect it will be for a while. But after three =
months of navigating token spend, I=E2=80=99ve learned four lessons for =
companies of our shape and size:

Establish a circuit breaker. In our case,=
 that=E2=80=99s a Ramp card limit and Slack notifications that keep total =
spending visible. When the card runs out, we choose whether to refill it =
and by how much. When we hit the limit, we pause and decide whether the =
work is worth what it will cost to continue.

Make usage visible. We gave =
everyone access to ChatGPT=E2=80=99s usage dashboard so they can see usage =
in real time, including which team members are consuming the most credits. =
Visibility turns spend from a month-end surprise into a team learning loop.=
 The engineer behind the $480 permissions run found ways to make future =
runs more efficient. The Tend owner reduced how often it checked. When the =
cost, output, and lesson are visible together, expensive doesn=E2=80=99t =
automatically mean irresponsible.

Earn the friction. Policies and decision=
 gates introduce friction when a team needs to move quickly. I see it as =
operations=E2=80=99 job to identify risk and demonstrate that a lighter =
guardrail can=E2=80=99t work before imposing heavier restrictions. We give =
the team the tools and resources they need, and we expect them to act =
responsibly in return.

Make change as the evidence changes. If we ever see=
 the team slipping on their end of the bargain=E2=80=94usage nobody can =
explain, lessons nobody shares=E2=80=94we=E2=80=99ll roll back the autonomy=
 and put a platform-level limit in place. We haven=E2=80=99t had to yet. =
We=E2=80=99re a 30-person company operating at the frontier, so we can =
afford to trust our team and react quickly for now. A larger or more =
regulated company may need more checks and limits sooner. The broader =
lesson is to introduce friction only after you=E2=80=99ve seen the problem =
it=E2=80=99s meant to prevent.

