R0cHM6Ly9ldmVyeS50by9AZGFuc2hpcHBlciIsInBvc2l0aW9uIjo1fQ=3D=3D/1/010001a011=
576c78-ce98f7da-fc48-4399-965d-7605189aaf2c-000000/0jgXwbA2IC96RNOF2NkfG1eQ=
MVMC5sPCp7yRpukm9N0=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">Da=
n Shipper</a></strong>, testing Sol (ultra) on tasks designed for a senior =
engineer for that day=E2=80=99s <u><a href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/http=
s:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce6=
87adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiT3VyIEFJIENvc3RzIEp1bXBlZCAyMzA=
gUGVyY2VudC4gSeKAmW0gTm90IFNldHRpbmcgVG9rZW4gQnVkZ2V0c-KAlFlldC4iLCJwb3N0X2=
lkIjo0NDExLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly9ldmVyeS50by92aWJlL=
WNoZWNrL2dwdC01LTYtc29sIiwicG9zaXRpb24iOjZ9/1/010001a011576c78-ce98f7da-fc4=
8-4399-965d-7605189aaf2c-000000/jDvTIOhVa3c9kQug09QTzYk_ICNazQcMRiqf_VjxZbY=
=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">Vibe Check</a></u> of=
 the model. By 10 a.m., we=E2=80=99d restocked the Ramp card with new funds=
, and I thought the storm had subsided. But our token spending stayed unusu=
ally high for the rest of the day, and we haven=E2=80=99t had a normal day =
since. </p>
<p>In the first five full days after <u><a href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0=
/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619e=
afce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiT3VyIEFJIENvc3RzIEp1bXBlZC=
AyMzAgUGVyY2VudC4gSeKAmW0gTm90IFNldHRpbmcgVG9rZW4gQnVkZ2V0c-KAlFlldC4iLCJwb=
3N0X2lkIjo0NDExLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly9ldmVyeS50by92=
aWJlLWNoZWNrL2dwdC01LTYtc29sIiwicG9zaXRpb24iOjd9/1/010001a011576c78-ce98f7d=
a-fc48-4399-965d-7605189aaf2c-000000/UheDVFBklRJ6XsQZjEmUmAJrwdv1QzXS-5B1a-=
niwzQ=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">GPT-5.6</a></u> =
Sol rolled out, our daily credit usage rose from 11,520 to 26,685 credits=
=E2=80=94almost 2.5 times our previous-week baseline. I had spent weeks bra=
cing for <u><a href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femai=
ls%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e2=
42%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiT3VyIEFJIENvc3RzIEp1bXBlZCAyMzAgUGVyY2VudC4gSeKAmW0gTm=
90IFNldHRpbmcgVG9rZW4gQnVkZ2V0c-KAlFlldC4iLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0NDExLCJwb3N0X3R5c=
GUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly9ldmVyeS50by92aWJlLWNoZWNrL2FudGhyb3BpYy1t=
eXRob3Mtb3VyLWZhYmxlLXZpYmUtY2hlY2siLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6OH0=3D/1/010001a011576c=
78-ce98f7da-fc48-4399-965d-7605189aaf2c-000000/qWgkN5eDOWmHQ5EP8p05Cz9WPQR1=
A-Dry2vUVS31hDQ=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">Fable<=
/a></u> to blow up our budget, but Sol was the storm I didn=E2=80=99t see c=
oming. Suddenly, I had to figure out how to enable daily work without bankr=
upting us. My colleagues=E2=80=99 reactions ran the gamut from =E2=80=9CLet=
 =E2=80=98er rip and let=E2=80=99s see where it lands at the end of the mon=
th!=E2=80=9D to =E2=80=9CWe gotta impose limits now, and we should start ex=
ploring running our own models locally.=E2=80=9D Meanwhile, we were burning=
 through a month=E2=80=99s worth of token spend every few days.  </p>
<p>There was no easy solution. Experimentation is part of everyone=E2=80=99=
s job at Every; from engineering to business development, we all need to le=
arn what these models can do and where they=E2=80=99re useful. Because valu=
able insights can come from anywhere in our company, everyone needs to be a=
ble to spend. Unlike many companies, we don=E2=80=99t go all-in on one mode=
l. People use whichever works best for the job, which makes our costs harde=
r to predict as new models with different strengths and pricing structures =
come out. Any intricate allocation scheme I devised would be obsolete in da=
ys, if not hours. </p>
<p>With input from the team and a lot of thought, I put in place a loose op=
erational process instead of strict spending policies=E2=80=94and for now, =
it=E2=80=99s working.</p>  <div class=3D"ea-block normal">
