<p>Mike predicts that tokens will be allocated and controlled on a stricter=
 basis under this system: =E2=80=9CJust like with trading, you=E2=80=99ll h=
ave risk limits, auditing, and you=E2=80=99ll have to get certain-size bets=
 approved.=E2=80=9D More broadly, we=E2=80=99re likely headed for a world w=
ith more restrictions placed on who is granted a token budget and what they=
=E2=80=99re allowed to do with it. Top engineers who can prove ROI will ben=
efit, as will managers. =E2=80=9CWho are you going to give a token budget t=
o, an IC [individual contributor] who prefers to handcraft their code anywa=
y, or a manager who is already accustomed to directing 5x or 10x their own =
salary in resources?=E2=80=9D Mike asks. </p>
<p>In this version of the near future, an intern might have access to Compo=
ser 2.5, most employees will work out of Codex or an equivalent, while Fabl=
e-grade models are reserved for top engineers. There=E2=80=99s too much mon=
ey on the line to hand over frontier access to anyone but an elite few. </p=
