In 2025, Microsoft CTO Kevin Scott made a bet on what would come =
next for AI.

He argued that agents wouldn=E2=80=99t become truly useful =
until they could act autonomously=E2=80=94and that doing so would require =
building an =E2=80=9Cagentic web=E2=80=9D: the plumbing that lets agents =
access the tools, data, and systems they need to take action.

So far, that bet is paying off. MCP, the protocol that allows agents to =
connect to outside tools and information, has since been adopted by OpenAI,=
 Google, Amazon, and Microsoft=E2=80=94and agents are now able to work =
asynchronously without the need for constant prompting, just as Kevin =
predicted.

On this week=E2=80=99s AI & I, we=E2=80=99re revisiting the =
episode. Kevin and Dan Shipper discuss the beginnings of the agentic =
web=E2=80=94and why Kevin thinks it has to be open rather than owned by any=
 single company.

