<h2 id=3D"signal"><strong>Signal</strong></h2>
<h4 id=3D"ai-attacks-are-leaks-not-heists"><strong>AI attacks are leaks, no=
t heists</strong></h4>
<p><strong>What happened:</strong> An OpenAI agent <u><a href=3D"https://ic=
u.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f8769=
8e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiQWdlbnRzIEZp=
bmQgYSBXYXkiLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0NDA3LCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM=
6Ly9vcGVuYWkuY29tL2luZGV4L2h1Z2dpbmctZmFjZS1tb2RlbC1ldmFsdWF0aW9uLXNlY3VyaX=
R5LWluY2lkZW50LyIsInBvc2l0aW9uIjo3fQ=3D=3D/1/0100019ff7ab53db-2d613fbe-3579=
-4dfe-8e38-e9130ba7485e-000000/HADJLplbv3xkthkZ5TfRaQh1WPLKFIy_zvJrWhvC0Gg=
=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">escaped</a></u> its t=
est environment and hacked into AI research library Hugging Face=E2=80=99s =
systems, causing an understandable uproar. Online, reactions swirled into a=
 narrative about AI agents scheming behind the scenes. </p>
<p>This nefarious <u><a href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.=
to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc0=
2e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiQWdlbnRzIEZpbmQgYSBXYXkiLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0NDA3L=
CJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly93d3cudGhlZ3VhcmRpYW4uY29tL3Rl=
Y2hub2xvZ3kvMjAyNi9qdWwvMjIvb3BlbmFpLXNheXMtaXRzLW1vZGVscy13ZW50LXJvZ3VlLWF=
uZC1oYWNrZWQtc3RhcnR1cC1pbi11bnByZWNlZGVudGVkLWluY2lkZW50IiwicG9zaXRpb24iOj=
h9/1/0100019ff7ab53db-2d613fbe-3579-4dfe-8e38-e9130ba7485e-000000/REt5mkXtX=
vhgEZIp2pkxekSNFpURvkNobcZlur_U_cg=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" targe=
t=3D"_blank">rogue-agent angle</a></u> misses the point, says Every CEO <st=
rong><u><a href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2=
Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2=
FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiQWdlbnRzIEZpbmQgYSBXYXkiLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0NDA3LCJwb3N0X3R5cG=
UiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly9ldmVyeS50by9AZGFuc2hpcHBlciIsInBvc2l0aW9uI=
jo5fQ=3D=3D/1/0100019ff7ab53db-2d613fbe-3579-4dfe-8e38-e9130ba7485e-000000/=
DDPm2yPgVPGyh-GRwnoX3JKrowuAJ5IUkXXNi8SMXe4=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferr=
er" target=3D"_blank">Dan Shipper</a></u></strong>: =E2=80=9CYou have a GPT=
-5.6 Sol model that=E2=80=99s trained to be more persistent than usual, wit=
h no cyber safeguards, and it=E2=80=99s asked to do an exploit.=E2=80=9D Of=
 <em>course</em> it exploited the control failures it found.</p>
<p>The real story is the scale and relentlessness of the agent=E2=80=99s ef=
forts: Hugging Face <u><a href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fever=
y.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefc=
c02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiQWdlbnRzIEZpbmQgYSBXYXkiLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0NDA=
3LCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly9odWdnaW5nZmFjZS5jby9ibG9nL2=
FnZW50LWludHJ1c2lvbi10ZWNobmljYWwtdGltZWxpbmUiLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6MTB9/1/010001=
9ff7ab53db-2d613fbe-3579-4dfe-8e38-e9130ba7485e-000000/1dy4wvmOMdZX2w1dqy_B=
NevaZfo0CpPC8GcqACn9MrM=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank=
">reconstructed roughly 17,600 agent actions</a></u> over four and a half d=
ays. =E2=80=9CWhen you have things that can code and have nearly infinite p=
atience and persistence, they=E2=80=99re going to find vulnerabilities,=E2=
=80=9D Dan says.</p>
<p><strong>Why it matters: </strong>AI agents don=E2=80=99t operate like th=
ieves; they operate like water: =E2=80=9CAny leak and they=E2=80=99re going=
 to get through,=E2=80=9D Dan says. </p>
<p>Perimeter defenses alone are no longer enough; Dan compares them to secu=
rity cameras and guard dogs. Companies need always-on, proactive systems th=
at can connect subtle warning signs and contain breaches at machine speed. =
You try to make your systems watertight, and you build pumps for the water =
that inevitably slips through.</p>
<p>OpenAI and Hugging Face are already operating this way, using tactics in=
cluding classifiers, cyber refusals, and defensive agents. Dan sees a world=
 in which frontier labs make their agents =E2=80=9Cmore snitchy,=E2=80=9D o=
r likelier to flag each other=E2=80=99s suspicious or unexpected behavior=
=E2=80=94one more tool that raises the cost of an attack and buys defenders=
 time.</p>
<p><strong>What it means:</strong> As models improve and agents are optimiz=
ed for attack=E2=80=94and become cheaper to run=E2=80=94the scale of agent-=
orchestrated attacks will grow so large we could all be impacted, says engi=
neer <strong>Lee Knowlton</strong>. </p>
<p>=E2=80=9CAs a developer, a parent, and the person who=E2=80=99s probably=
 in charge of my family=E2=80=99s passwords, I=E2=80=99m thinking: =E2=80=
=98Make sure you don=E2=80=99t have weak passwords still out there,=E2=80=
=99=E2=80=9D he says. =E2=80=9CIf humans are doing it now, suddenly you can=
 have infinite agents doing the same thing.=E2=80=9D</p>
