<h2 id=3D"ai-i-building-the-internet-for-ai-agents"><strong>=E2=80=98AI &am=
p; I=E2=80=99: Building the internet for AI agents </strong></h2>
<p>In 2025, Microsoft CTO Kevin Scott made a bet on what would come next fo=
r AI.</p>
<p>He argued that agents wouldn=E2=80=99t become truly useful until they co=
uld act autonomously=E2=80=94and that doing so would require building an =
=E2=80=9Cagentic web=E2=80=9D: the plumbing that lets agents access the too=
ls, data, and systems they need to take action. </p>
<p>So far, that bet is paying off. MCP, the protocol that allows agents to =
connect to outside tools and information, has since been adopted by OpenAI,=
 Google, Amazon, and Microsoft=E2=80=94and agents are now able to work asyn=
chronously without the need for constant prompting, just as Kevin predicted=
. </p>
<p>On this week=E2=80=99s <em>AI &amp; I</em>, we=E2=80=99re revisiting the=
 episode. Kevin and Dan Shipper discuss the beginnings of the agentic web=
=E2=80=94and why Kevin thinks it has to be open rather than owned by any si=
ngle company.</p>
