jb20vaW4vcGFyaWRoaTcvIiwicG9zaXRpb24iOjEwfQ=3D=3D" rel=3D"noopener noreferr=
er" target=3D"_blank">Paridhi Agarwal</a></u></strong> use multiple termina=
ls to parallelize her work. =E2=80=9CI=E2=80=99ve never seen it think about=
 my setup like that!=E2=80=9D she says. </p>
<p>When head of growth and known Codex convert <strong><u><a href=3D"https:=
//every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefc=
c02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiT3B1cyA0LjcgUmVlbHMgVXMgQmFjayBJbiIsInBvc3Rfa=
WQiOjQyMjgsInBvc3RfdHlwZSI6InBvc3QiLCJ1cmwiOiJodHRwczovL2V2ZXJ5LnRvL0B0ZWRl=
c2NhdSIsInBvc2l0aW9uIjoxMX0=3D" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blan=
k">Austin Tedesco</a></u></strong> fired up Opus 4.7 over the weekend for a=
 creative writing project, he was surprised by how good the results were. C=
ompared to Codex, which Austin says operates like an =E2=80=9CAP fact check=
er,=E2=80=9D Opus 4.7 was closer to a senior magazine editor. Dan agrees: =
=E2=80=9CCodex feels fast but thin in terms of thinking.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p>On Tuesday, Anthropic released <u><a href=3D"https://every.to/emails/cli=
