bi5zcG90aWZ5LmNvbS9lcGlzb2RlLzYwUzg5Q3VIUDJSRG5HMkg4clZLY0Y_c2k9SzB4WTU2eDN=
SVGVuUUlFYnIzaVRYUSIsInBvc2l0aW9uIjoxMX0=3D" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" ta=
rget=3D"_blank">Spotify</a> or <a href=3D"https://every.to/emails/click/7c3=
f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0I=
joiTWluaS1WaWJlIENoZWNrOiBDbGF1ZGUgTWFuYWdlZCBBZ2VudHMgSGFuZGxlIHRoZSBJbmZy=
YXN0cnVjdHVyZSBXb3JrIiwicG9zdF9pZCI6NDExMSwicG9zdF90eXBlIjoicG9zdCIsInVybCI=
6Imh0dHBzOi8vcG9kY2FzdHMuYXBwbGUuY29tL3VzL3BvZGNhc3QvdGhlLWFpLW1vZGVsLWJ1aW=
x0LWZvci13aGF0LWxsbXMtY2FudC1kby9pZDE3MTk3ODkyMDE_aT0xMDAwNzYxNTYxNDI4Iiwic=
G9zaXRpb24iOjEyfQ=3D=3D" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">Appl=
e Podcasts</a>. You can also read <a href=3D"https://every.to/emails/click/=
7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZW=
N0IjoiTWluaS1WaWJlIENoZWNrOiBDbGF1ZGUgTWFuYWdlZCBBZ2VudHMgSGFuZGxlIHRoZSBJb=
mZyYXN0cnVjdHVyZSBXb3JrIiwicG9zdF9pZCI6NDExMSwicG9zdF90eXBlIjoicG9zdCIsInVy=
bCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vZXZlcnkudG8vcG9kY2FzdC90cmFuc2NyaXB0LXRoZS1haS1tb2RlbC1idWl=
sdC1mb3Itd2hhdC1sbG1zLWNhbi10LWRvIiwicG9zaXRpb24iOjEzfQ=3D=3D" rel=3D"noope=
ner noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">the transcript</a>.</p>
<p>Here=E2=80=99s how LLMs and EBMs are different, according to Bodnia: </p=
>
<ul>
<li>
<strong>Architecture transparency:</strong> You can=E2=80=99t see inside an=
 LLM; you can only evaluate its outputs. EBMs are governed by physics, whic=
h means their architecture is legible while they=E2=80=99re running. =E2=80=
=9CThink of it as something that doesn=E2=80=99t play a guessing game, with=
 an architecture that essentially allows it to self-align as it processes i=
nformation,=E2=80=9D she says. =E2=80=9CIt=E2=80=99s no longer a black box.=
=E2=80=9D </li>
<li>
<strong>Language-based versus data-native: </strong>LLMs are language-depen=
dent even when the task has nothing to do with language, like data analysis=
=2E =E2=80=9CIf your data is numbers, rela=
tionships, and functions, and you t=
ry to map those rules into words and then search for the next word, you=E2=
=80=99re losing a lot of information,=E2=80=9D Bodnia says. EBMs work direc=
tly with the underlying data structure, including numbers and spatial coord=
inates.</li>
<li>
<strong>Sequential versus panoramic reasoning:</strong> An LLM is like navi=
gating San Francisco without a map. Each turn constrains the next, and if y=
ou go down the wrong street, you can=E2=80=99t reverse course. An EBM, by c=
ontrast, has the bird=E2=80=99s-eye view=E2=80=94it can evaluate multiple r=
outes at once and course-correct before hitting a dead end.</li>
</ul>
