t=3D"_blank">Opus 4.7</a></u>. Humans still score in the high 80s and low 9=
0s. The twist: GPT-5.5=E2=80=99s best run used an Opus-written plan.</li>
<li>
<strong>A real writing comeback. </strong>It=E2=80=99s the strongest OpenAI=
 model we=E2=80=99ve tested in a year, with cleaner structure and smoother =
logical progression than Opus 4.7. </li>
<li>
<strong>Strong everyday knowledge work.</strong> GPT-5.5 beat Opus 4.7 on d=
ashboards and felt dependable for creating client deliverables or customer =
support replies. </li>
<li>
<strong>Best with structure.</strong> GPT-5.5 shines with a plan, an existi=
ng system, or a tight feedback loop. Opus 4.7 still has advantages on one-s=
hot vibe coding, PowerPoint, Ruby, and some broad product-design tasks.</li=
>
</ul>
