<h2 id=3D"alignment">Alignment</h2>
<p><strong>The hand across the page. </strong>Juneteenth=E2=80=94the day Am=
ericans mark the end of slavery=E2=80=94was a few days ago. I=E2=80=99m hal=
fway through <strong>James Baldwin</strong>=E2=80=99s semi-autobiographical=
 novel <em><u><a href=3D"https://icu.every.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Fem=
ails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966=
e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiQnVpbHQgb24gTW92aW5nIEdyb3VuZCIsInBvc3RfaWQiOjQzMTAs=
InBvc3RfdHlwZSI6InBvc3QiLCJ1cmwiOiJodHRwczovL2VuLndpa2lwZWRpYS5vcmcvd2lraS9=
Hb19UZWxsX0l0X29uX3RoZV9Nb3VudGFpbl8obm92ZWwpIiwicG9zaXRpb24iOjU3fQ=3D=3D/1=
/0100019eea0ba790-662a066a-2a7e-482e-9388-9d747ce2102d-000000/kclgoDb9ESjNM=
F8cU0pKTaDvhJrhM5eGkt-1yS6eYjs=3D452" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D=
"_blank">Go Tell It on the Mountain</a></u></em><u><a href=3D"https://icu.e=
very.to/CL0/https:%2F%2Fevery.to%2Femails%2Fclick%2F7c3f95455f05e60f87698e6=
54f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242%2FeyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiQnVpbHQgb24gTW9=
2aW5nIEdyb3VuZCIsInBvc3RfaWQiOjQzMTAsInBvc3RfdHlwZSI6InBvc3QiLCJ1cmwiOiJodH=
RwczovL2VuLndpa2lwZWRpYS5vcmcvd2lraS9Hb19UZWxsX0l0X29uX3RoZV9Nb3VudGFpbl8ob=
m92ZWwpIiwicG9zaXRpb24iOjU4fQ=3D=3D/1/0100019eea0ba790-662a066a-2a7e-482e-9=
388-9d747ce2102d-000000/AuF49gaFwlGDv0LP-d9vsoGD6GwRAOU2bdgNxGl8JFo=3D452" =
rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">,</a></u> reading several pag=
es each night as an excuse to keep my phone out of my hands before bed. </p=
>
<p>It=E2=80=99s the best thing I=E2=80=99ve read all year. Baldwin drops us=
 into the shoes of his young Black protagonist, John, as he=E2=80=99s about=
 to turn 14 and his family=E2=80=99s Pentecostal church prepares to hold an=
 all-night prayer service. The story takes place in late winter, in 1930s H=
arlem, and reads like a time capsule of the era=E2=80=99s bubbling social t=
ensions. </p>
<p>Baldwin=E2=80=99s prose is constantly surprising; his turns of phrase ri=
ng so true that they disarm you, open you to feeling what his character fee=
ls: =E2=80=9CJohn=E2=80=99s heart was hardened against the Lord,=E2=80=9D h=
e writes. =E2=80=9CHis father was God=E2=80=99s minister, the ambassador of=
 the King of Heaven, and John could not bow before the throne of grace with=
out first kneeling to his father.=E2=80=9D You come to that sentence braced=
 for a question of faith and leave it understanding a boy who cannot reach =
God because he cannot get past his own father. </p>
<p>The element of surprise is the first thing stripped out when AI is hande=
d the most personal things we have to express. A few weeks ago, I listened =
to an AI-written wedding speech, and the disappointment I felt in the momen=
t has stuck with me. The groom had handed off the one chance to say, in his=
 own surprising and unrepeatable way, what his partner meant to him. What c=
ame out instead were words that could=E2=80=99ve been written for anyone. <=
/p>
<p>I don=E2=80=99t expect everyone to be (or even approximate) a Baldwin or=
 <strong>Hemingway</strong>, or to deliver <strong>JFK</strong>-like speech=
