<h2>How I=E2=80=99m using Monologue Notes</h2>
<p><em>On morning walks.</em> I don=E2=80=99t listen to music or podcasts. =
When I leave the house, I hit record and start thinking out loud.</p>
<p>There=E2=80=99s no agenda. Sometimes I fixate on a feature question or a=
 tough conversation I had with a colleague. Other times, my mind wanders, c=
ycling through topics in rapid succession.</p>
<p>Back at my desk, I open Codex and run the same prompt: =E2=80=9CPull up =
my last Monologue note, and start building this.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p>Just like that, my rambling thoughts become action items.</p>
