<h3><hr class=3D"quill-line"></h3>
<h2 id=3D"steal-this-workflow"><strong>Steal this workflow</strong></h2>
<h4 id=3D"turn-a-bad-support-chat-into-better-agent-instructions"><strong>T=
urn a bad support chat into better agent instructions</strong></h4>
<p>When Fin=E2=80=99s customer support agent handles a customer conversatio=
n incorrectly, CS manager <strong>Waqqas Mir</strong> doesn=E2=80=99t rewri=
te its entire support setup. Instead, he uses Codex to turn the mishandled =
chat into a targeted new instruction. Using this method, he=E2=80=99s added=
 a rule specifying when the agent should escalate an angry customer to a hu=
man and an explicit instruction to patch a bug in which Fin would generate =
code for a user if they asked=E2=80=94a guardrail Waqqas put in after he go=
t Fin to write him a file-conversion script during a test.</p>
<h5 id=3D"waqqass-workflow"><strong>Waqqas=E2=80=99s workflow:</strong></h5=
>
<ol>
<li>
<strong>Connect Codex to Fin through the platform=E2=80=99s Model Context P=
rotocol (MCP) server.</strong> Once authorized, the MCP lets Codex retrieve=
 conversations from your Fin workspace. In a Codex prompt, enter the identi=
fication numbers for two or three chats where Fin made the wrong call and a=
sk Codex to pull the full conversations and diagnose what went wrong.</li>
<li>
<strong>Ask Codex where the instructions broke down.</strong> Follow up by =
asking, =E2=80=9CWhy did it not follow my instructions? Can you identify wh=
at is causing the confusion?=E2=80=9D Codex will identify missing, unclear,=
 or contradictory guidance, and propose concise additions to fix the issue.=
 </li>
<li>
<strong>Add the proposed rule and retest the scenario.</strong> The MCP con=
nection allows Codex to analyze Fin data, but Codex cannot directly change =
Fin=E2=80=99s setup. Waqqas adds the new guidance himself, then runs the sa=
me type of conversation again. If Fin repeats the mistake, he gives Codex t=
hat conversation=E2=80=99s chat ID and asks it to pinpoint which instructio=
n is still causing the issue. </li>
</ol>
