lank">Alephic</a></u>=E2=80=94and in his own work, where he uses Claude Cod=
e as a</em> <em><u><a href=3D"https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60=
f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiVGhlIEN1b=
HR1cmUgb2YgQUkgRW5naW5lZXJpbmciLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0MTkwLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0=
IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly93d3cueW91dHViZS5jb20vd2F0Y2g_dj04Vjl0WndnamlScyIsInB=
vc2l0aW9uIjo2fQ=3D=3D" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">second=
 brain</a></u>=E2=80=94he=E2=80=99s facing that same problem with agents in=
 the mix. AI was supposed to make coordination easier. Instead, Noah argues=
, it has created new coordination problems of its own. In this piece, he pu=
shes back on the =E2=80=9Csoftware factory=E2=80=9D metaphor and offers a f=
ramework, drawn from </em><strong><em>Stewart Brand</em></strong><em>=E2=80=
=99s pace layers, for getting carbon and silicon to build the same thing.=
=E2=80=94<u><a href=3D"https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e=
654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiVGhlIEN1bHR1cmUg=
b2YgQUkgRW5naW5lZXJpbmciLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0MTkwLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJ=
sIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly9ldmVyeS50by9Aa2F0ZV8xNzY3IiwicG9zaXRpb24iOjd9" rel=3D"noope=
ner noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">Kate Lee</a></u></em></p>
