<p></p>
<p>Strong DM is a software company whose three-person AI team calls their s=
ystem for autonomous code generation a <u><a href=3D"https://every.to/email=
s/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/ey=
JzdWJqZWN0IjoiVGhlIEN1bHR1cmUgb2YgQUkgRW5naW5lZXJpbmciLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0MTkwL=
CJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly9mYWN0b3J5LnN0cm9uZ2RtLmFpLyIs=
InBvc2l0aW9uIjo4fQ=3D=3D" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">=E2=
=80=9CSoftware Factory.=E2=80=9D</a></u> Entrepreneur <strong>Dan Shapiro</=
strong>=E2=80=98s <u><a href=3D"https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e=
60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiVGhlIEN=
1bHR1cmUgb2YgQUkgRW5naW5lZXJpbmciLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0MTkwLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3=
N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZGFuc2hhcGlyby5jb20vYmxvZy8yMDI2LzAxL3RoZS1ma=
XZlLWxldmVscy1mcm9tLXNwaWN5LWF1dG9jb21wbGV0ZS10by10aGUtc29mdHdhcmUtZmFjdG9y=
eS8iLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6OX0=3D" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">w=
idely circulated framework for AI coding</a></u> culminates in =E2=80=9Cthe=
 Dark Factory,=E2=80=9D named after a Japanese robotics plant that <u><a hr=
ef=3D"https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce6=
87adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiVGhlIEN1bHR1cmUgb2YgQUkgRW5naW5lZ=
XJpbmciLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0MTkwLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly9l=
bi53aWtpcGVkaWEub3JnL3dpa2kvTGlnaHRzX291dF8obWFudWZhY3R1cmluZykiLCJwb3NpdGl=
vbiI6MTB9" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">runs with the ligh=
ts off</a></u>. <u><a href=3D"https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60=
f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiVGhlIEN1b=
HR1cmUgb2YgQUkgRW5naW5lZXJpbmciLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0MTkwLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0=
IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cDovL2ZhY3RvcnkuYWkiLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6MTF9" rel=3D"noopener n=
oreferrer" target=3D"_blank">Factory.ai</a></u>, which has raised millions =
from Sequoia and Khosla Ventures, has built an entire business around the m=
etaphor=E2=80=94its autonomous coding agents are called Droids. </p>
<p>I=E2=80=99ve been incorporating many of StrongDM=E2=80=99s concepts abou=
t agentic software development into our work at <u><a href=3D"https://every=
=2Eto/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f8769=
8e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e189=
66e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiVGhlIEN1bHR1cmUgb2YgQUkgRW5naW5lZXJpbmciLCJwb3N0X2lk=
Ijo0MTkwLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYWxlcGhpYy5jb20=
vIiwicG9zaXRpb24iOjEyfQ=3D=3D" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank=
">Alephic</a></u>, the consulting company I co-founded=E2=80=94but I have o=
ne fundamental disagreement: I think factory is the wrong metaphor.</p>
<p>If the hardest problem is making something people want, then the process=
 of building software looks a lot more like <strong>Andy Warhol</strong>=E2=
=80=98s factory than <strong>Henry Ford</strong>=E2=80=98s. Both are focuse=
d on throughput, but Ford=E2=80=99s is focused on mechanization and stampin=
g out identical cars with as little variance as possible. Warhol, on the ot=
her hand, was concerned with ensuring all work aligned with a single creati=
ve vision.</p>
<p>Ford=E2=80=99s factory=E2=80=94or more specifically, the assembly lines =
inside it=E2=80=94was designed to eliminate imperfections. <u><a href=3D"ht=
tps://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5e=
befcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiVGhlIEN1bHR1cmUgb2YgQUkgRW5naW5lZXJpbmciL=
CJwb3N0X2lkIjo0MTkwLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly9lbi53aWtp=
cGVkaWEub3JnL3dpa2kvU2l4X1NpZ21hIiwicG9zaXRpb24iOjEzfQ=3D=3D" rel=3D"noopen=
er noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">Six Sigma</a></u>, the quality methodology=
 made famous by General Electric and beloved of manufacturers, is literally=
 a measure of the defect rate. Quality starts with deciding what to build. =
This is why <u><a href=3D"https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f876=
98e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiVGhlIEN1bHR1c=
mUgb2YgQUkgRW5naW5lZXJpbmciLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0MTkwLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0Iiwi=
dXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly9wbWFyY2hpdmUuY29tL2d1aWRlX3RvX3N0YXJ0dXBzX3BhcnQ0Lmh0bWw=
iLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6MTR9" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">produc=
t-market fit</a></u> is the lingua franca of startups: If you haven=E2=80=
=99t built something the market needs, nothing else=E2=80=94including the q=
uality of your code=E2=80=94matters.</p>
<p>Too much of the industry treats software as a problem to be optimized an=
d solved. That may be true for code writing and testing, but the better met=
aphor is staring us in the face: It=E2=80=99s a software <em>company</em>, =
not a software <em>factory</em>.</p>
<p>Just as in the days before AI, the hardest problem for a business is sti=
ll creating this vision and alignment around it=E2=80=94how to keep an enti=
re team of humans, and now humans and agents (and humans with agents), buil=
ding toward the same vision, from the system architecture down to the indiv=
idual lines of code. As I=E2=80=99ve learned long before agents existed, ac=
hieving this is much more akin to building a startup than assembling a car.=
 What follows is my attempt at a framework for keeping an entire system of =
humans and agents building the same thing. </p>  <div class=3D"ea-block nor=
mal">
