<p><br></p>
<p>Here=E2=80=99s how I=E2=80=99ve been thinking about the =E2=80=9Cpace la=
yers=E2=80=9D of AI engineering and how we=E2=80=99re building tooling at A=
lephic to help both humans and agents move in the same direction:</p>
<ol>
<li>
<strong>Code is fashion now</strong>. Whereas it once sat deeper in the sta=
ck, where it was slower moving and insulated by other layers, in a world of=
 AI, code is free to produce and reproduce. The challenge is how to do it r=
ight: free of bugs at the macro level, and aligned with your own vision and=
 best practices at the micro level. By the time we get to this layer, we ha=
ve to trust that the layers beneath are strong enough to steer the system t=
o the places we need it to go.</li>
<li>
<strong>Plans sit beneath code</strong>. Before an agent writes anything, i=
t should pause to survey the problem=E2=80=94<u><a href=3D"https://every.to=
/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e=
242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiVGhlIEN1bHR1cmUgb2YgQUkgRW5naW5lZXJpbmciLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo=
0MTkwLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly9ldmVyeS50by9zb3VyY2UtY2=
9kZS9zdG9wLWNvZGluZy1hbmQtc3RhcnQtcGxhbm5pbmctYmUwYjRmZDEtNTg5OC00YjA5LWJmZ=
GEtMGIwMGVhMDAwNGZkIiwicG9zaXRpb24iOjMwfQ=3D=3D" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer=
" target=3D"_blank">what are the possible approaches</a></u>, and what are =
the trade-offs? Only after completing this step should the agent pick a dir=
ection and build. Many algorithms in computer science rely on the explore-e=
xploit shift=E2=80=94when you time-box a broad search phase before zeroing =
in on a solution to run with=E2=80=94and this plan phase is no different. A=
 plan doesn=E2=80=99t have to be a formal document, but it must separate th=
e <u><a href=3D"https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454=
c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiVGhlIEN1bHR1cmUgb2YgQUk=
gRW5naW5lZXJpbmciLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0MTkwLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaH=
R0cHM6Ly93d3cubm9haGJyaWVyLmNvbS9hcmNoaXZlcy8yMDE5LzAzL2V4cGxvcmF0aW9uLXZzL=
WV4cGxvaXRhdGlvbiIsInBvc2l0aW9uIjozMX0=3D" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" targ=
et=3D"_blank">thinking from the doing</a></u>. Without this pause, explorat=
ion and execution get mashed together.</li>
<li>
<strong>Specs sit beneath plans</strong>. A good plan needs a good specific=
ation. That can be a ticket (a task that needs doing), a document, or just =
a conversation, but it explains what we are building, why we are building i=
t, how you know you=E2=80=99ve done it right, and, critically, what we are =
not tackling right now. That last bit is particularly important for overeag=
er AI that wants to please by building everything you wanted and a little m=
ore. There=E2=80=99s a <u><a href=3D"https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f9545=
5f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiVG=
hlIEN1bHR1cmUgb2YgQUkgRW5naW5lZXJpbmciLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0MTkwLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiO=
iJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly9oYXNrZWxsZm9yYWxsLmNvbS8yMDI2LzAzL2Etc3VmZmlj=
aWVudGx5LWRldGFpbGVkLXNwZWMtaXMtY29kZSIsInBvc2l0aW9uIjozMn0=3D" rel=3D"noop=
ener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">good debate</a></u> in the engineering c=
ommunity about what constitutes a good spec. It=E2=80=99s the simplest set =
of directives that shrink the planning space: a goal, a set of acceptance c=
riteria, and an explicit list of out-of-scope problems.</li>
<li>
<strong>Architecture is the theory of the system</strong>. I=E2=80=99ve bee=
n keeping an ARCHITECTURE.md doc in all my codebases for a while now, borro=
wing from computer scientist <strong>Peter Naur</strong>=E2=80=98s <u><a hr=
ef=3D"https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce6=
87adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiVGhlIEN1bHR1cmUgb2YgQUkgRW5naW5lZ=
XJpbmciLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0MTkwLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly9j=
ZWtyZW0uZ2l0aHViLmlvL3Bvc3RzL3Byb2dyYW1taW5nLWFzLXRoZW9yeS1idWlsZGluZy1uYXV=
yLyIsInBvc2l0aW9uIjozM30=3D" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">=
idea</a></u> that the real program isn=E2=80=99t the code, it=E2=80=99s the=
 mental model the developers carry. The document shows how the business pro=
blem maps to the codebase, so you can predict where to find the code that s=
olves this problem. It captures the key decisions and why they were made, a=
nd lays out the rules that must always hold, such as =E2=80=9Cno database q=
ueries outside the repository layer=E2=80=9D and =E2=80=9Cno framework impo=
rts in the business logic.=E2=80=9D Critically, it also names what=E2=80=99=
s still an open question, so AI doesn=E2=80=99t silently make architectural=
 decisions for you, taking the codebase somewhere you didn=E2=80=99t intend=
=2E</li>
<li>
<strong>Standards</strong> <strong>are the foundation.</strong> Some are ge=
neral principles of good software-building; others reflect our specific bel=
iefs about how software should be built. One of the insights that drove me =
to start the company was when, years ago, I asked a developer I had worked =
with for a decade if I could have all his <u><a href=3D"https://every.to/em=
ails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242=
/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiVGhlIEN1bHR1cmUgb2YgQUkgRW5naW5lZXJpbmciLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0MT=
kwLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYWxlcGhpYy5jb20vZ2xvc=
3NhcnkvbGludGluZyIsInBvc2l0aW9uIjozNH0=3D" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" targ=
et=3D"_blank">configuration files</a></u>, the ones that encode his rules f=
or how code should be written. When I applied this rulebook to my own work,=
 I became a significantly better developer. His strict approach to linting,=
 or automated rules that reject code with unused imports or superfluous def=
initions, meant my code wouldn=E2=80=99t even run unless it met his standar=
ds. Cutting corners was no longer an option. At Alephic, we enforce many of=
 these standards with tools like tests and static analysis, which let the c=
omputer check your code automatically. But a lot of this guidance also live=
s in skills we distribute across the company, so people can use it in whate=
ver harness they choose. The code-organization skill memorializes how we wa=
nt team members to organize their codebases, and coding-best-practices hard=
codes the stylistic and technical preferences our platform engineering team=
 has established.</li>
</ol>
<p>With AI, we can take these ideas beyond the mechanisms of cultural excha=
nge I had in my Percolate days (like documents and meetings) and encode the=
m into tools that every person can interact with every day.</p>
<p>The layers at the bottom move the slowest, so they should get updated th=
e least frequently. For instance, I could start keeping a document in a sin=
gle project as a way to give agents context on how the codebase was organiz=
ed. If it works well enough, I turn it into a <u><a href=3D"https://every.t=
o/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966=
e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiVGhlIEN1bHR1cmUgb2YgQUkgRW5naW5lZXJpbmciLCJwb3N0X2lkIj=
o0MTkwLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly9ldmVyeS50by92aWJlLWNoZ=
WNrL3ZpYmUtY2hlY2stY2xhdWRlLXNraWxscy1uZWVkLWEtc2hhcmUtYnV0dG9uIiwicG9zaXRp=
b24iOjM1fQ=3D=3D" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">skill</a></=
u> so the rest of the team can adopt the pattern across their projects. The=
n, I can decide that it=E2=80=99s a fundamental piece of how we build and, =
eventually, a best practice I want to enforce for the entire team.</p>
<h2 id=3D"companies-factories">Companies &gt; factories</h2>
<p>While Henry Ford may be famous for the assembly line, he=E2=80=99s argua=
bly more famous for his (<u><a href=3D"https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95=
455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0Ijoi=
VGhlIEN1bHR1cmUgb2YgQUkgRW5naW5lZXJpbmciLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0MTkwLCJwb3N0X3R5cGU=
iOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly9xdW90ZWludmVzdGlnYXRvci5jb20vMjAxMS8wNy8yOC=
9mb3JkLWZhc3Rlci1ob3JzZS8iLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6MzZ9" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer"=
 target=3D"_blank">likely</a></u> apocryphal) quip about how if he asked pe=
ople what they wanted, they=E2=80=99d say faster horses. Assembly lines exi=
st to serve factories, just like factories exist to serve products, and pro=
ducts exist to serve companies. You don=E2=80=99t build a factory without a=
n idea worth building it for.</p>
<p>The factory is one piece in a larger organization, where layers of co-de=
pendent systems interact and move at different speeds. The interesting prob=
lems around alignment occur at the seams, where layers rub against each oth=
er: Is this a problem that should be solved with a meeting, a document, a s=
kill, or a test? When does something graduate from a pattern in a codebase =
to something that should be established in all codebases?</p>
<p>At first glance, AI seems to smooth over these frictions. But that=E2=80=
=99s only true if you don=E2=80=99t scratch below the surface. What you fin=
d there is that the same problems that plague companies plague agents: inco=
mplete information, overeager employees trying to solve the wrong problem, =
not wanting to admit you don=E2=80=99t know. The difference is speed. As <s=
trong><u><a href=3D"https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654=
f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiVGhlIEN1bHR1cmUgb2Y=
gQUkgRW5naW5lZXJpbmciLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0MTkwLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIj=
oiaHR0cHM6Ly9tYXJpb3plY2huZXIuYXQvcG9zdHMvMjAyNi0wMy0yNS10aG91Z2h0cy1vbi1zb=
G93aW5nLXRoZS1mdWNrLWRvd24vIiwicG9zaXRpb24iOjM3fQ=3D=3D" rel=3D"noopener no=
referrer" target=3D"_blank">Mario Zechner</a></u></strong>, who built open-=
source coding agent <u><a href=3D"https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f0=
5e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiVGhlI=
EN1bHR1cmUgb2YgQUkgRW5naW5lZXJpbmciLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0MTkwLCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJw=
b3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly9naXRodWIuY29tL2JhZGxvZ2ljL3BpLW1vbm8iLCJwb3NpdGl=
vbiI6Mzh9" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">Pi</a></u>, recent=
ly observed, the mess that used to take a large organization years to accum=
ulate now arrives in weeks with a two-person team and a fleet of agents. </=
p>
<p>That is not a reason to retreat to being obsessed with defects. It=E2=80=
=99s a reason to take the harder problem seriously: how to keep an entire s=
ystem of humans, agents, and the layers between them aligned. This problem =
has a decidedly human shape. Civilizations have been organizing large group=
s of autonomous agents to do good work for a very long time. The agents wer=
e just carbon instead of silicon.</p>
<p></p>
<hr class=3D"quill-line">
<p></p>
<h2 id=3D"the-man-underneath-the-layers">The man underneath the layers </h2=
>
<p>As part of this thesis, Every chatted to Noah about how he works and wha=
t inspires him. </p>
<p><strong>If there=E2=80=99s a chessboard out:</strong> there=E2=80=99s a =
good chance [my kids and I] will do that instead of reverting to less enric=
hing activities like being on screens. That chess set was designed by some =
friends and inspired by the <u><a href=3D"https://every.to/emails/click/7c3=
f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0I=
joiVGhlIEN1bHR1cmUgb2YgQUkgRW5naW5lZXJpbmciLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0MTkwLCJwb3N0X3R5=
cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly9ueW16by53b3JsZC8iLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6Mzl9" r=
el=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">New York City outdoor chess sc=
