<p><br></p>
<p>Ultimately, the instructions I care about boil down to this: Help me org=
anize the week, keep the quarterly objectives on track, and do the useful w=
ork first instead of requiring so much input from me that I might as well h=
ave gone in and looked at all the inputs myself.  I might as well have </p>
<h2 id=3D"i-cant-automate-the-me-of-it-all">I can=E2=80=99t automate the =
=E2=80=98me=E2=80=99 of it all</h2>
<p>I may be offloading a type of work that I hate and am bad at, but I=E2=
=80=99m also learning new skills=E2=80=94or relearning them for the agentic=
 era. Mostly, these lessons emerge through failure.</p>
<p>Oftentimes, the failure is one of communication. It took time to get in =
the habit of keeping my agent up-to-date on the details it <em>can=E2=80=99=
t </em>see. An article would be published, and I=E2=80=99d forget to tell t=
he agent or move the card in Notion that corresponded to it. Deadlines move=
d while Notion stayed stuck on the old date, and the agent became about as =
useful as my dog when I tell her to go get a toy from upstairs.</p>
