bm9haF8xNzI5IiwicG9zaXRpb24iOjl9" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_bl=
ank">Noah Brier</a></u>, AI entrepreneur and seer</strong></h4>
<p>Brier is a true AI early adopter. The cofounder of the AI consultancy <u=
><a href=3D"https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619=
eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiTWluaW5nIFlvdXIgTGlmZSBmb3I=
gQ29udGV4dCAiLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0MTk0LCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cH=
M6Ly93d3cuYWxlcGhpYy5jb20vIiwicG9zaXRpb24iOjEwfQ=3D=3D" rel=3D"noopener nor=
eferrer" target=3D"_blank">Alephic</a></u>, Brier was all in on using Claud=
e Code as a <u><a href=3D"https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f876=
98e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiTWluaW5nIFlvd=
XIgTGlmZSBmb3IgQ29udGV4dCAiLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0MTk0LCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0Iiwi=
dXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly9ldmVyeS50by9wb2RjYXN0L2hvdy10by11c2UtY2xhdWRlLWNvZGUtYXM=
tYS10aGlua2luZy1wYXJ0bmVyIiwicG9zaXRpb24iOjExfQ=3D=3D" rel=3D"noopener nore=
ferrer" target=3D"_blank">=E2=80=9Csecond brain=E2=80=9D</a></u> for knowle=
dge work back when most people still viewed the tool as a place to write co=
de.</p>
<p>In September, Brier told <strong><u><a href=3D"https://every.to/emails/c=
lick/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzd=
WJqZWN0IjoiTWluaW5nIFlvdXIgTGlmZSBmb3IgQ29udGV4dCAiLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0MTk0LCJw=
b3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly9ldmVyeS50by9AZGFuc2hpcHBlciIsInB=
vc2l0aW9uIjoxMn0=3D" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">Dan Ship=
per</a></u></strong> on our podcast, <em><u><a href=3D"https://every.to/ema=
ils/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/=
eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiTWluaW5nIFlvdXIgTGlmZSBmb3IgQ29udGV4dCAiLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0MTk=
0LCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly9ldmVyeS50by9wb2RjYXN0IiwicG=
9zaXRpb24iOjEzfQ=3D=3D" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">AI &a=
mp; I</a></u></em>, how he turned the coding app into a research, thinking,=
 and writing partner by connecting it to thousands of his personal notes. S=
ince then, he=E2=80=99s started thinking beyond his own productivity=E2=80=
=94how does AI make it easier or harder for an entire organization to stay =
working toward the same goal? For that, he has a new framework, <u><a href=
=3D"https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687=
adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiTWluaW5nIFlvdXIgTGlmZSBmb3IgQ29udGV=
4dCAiLCJwb3N0X2lkIjo0MTk0LCJwb3N0X3R5cGUiOiJwb3N0IiwidXJsIjoiaHR0cHM6Ly9ldm=
VyeS50by90aGVzaXMvdGhlLWN1bHR1cmUtb2YtYWktZW5naW5lZXJpbmciLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6M=
TR9" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">announced in Every last =
week</a></u>, that he calls the =E2=80=9Cpace layers=E2=80=9D of AI enginee=
ring, drawn from <strong>Stewart Brand</strong>=E2=80=99s system for descri=
bing how different parts of society change at different speeds. </p>
<p>Just as hooking up Claude Code to an ocean of personal information requi=
res you to determine what is=E2=80=94and isn=E2=80=99t=E2=80=94worth surfac=
ing, running a successful AI company relies on human judgment. Similarly, A=
I makes code free to produce, but it doesn=E2=80=99t make it easier to iden=
tify a product people actually want or orient an entire system of humans an=
d agents around that vision.</p>
