<p>A cluttered file system can feel like a cluttered brain. When your compu=
ter is a mess, it takes mental energy to find what you need, much less do a=
ctual work. </p>
<p>Clutter is universal=E2=80=94and most of it isn=E2=80=99t worth keeping.=
 Around 80 percent of files on the average Mac are screenshots, installer p=
ackages, duplicates, and digital debris you=E2=80=99ll never open again. So=
 before you can get organized, you need to purge. =E2=80=9COrganized,=E2=80=
=9D then, depends on the person. Maybe you want to arrange files by topic o=
r date, or by a highly-specific system that only makes sense to you. All co=
unt as organized if you can find what you want when you want it. </p>
<p>We=E2=80=99ve rebuilt <strong><u><a href=3D"https://every.to/emails/clic=
k/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJq=
ZWN0IjoiKFJlKFJlKSlJbnRyb2R1Y2luZyBTcGFya2xlOiBNYXJpZSBLb25kbyBZb3VyIE1hYyI=
