<h2>Getting organized</h2>
<p>Once cleanup is done, the next stage of work can begin. Sparkle uses a s=
ample of your most recent files to propose a folder structure. You see exac=
tly what it=E2=80=99s suggesting=E2=80=94top-level folders, subfolder label=
s, and what goes where.</p>
<p>From there, you can rename, merge, delete, reorganize, and add folders, =
all through chat. If Sparkle creates a =E2=80=9CProjects=E2=80=9D folder bu=
t you=E2=80=99d prefer a =E2=80=9CWork=E2=80=9D folder=E2=80=94with =E2=80=
=9CClient Projects=E2=80=9D and =E2=80=9CInternal Projects=E2=80=9D nested =
inside=E2=80=94you can tell the agent and it will make the update.</p>
