al manager <strong><u><a href=3D"https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05=
e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiWW914o=
CZcmUgdGhlIE1hbmFnZXIgTm93IiwicG9zdF9pZCI6NDExMywicG9zdF90eXBlIjoicG9zdCIsI=
nVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vZXZlcnkudG8vQG5hdmVlbl82ODA0IiwicG9zaXRpb24iOjExfQ=3D=3D=
" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">Naveen Naidu</a></u></stron=
g>. Cursor offers a similar experience, and both companies =E2=80=9Cjust co=
pied Codex=E2=80=99s design,=E2=80=9D he says.</p>
<p>But it confirms where dev work is headed: <u><a href=3D"https://every.to=
/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e=
242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiWW914oCZcmUgdGhlIE1hbmFnZXIgTm93IiwicG9zdF9pZCI6NDExMyw=
icG9zdF90eXBlIjoicG9zdCIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vZXZlcnkudG8vc291cmNlLWNvZGUvdG=
hlLWZvbGRlci1pcy10aGUtYWdlbnQiLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6MTJ9" rel=3D"noopener norefer=
rer" target=3D"_blank">overseeing agents</a></u>, not writing code.</p>
<p><strong>Nixed:</strong> The idea that command-line interface (CLI) will =
eat user interface (UI). With a CLI-first workflow, you mostly supervise th=
rough text: commands, logs, git state, diffs, and terminal output. Now that=
 agents are doing the coding, that=E2=80=99s not a good primary interface.<=
/p>
<p>Instead, the future coding UI is centered on managing parallel work, sta=
ying aware of git/task context, and=E2=80=94most importantly, Kieran says=
=E2=80=94having access to a preview of what you=E2=80=99re building.</p>
<p></p>
<hr class=3D"quill-line">
<p></p>
<h2>Permission to skip</h2>
<h4>Smaller models can=E2=80=99t do what Claude Mythos does</h4>
<p>A researcher at a cybersecurity company made waves online when he report=
ed smaller models could find the <u><a href=3D"https://every.to/emails/clic=
k/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJq=
ZWN0IjoiWW914oCZcmUgdGhlIE1hbmFnZXIgTm93IiwicG9zdF9pZCI6NDExMywicG9zdF90eXB=
lIjoicG9zdCIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vYWlzbGUuY29tL2Jsb2cvYWktY3liZXJzZWN1cml0eS=
1hZnRlci1teXRob3MtdGhlLWphZ2dlZC1mcm9udGllciIsInBvc2l0aW9uIjoxM30=3D" rel=
=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">same security vulnerabilities</a=
></u> as Mythos, Anthropic=E2=80=99s new model so powerful it <u><a href=3D=
"https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adc=
e5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiWW914oCZcmUgdGhlIE1hbmFnZXIgTm93IiwicG=
9zdF9pZCI6NDExMywicG9zdF90eXBlIjoicG9zdCIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vZXZlcnkudG8vY=
29udGV4dC13aW5kb3cvZXZlcnktaXMtaGFsZi1hZ2VudC1ub3ciLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6MTR9" re=
l=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">isn=E2=80=99t being made public=
</a></u>, when pointed to the relevant code.</p>
<p>You have permission to skip this discourse=E2=80=94or better yet, refram=
e it.</p>
<p>Because this is a framing issue, says <strong><u><a href=3D"https://ever=
y.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18=
966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiWW914oCZcmUgdGhlIE1hbmFnZXIgTm93IiwicG9zdF9pZCI6NDE=
xMywicG9zdF90eXBlIjoicG9zdCIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vZXZlcnkudG8vQGRhbnNoaXBwZX=
IiLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6MTV9" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">Dan S=
hipper</a></u></strong>, Every=E2=80=99s CEO. Mythos and smaller models are=
 operating within completely different ones. Yes, you can point a smaller m=
odel to a codebase and tell it to find a bug when you already know that cap=
ability is possible, but you cannot ask it to find serious vulnerabilities =
in critical software across every major operating system and browser, auton=
omously, the way Mythos did.</p>
