<h5><strong>The workflow:</strong></h5>
<ol>
<li>
<strong>Finish the task, then ask for a confidence score.</strong> Once Cla=
ude Code has a working solution, type: =E2=80=9CHow confident are you in th=
is, 1=E2=80=93100?=E2=80=9D If it comes back above 90, move on. If not, go =
to step 2.</li>
<li>
<strong>Send it back.</strong> Tell it: =E2=80=9CFind improvements and get =
to 90+.=E2=80=9D Claude will catch edge cases, tighten logic, or flag assum=
ptions it glossed over the first time. Repeat until it crosses the threshol=
d.</li>
<li>
<strong>Ship at 90.</strong> Don=E2=80=99t chase 100=E2=80=94that=E2=80=99s=
 where you burn tokens on diminishing returns. At 90, it=E2=80=99s checked =
its own work and flagged what it wasn=E2=80=99t sure about.=E2=80=94<em><u>=
