2YtZml2ZSIsInBvc2l0aW9uIjoxNn0=3D" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_b=
lank">run parallel Claude Code sessions</a></u> for months, which works whe=
n each agent has a clear task, and I=E2=80=99m directing the work. The swar=
m experiment was different: agents coordinating with each other, deciding w=
hat to work on, producing output I hadn=E2=80=99t shaped. When 10 of them f=
inished simultaneously, I had 10 <u><a href=3D"https://every.to/emails/clic=
k/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJq=
