<h2><strong>The agents hiding on your hard drive</strong></h2>
<p>People hear =E2=80=9Cagent=E2=80=9D and picture a <u><a href=3D"https://=
every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc0=
2e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiVGhlIEZvbGRlciBJcyB0aGUgQWdlbnQgIiwicG9zdF9pZCI=
6NDEwOCwicG9zdF90eXBlIjoicG9zdCIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vZW4ud2lraXBlZGlhLm9yZy=
93aWtpL1J1YmVfR29sZGJlcmdfbWFjaGluZSIsInBvc2l0aW9uIjoyM30=3D" rel=3D"noopen=
er noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">Rube Goldberg machine</a></u>=E2=80=94doze=
ns of comically complex moving parts, each one triggering the next. But an =
agent is much simpler: a model with enough context so you don=E2=80=99t hav=
e to re-explain everything each time you open the chat. </p>
<p>Here=E2=80=99s an example: All of Cora=E2=80=99s code lives in a project=
 folder in the Every organization on GitHub. When I open that folder with C=
laude, Claude can see the code and the structure. But it doesn=E2=80=99t kn=
ow my way of working or what I care about, which is why the folder also inc=
ludes a <u><a href=3D"https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e6=
54f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiVGhlIEZvbGRlciBJc=
yB0aGUgQWdlbnQgIiwicG9zdF9pZCI6NDEwOCwicG9zdF90eXBlIjoicG9zdCIsInVybCI6Imh0=
dHA6Ly9jbGF1ZGUubWQiLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6MjR9" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" targe=
t=3D"_blank">CLAUDE.md</a></u> file. The file tells Claude how I name thing=
s and how I structure tests. That=E2=80=99s an agent=E2=80=94not a fancy on=
e, but an agent nonetheless. Just by pointing the model at this folder, whi=
ch contains some of my personality, knowledge, and <u><a href=3D"https://ev=
ery.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e=
18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiVGhlIEZvbGRlciBJcyB0aGUgQWdlbnQgIiwicG9zdF9pZCI6N=
DEwOCwicG9zdF90eXBlIjoicG9zdCIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vZXZlcnkudG8vcC93aGF0LWlz=
LXRhc3RlLXJlYWxseSIsInBvc2l0aW9uIjoyNX0=3D" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" tar=
get=3D"_blank">taste</a></u>, the model can be a specialist in my codebase.=
