pener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">Austin Tedesco</a></u></strong> wants t=
o ship a careers page or a YouTube thumbnail in Every=E2=80=99s style witho=
ut bothering the design team, Claude Design is the tool for the job.</p>
<p>Claude Design=E2=80=99s live, generative interface is also a nice touch,=
 Lucas says. The tool starts by asking you questions=E2=80=94layout density=
, accent color, whether to animate emojis=E2=80=94and you can draw or leave=
 comments on top of the output, or click a specific element and edit it in =
place. The sketch-on-top feature is the closest Claude Design gets to feeli=
ng like Figma.</p>
<p><strong>What could be better:</strong><em> The menu-driven interaction.<=
/em> Creating in Claude Design means answering a series of text prompts abo=
ut layout, tone, and color, and reacting to what the tool produces. =E2=80=
=9CIt feels like we=E2=80=99re filling a bunch of forms=E2=80=94design is s=
upposed to be fun,=E2=80=9D Lucas says.</p>
<p>This prompt-and-react loop works for extending or revising an existing d=
esign system. But it isn=E2=80=99t well-suited for starting something from =
