<h2>Signal</h2>
<h5>Two new ways AI tools can leak your data</h5>
<p>Two AI-tool security stories broke inside 24 hours over the weekend. The=
y reveal two different points of failure in AI security: one where the atta=
ck surface was the vendor, and one where it was the AI=E2=80=99s <em>output=
</em>. </p>
<p><strong>What happened: </strong>On Sunday, Vercel, an infrastructure com=
pany behind a big chunk of the web, <u><a href=3D"https://every.to/emails/c=
lick/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzd=
WJqZWN0IjoiTWluaS1WaWJlIENoZWNrOiBDbGF1ZGUgRGVzaWduIElzbuKAmXQgZm9yIERlc2ln=
bmVyc-KAlFlldCIsInBvc3RfaWQiOjQxMTgsInBvc3RfdHlwZSI6InBvc3QiLCJ1cmwiOiJodHR=
wczovL3ZlcmNlbC5jb20va2IvYnVsbGV0aW4vdmVyY2VsLWFwcmlsLTIwMjYtc2VjdXJpdHktaW=
5jaWRlbnQiLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6MTl9" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blan=
k">confirmed a breach</a></u>. Except the break-in didn=E2=80=99t start at =
Vercel but at a third-party tool called Context AI. The attackers used the =
hacked connection to climb into a Vercel employee=E2=80=99s Google workspac=
e account, then their Vercel account, and finally into customer data=E2=80=
=94including the private passwords and credentials that customers=E2=80=99 =
apps use to connect to their payment systems, databases, and other services=
=2E</p>
<p>Then on Monday, vibe coding platform Lovable did damage control after us=
ers <u><a href=3D"https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f4=
54c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiTWluaS1WaWJlIENoZWNrO=
iBDbGF1ZGUgRGVzaWduIElzbuKAmXQgZm9yIERlc2lnbmVyc-KAlFlldCIsInBvc3RfaWQiOjQx=
MTgsInBvc3RfdHlwZSI6InBvc3QiLCJ1cmwiOiJodHRwczovL3guY29tL21vcmdhbmxpbnRvbi9=
zdGF0dXMvMjA0NjIwNjczNzY3NDY1MzczNCIsInBvc2l0aW9uIjoyMH0=3D" rel=3D"noopene=
r noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">started warning each other</a></u> that app=
s built on the platform were leaking their users=E2=80=99 data to the publi=
c internet. The issue turned out to be in the permissions: A basic database=
 rule, =E2=80=9Ca customer can only see their own records,=E2=80=9D was tur=
ned off by default in the apps Lovable generated.</p>
<p><strong>Why it matters:</strong> Every AI app your team signs up for is =
a new door into your company. If the vendor gets hacked, the keys they were=
 holding=E2=80=94to your email, your calendar, your codebase=E2=80=94walk o=
ut with the attackers. You inherit that vendor=E2=80=99s security posture e=
ven if your IT team didn=E2=80=99t pick the tool.</p>
<p>And when an AI writes your app for you, your app inherits the AI=E2=80=
=99s defaults. There isn=E2=80=99t always someone looking over the generato=
r=E2=80=99s shoulder to check whether those defaults are safe. =E2=80=9CI v=
ibe-coded a prototype=E2=80=9D now means =E2=80=9CI shipped something prote=
cted by whatever rules the generator thought were fine.=E2=80=9D</p>
<h5><strong>What to do this week: </strong></h5>
<ul>
<li>Take stock of every AI app your employees have connected to a work acco=
unt. Then turn on two-factor authentication everywhere it isn=E2=80=99t alr=
eady on.</li>
<li>Before you ship anything an AI built=E2=80=94even a weekend prototype=
=E2=80=94ask the generator one question: <em>=E2=80=9CWhat is this app expo=
sing to the public internet, and should it be?=E2=80=9D</em> If you can=E2=
=80=99t get a clear answer, don=E2=80=99t ship.</li>
<li>For anything touching customer data, like a CRM or billing system, pair=
 the AI with a tool designed for a safer-by-default posture. Anthropic=E2=
=80=99s recently launched <u><a href=3D"https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f9=
5455f05e60f87698e654f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0Ijo=
iTWluaS1WaWJlIENoZWNrOiBDbGF1ZGUgRGVzaWduIElzbuKAmXQgZm9yIERlc2lnbmVyc-KAlF=
lldCIsInBvc3RfaWQiOjQxMTgsInBvc3RfdHlwZSI6InBvc3QiLCJ1cmwiOiJodHRwczovL3d3d=
y5hbnRocm9waWMuY29tL25ld3MvbWFuYWdlZC1hZ2VudHMiLCJwb3NpdGlvbiI6MjF9" rel=3D=
"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">Managed Agents</a></u>, for example=
, runs each session in a sealed-off computing environment with credentials =
held outside the sandbox.</li>
</ul>
<h2><hr class=3D"quill-line"></h2>
<h2>Steal this workflow</h2>
<h5>Give your agent its own X feed to watch for vulnerabilities</h5>
<p>You can=E2=80=99t personally stay on top of every vulnerability that mig=
ht hit the AI stack you=E2=80=99re building on. Every AI engineer <strong><=
u><a href=3D"https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e654f454c61=
9eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiTWluaS1WaWJlIENoZWNrOiBDbG=
F1ZGUgRGVzaWduIElzbuKAmXQgZm9yIERlc2lnbmVyc-KAlFlldCIsInBvc3RfaWQiOjQxMTgsI=
nBvc3RfdHlwZSI6InBvc3QiLCJ1cmwiOiJodHRwczovL2V2ZXJ5LnRvL0BuaXR5ZXNoIiwicG9z=
aXRpb24iOjIyfQ=3D=3D" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">Nityesh=
 Agarwal</a></u></strong> decided to stop trying, and assign situation moni=
toring to an agent that doesn=E2=80=99t sleep.</p>
<h5><strong>The workflow:</strong></h5>
<ol>
<li>
<strong>Create a dedicated X account for your agent.</strong> Nityesh made =
one for <u><a href=3D"https://every.to/emails/click/7c3f95455f05e60f87698e6=
54f454c619eafce687adce5ebefcc02e18966e242/eyJzdWJqZWN0IjoiTWluaS1WaWJlIENoZ=
WNrOiBDbGF1ZGUgRGVzaWduIElzbuKAmXQgZm9yIERlc2lnbmVyc-KAlFlldCIsInBvc3RfaWQi=
OjQxMTgsInBvc3RfdHlwZSI6InBvc3QiLCJ1cmwiOiJodHRwczovL2V2ZXJ5LnRvL3Avd2hhdC1=
pLWxlYXJuZWQtb25ib2FyZGluZy1vdXItYWktcHJvamVjdC1tYW5hZ2VyIiwicG9zaXRpb24iOj=
IzfQ=3D=3D" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank">Claudie, Every=E2=
=80=99s consulting project manager agent</a></u>, and had her follow the AI=
 security people he=E2=80=99d otherwise be glued to=E2=80=94Anthropic resea=
